Object.assign(window.TEM8_DICTIONARY, {"forbidding":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forbidding__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forbidding__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈbɪdɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"seeming unfriendly and frightening","cn":"冷峻的；令人生畏的","ex":{"en":"a forbidding appearance/look/manner","cn":"冷峻的样子／面孔／态度"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"可怕的;令人生畏的","en":"If you describe a person, place, or thing as forbidding, you mean they have a severe, unfriendly, or threatening appearance.","ex":{"en":"There was something a little severe and forbidding about her face.","cn":"她脸上有种严肃、冷峻的表情。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The house looked dark and forbidding.","cn":"房子黑森森的，令人望而生畏。"},{"en":"a forbidding appearance/look/manner","cn":"冷峻的样子/面孔/态度"}]},"focus":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/focus__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/focus__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊkəs","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give attention, effort, etc. to one particular subject, situation or person rather than another","cn":"集中（注意力、精力等于）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"She was distracted and finding it hard to focus.","cn":"她心烦意乱，很难集中注意力。"}},{"en":"to adapt or be changed so that things can be seen clearly; to change something so that you can see things clearly","cn":"（使）调节焦距","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","ex":{"en":"It took a few moments for her eyes to focus in the dark.","cn":"过了一会儿她的眼睛才适应了黑暗。"}},{"en":"to aim light onto a particular point using a lens","cn":"集中（光束于）；聚焦（于）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"A laser focuses a beam of light.","cn":"激光聚焦光束。"}},{"en":"to shine on somebody/something","cn":"照射","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Suddenly a spotlight focused on us.","cn":"突然聚光灯聚焦在我们身上。"}},{"en":"the thing or person that people are most interested in; the act of paying special attention to something and making people interested in it","cn":"中心点（指人或事物）；关注；引起关注","g":"[uncountable, countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"It was the main focus of attention at the meeting.","cn":"这是会议上关注的主要焦点。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a point or distance at which the outline of an object is clearly seen by the eye or through a lens","cn":"（眼睛或镜头的）焦点，焦距","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Some parts of the photograph are out of focus (= blurred rather than clearly seen).","cn":"照片上有几处因失焦而模糊了。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a point at which waves of light, sound, etc. meet after reflection or refraction; the point from which waves of light, sound, etc. seem to come","cn":"（光、声等的）焦点，中心点，源","g":"[countable]","lab":"physics","pos":"noun"},{"en":"the point at which an earthquake starts to happen","cn":"（地震的）震源","g":"[countable]","lab":"geology","pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"集中(注意力);关注","en":"If you focus on a particular topic or if your attention is focused on it, you concentrate on it and think about it, discuss it, or deal with it, rather than dealing with other topics.","ex":{"en":"The research effort has focused on tracing the effects of growing levels of five compounds","cn":"研究重点追踪了5种化合物含量上升的影响。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"主题;重点;焦点","en":"The focus of something is the main topic or main thing that it is concerned with.","ex":{"en":"The UN's role in promoting peace is increasingly the focus of international attention","cn":"联合国在促进和平方面的作用越来越受到国际社会的关注。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"关注;注意","en":"Your focus on something is the special attention that you pay it.","ex":{"en":"He said his sudden focus on foreign policy was not motivated by presidential politics","cn":"他说他突然关注外交政策并非受总统政治的驱使。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"目的;意图;含义","en":"If you say that something has a focus, you mean that you can see a purpose in it.","ex":{"en":"Somehow, though, their latest album has a focus that the others have lacked","cn":"但是，他们的最新专辑设法找到了其他专辑所欠缺的一种目的性。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"注视;使(相机、望远镜等)聚焦;给…调焦","en":"If you focus your eyes or if your eyes focus, your eyes adjust so that you can clearly see the thing that you want to look at. If you focus a camera, telescope, or other instrument, you adjust it so that you can see clearly through it.","ex":{"en":"Kelly couldn't focus his eyes well enough to tell if the figure was male or female","cn":"凯利没有看清楚那个人影到底是男的还是女的。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"注视;调焦;对焦","en":"You use focus to refer to the fact of adjusting your eyes or a camera, telescope, or other instrument, and to the degree to which you can see clearly.","ex":{"en":"His focus switched to the little white ball","cn":"他把关注点转移到那个小白球上。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"集中(光束);聚焦","en":"If you focus rays of light on a particular point, you pass them through a lens or reflect them from a mirror so that they meet at that point.","ex":{"en":"Magnetic coils focus the electron beams into fine spots.","cn":"磁线圈把电子束聚焦成微小的点。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"聚焦点","en":"The focus of a number of rays or lines is the point at which they meet."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(图像)清晰;(照相机、望远镜等)对准焦点","en":"If an image or a camera, telescope, or other instrument is in focus, the edges of what you see are clear and sharp.","ex":{"en":"Pictures should be in focus, with realistic colours and well composed groups.","cn":"照片应该图像清晰，颜色逼真，构图合理。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"受关注;在讨论;(目的和性质)清楚的，明白的","en":"If something is in focus, it is being discussed or its purpose and nature are clear.","ex":{"en":"This aggression is the real issue the world should be concerned about. We want to keep that in focus","cn":"这次侵略才是世界应该关注的真正问题。我们想继续保持关注。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"焦点没对准;脱焦;失焦","en":"If an image or a camera, telescope, or other instrument is out of focus, the edges of what you see are unclear.","ex":{"en":"In some of the pictures the subjects are out of focus while the background is sharp.","cn":"一些照片背景很清晰，被摄主体却因失焦而显得模糊。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"不受关注;(目的和性质)不清晰的","en":"If something is out of focus, it is not being discussed or its purpose or nature is not clear.","ex":{"en":"The deficit in the US balance of payments put these considerations out of focus","cn":"美国的国际收支逆差使这些因素没有得到关注。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"In today's lecture the focus will be on tax structures within the European Union.","cn":"今天讲课的重点是欧洲联盟内部的税制结构。"},{"en":"In this scene, the camera focuses on the actor's face.","cn":"在这个镜头中，摄影机对准演员的脸部。"}]},"forty":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forty__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forty__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːti","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"40","cn":"四十"},{"en":"numbers, years or temperatures from 40 to 49","cn":"四十几；四十年代","g":"[plural]"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"NUM 数词","cn":"(数字)40","en":"Forty is the number 40."},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"四十多，四十几(指从40至49的数字)","en":"When you talk about the forties, you are referring to numbers between 40 and 49. For example, if you are in your forties, you are aged between 40 and 49. If the temperature is in the forties, the temperature is between 40 and 49 degrees.","ex":{"en":"He was a big man in his forties, smartly dressed in a suit and tie.","cn":"他是一个四十多岁的高大男子，穿西装打领带，看上去很精神。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"二十世纪四十年代(指从 1940 年至 1949 年)","en":"The forties is the decade between 1940 and 1949.","ex":{"en":"Steel cans were introduced sometime during the forties.","cn":"钢罐是 20 世纪 40 年代时开始使用的。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The place was built as a casino in the forties.","cn":"这个地方建于20世纪40年代﹐起初是一座赌场。"},{"en":"He spent several years in Paris in the late forties. 20","cn":"世纪40年代末﹐他在巴黎待了几年。"}]},"forgive":{"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈɡɪv","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to stop feeling angry with somebody who has done something to harm, annoy or upset you; to stop feeling angry with yourself","cn":"原谅；宽恕","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Can you ever forgive me?","cn":"你能原谅我吗？"}},{"en":"used to say in a polite way that you are sorry if what you are doing or saying seems rude or silly","cn":"对不起；请原谅","g":"[transitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Forgive me, but I don't see that any of this concerns me.","cn":"对不起，我看不出这与我有什么关系。"}},{"en":"to say that somebody does not need to pay back money that they have borrowed","cn":"免除（债务）","g":"[transitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"The government has agreed to forgive a large part of the debt.","cn":"政府同意免除一大部分债务。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"原谅;饶恕;宽恕","en":"If you forgive someone who has done something bad or wrong, you stop being angry with them and no longer want to punish them.","ex":{"en":"Hopefully she'll understand and forgive you, if she really loves you","cn":"如果她真的爱你的话，希望她会理解并原谅你。"}},{"pos":"V-PASSIVE 被动动词","cn":"情有可原","en":"If you say that someone could be forgiven for doing something, you mean that they were wrong or mistaken, but not seriously, because many people would have done the same thing in those circumstances.","ex":{"en":"Looking at the figures, you could be forgiven for thinking the recession is already over","cn":"看看这些数字，难怪你会觉得经济衰退已经结束了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(用于礼貌用语或道歉语中)请原谅/恕我无知","en":"Forgive is used in polite expressions and apologies like 'forgive me' and 'forgive my ignorance' when you are saying or doing something that might seem rude, silly, or complicated.","ex":{"en":"Forgive me, I don't mean to insult you","cn":"请原谅，我并非有意侮辱你。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"免除(债务)","en":"If an organization such as a bank forgives someone's debt, they agree not to ask for that money to be repaid.","ex":{"en":"The American Congress has agreed to forgive Egypt's military debt.","cn":"美国国会同意免除埃及的军事债务。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgive__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgive__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Looking at the crowds out shopping, you could be forgiven for thinking that everyone has plenty of money.","cn":"见到人们成群结队地外出购物，难怪你会以为人人都很富有。"},{"en":"I'd never forgive myself if she heard the truth from someone else.","cn":"如果她从别人那里听到了真相，我永远不会原谅自己。"}]},"forest":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forest__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forest__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrɪst","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large area of land that is thickly covered with trees","cn":"森林；林区","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a tropical/pine forest","cn":"热带森林；松树林"}},{"en":"a mass of tall narrow objects that are close together","cn":"（森林似的）一丛，一片","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"a forest of cranes on the skyline","cn":"天空映衬下的鹤群"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"森林;树林","en":"A forest is a large area where trees grow close together.","ex":{"en":"Parts of the forest are still dense and inaccessible.","cn":"森林的一些部分仍然很茂密，人迹罕至。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"林立;大量耸立","en":"A forest of tall or narrow objects is a group of them standing or sticking upright.","ex":{"en":"They descended from the plane into a forest of microphones and cameras.","cn":"他们从飞机上走下来，迎接他们的是数不清的麦克风和照相机。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Thousands of hectares of forest are destroyed each year.","cn":"每年都有几千公顷的森林遭到破坏。"},{"en":"a forest of television aerials","cn":"林立的电视天线"}]},"forgiving":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgiving__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgiving__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈɡɪvɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"willing to forgive","cn":"宽宏大量的；宽容的","ex":{"en":"She had not inherited her mother's forgiving nature.","cn":"她没有承袭她母亲的宽厚天性。"}},{"en":"easy or safe to deal with","cn":"可轻松应对的；安全的","ex":{"en":"Snow is a forgiving surface on which to fall.","cn":"在雪地即使摔倒也很安全。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"宽大的;仁慈的","en":"Someone who is forgiving is willing to forgive.","ex":{"en":"Voters can be remarkably forgiving of presidents who fail to keep their campaign promises","cn":"选民对总统未履行竞选承诺往往表现出惊人的宽容。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The public was more forgiving of the president's difficulties than the press and fellow politicians.","cn":"公众比报界和总统的政界同事更能体谅他的难处。"},{"en":"She had not inherited her mother's forgiving nature.","cn":"她没有承袭她母亲的宽厚天性。"}]},"forth":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forth__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forth__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːθ","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"away from a place; out","cn":"离去；外出","ex":{"en":"They set forth at dawn.","cn":"他们在黎明时出发。"}},{"en":"towards a place; forwards","cn":"向某处；向前","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"Water gushed forth from a hole in the rock.","cn":"水从岩洞里涌出。"}},{"en":"a river that flows through central Scotland into the North Sea. The long wide area of water where the Forth flows into the sea is called the firth of Forth, and is well known for the Forth Bridges.","cn":"第四条：一条河流，流经苏格兰中部，流入北海。福斯（Forth）流入大海的水域很长，被称为福斯峡湾（Forth），以福斯桥（Forth Bridges）而闻名。","pos":""}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"向外，往外(走)","en":"When someone goes forth from a place, they leave it.","ex":{"en":"Go forth into the desert","cn":"向前走进沙漠。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"产生;得出","en":"If one thing brings forth another, the first thing produces the second.","ex":{"en":"Nature herself brings forth new forms of life","cn":"自然本身会创造出新的生命形态。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(带)来;(拿)出;(现)出","en":"When someone or something is brought forth, they are brought to a place or moved into a position where people can see them.","ex":{"en":"Pilate ordered Jesus to be brought forth","cn":"彼拉多命令把耶稣带上来。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"back and forth→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":". to hold forth→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Huge chimneys belched forth smoke and grime.","cn":"巨大的烟囱冒出烟和灰尘。"},{"en":"They set forth at dawn.","cn":"他们在黎明时出发。"}]},"foul":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foul__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foul__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"faʊl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"dirty and smelling bad","cn":"肮脏恶臭的；难闻的","ex":{"en":"foul air/breath","cn":"污浊难闻的空气／气息"}},{"en":"very unpleasant; very bad","cn":"很令人不快的；很坏的","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"She's in a foul mood.","cn":"她的情绪很糟。"}},{"en":"including rude words and swearing","cn":"充满脏话的；辱骂性的；下流的","ex":{"en":"She exploded in a torrent of foul language.","cn":"她爆发出滔滔不绝的脏话。"}},{"en":"very bad, with strong winds and rain","cn":"恶劣的；风雨交加的","ex":{"en":"a foul night","cn":"风雨交加的夜晚"}},{"en":"very evil or cruel","cn":"邪恶的；残忍的","lab":"literary","ex":{"en":"a foul crime/murder","cn":"邪恶的罪行；恶毒的谋杀"}},{"en":"done against the rules of a sport","cn":"犯规","g":"[only before noun]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"Harper was penalized for a foul tackle.","cn":"哈珀因铲球犯规而受到处罚。"}},{"en":"to do something to another player that is against the rules of the game","cn":"对（对手）犯规","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"He was fouled inside the penalty area.","cn":"在禁区内对方队员对他犯规。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to hit the ball outside the playing area","cn":"击（球）出界","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make something dirty, especially with waste matter from the body","cn":"（尤指用粪便）弄脏，污染","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Do not permit your dog to foul the grass.","cn":"禁止狗在草地便溺。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to become caught or twisted in something and stop it working or moving","cn":"（被）缠住","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The rope fouled the propeller.","cn":"绳索缠住了螺旋桨。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"an action that is against the rules of the game","cn":"犯规","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"It was a clear foul by Ford on the goalkeeper.","cn":"这明显是福特对守门员犯规。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"难吃的;肮脏的;恶臭的","en":"If you describe something as foul, you mean it is dirty and smells or tastes unpleasant.","ex":{"en":"...foul polluted water","cn":"恶臭的脏水"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(言语)粗俗的，冒犯的","en":"Foul language is offensive and contains swear words or rude words.","ex":{"en":"He was sent off for using foul language in a match last Sunday","cn":"他在上周日的一场比赛中因为骂人而被罚下场。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"易怒的;暴躁的","en":"If someone has a foul temper or is in a foul mood, they become angry or violent very suddenly and easily.","ex":{"en":"Collins was in a foul mood even before the interviews began.","cn":"柯林斯在采访还没开始时就暴躁不安起来。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(天气)恶劣的，多风的，有暴风雨的","en":"Foul weather is unpleasant, windy, and stormy."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"弄脏;弄污;污染","en":"If a place is fouled by someone or something, they make it dirty.","ex":{"en":"A village's entire beach and harbor can be fouled by a single rotting whale","cn":"一只腐烂的死鲸就足以弄脏一个村子的整片海滩和港口。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(动物拉屎)弄脏","en":"If an animal fouls a place, it drops faeces onto the ground.","ex":{"en":"It is an offence to let your dog foul a footpath.","cn":"让狗在人行道上拉屎是违法行为。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(使)绞住;(使)缠住","en":"If a machine or vehicle fouls part of its mechanism or if something such as a rope fouls the mechanism, the mechanism can no longer work properly because something has become twisted or knotted around it.","ex":{"en":"The freighter fouled its propeller in fishing nets.","cn":"货船的螺旋桨被渔网缠住了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"对…犯规","en":"In a game or sport, if a player fouls another player, they touch them or block them in a way which is not allowed according to the rules.","ex":{"en":"Middlesbrough's Jimmy Phillips was sent off for fouling Steve Tilson.","cn":"米德尔斯堡队的吉米·菲利普斯因为对史蒂夫·蒂尔森犯规而被罚下场。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"犯规","en":"A foul is an act in a game or sport that is not allowed according to the rules.","ex":{"en":"He picked up his first booking for a 45th-minute foul on Bull.","cn":"他因为在比赛进行到第 45 分钟时对公牛队犯规而被第一次记名警告。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"声明对手犯规;声称对手违法","en":"If you cry foul, you claim that someone, especially an opponent or rival, has acted illegally or unfairly.","ex":{"en":"Deprived of the crushing victory it was confidently expecting, the party cried foul.","cn":"失去了自以为十拿九稳的压倒性胜利，该政党声称对手违规。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"不择手段地;采取一切手段地","en":"If someone tries to achieve something by fair means or foul, they use every means possible in order to achieve it, and they do not care if their behaviour is dishonest or unfair.","ex":{"en":"They will only be satisfied if they regain control —by fair means or foul.","cn":"只有重新掌权他们才会满意——为此他们将不择手段。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"惹恼;触怒","en":"If you fall foul of someone or run foul of them, you do something which gets you into trouble with them.","ex":{"en":"He had fallen foul of the FBI.","cn":"他已经惹恼了联邦调查局。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"搞砸;弄糟","en":"If you foul up something such as a plan, you spoil it by doing something wrong or stupid.","ex":{"en":"There are serious risks that laboratories may foul up these tests.","cn":"实验室很有可能搞砸这些试验。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：foul up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"I'm sick of her foul mouth (= habit of swearing).","cn":"我讨厌她一开口就骂人的那张臭嘴。"},{"en":"He was fouled inside the penalty area.","cn":"在罚球区内对方队员对他犯规。"}]},"forgiveness":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgiveness__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgiveness__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈɡɪvnəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the act of forgiving somebody; the quality of being willing to forgive somebody","cn":"原谅；宽恕；宽宏大量","ex":{"en":"to pray for God’s forgiveness","cn":"祈求上帝宽恕"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"原谅;宽恕","en":"If you ask for forgiveness, you ask to be forgiven for something wrong that you have done.","ex":{"en":"I offered up a short prayer for forgiveness.","cn":"我做了个简短的祷告，祈求宽恕。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He begged forgiveness for what he had done.","cn":"他乞求饶恕他的所作所为。"},{"en":"to pray for God's forgiveness","cn":"祈求上帝宽恕"}]},"football":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtbɔːl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a game played by two teams of 11 players, using a round ball that players kick up and down the playing field. Teams try to kick the ball into the other team’s goal.","cn":"足球运动","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"The kids were outside playing football.","cn":"孩子们在外面踢足球。"}},{"en":"a game played by two teams of 11 players, using an oval ball which players kick, throw, or carry. Teams try to put the ball over the other team’s line.","cn":"美式足球，美式橄榄球（双方队员各 11 人，球呈椭圆形，球员可足踢、手传或持球奔跑，球越过对方得分线得分）","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"He played football for Iowa State University.","cn":"他是爱荷华州立大学美式足球队队员。"}},{"en":"a form of football played in Canada, similar to American football, but with twelve players on each team","cn":"加拿大式橄榄球（源自英式橄榄球，但现在与美式橄榄球相似，每队有12名队员）","g":"[uncountable]"},{"en":"a large round or oval ball made of leather or plastic and filled with air","cn":"足球；橄榄球","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"As a child he was always kicking a football.","cn":"他小时候总是踢足球。"}},{"en":"an issue or a problem that frequently causes people to disagree or argue","cn":"屡起争议的事情；被踢来踢去的难题","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Healthcare should not become a political football.","cn":"保健问题不应该成为被踢来踢去的政治皮球。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"足球运动","en":"Football is a game played by two teams of eleven players using a round ball. Players kick the ball to each other and try to score goals by kicking the ball into a large net.","ex":{"en":"Several boys were still playing football on the waste ground.","cn":"几个男孩还在那片废弃的空地上踢足球。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"橄榄球运动","en":"Football is a game played by two teams of eleven players using an oval ball. Players carry the ball in their hands or throw it to each other as they try to score goals that are called touchdowns.","ex":{"en":"Two blocks beyond our school was a field where boys played football","cn":"离我们学校两个街区远的地方有个男孩们玩橄榄球的球场。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"足球;橄榄球","en":"A football is a ball that is used for playing football."}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/americanfootball_comp.jpg","media/thumb/soccer.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/football__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/football__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Health care should not become a political football.","cn":"保健问题不应该成为被踢来踢去的政治皮球。"},{"en":"a football match/team/stadium","cn":"足球比赛/队；足球比赛专用体育场"}]},"fourfold":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"four times as much or as many","cn":"四倍的[地]"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Profits rose fourfold.","cn":"利润上升到原来的四倍。","src":"ld"},{"en":"a fourfold increase in price","cn":"价格的四倍上涨","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fourfold__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fourfold__us_1.mp3"}},"forums":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːrəm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a place where people can exchange opinions and ideas on a particular issue; a meeting organized for this purpose","cn":"公共讨论场所；论坛；讨论会"},{"en":"(in ancient Rome) a public place where meetings were held （","cn":"古罗马）公共集会场所"}]}},"fortunately":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fortunately__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fortunately__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtʃənətli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"by good luck","cn":"幸运地；交好运地；吉利地","ex":{"en":"I was late, but fortunately the meeting hadn't started.","cn":"我迟到了，不过幸好会议还没有开始。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"幸好;幸运的是","en":"Fortunately is used to introduce or indicate a statement about an event or situation that is good.","ex":{"en":"Fortunately, the weather that winter was reasonably mild","cn":"幸好那个冬天还算暖和。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Fortunately for him, he was very soon offered another job.","cn":"他运气好，很快就有人聘请他做另一个工作。"},{"en":"I was late, but fortunately the meeting hadn't started.","cn":"我迟到了，不过幸好会议还没有开始。"}]},"forbid":{"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈbɪd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to order somebody not to do something; to order that something must not be done","cn":"禁止；不准","ex":{"en":"He forbade them from mentioning the subject again.","cn":"他不准他们再提这个话题。"}},{"en":"to make it difficult or impossible to do something","cn":"妨碍；阻碍；阻止","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Lack of space forbids further treatment of the topic here.","cn":"由于篇幅所限，这里不能深入阐述这个问题。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"禁止;不准","en":"If you forbid someone to do something, or if you forbid an activity, you order that it must not be done.","ex":{"en":"They'll forbid you to marry","cn":"他们不会准许你结婚。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"阻止;妨碍;阻碍","en":"If something forbids a particular course of action or state of affairs, it makes it impossible for the course of action or state of affairs to happen.","ex":{"en":"His own pride forbids him to ask Arthur's help","cn":"他的自尊心不允许他开口向阿瑟求助。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"God forbid→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"heaven forbid→see: ;"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forbid__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forbid__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"‘Maybe you'll end up as a lawyer, like me.’ ‘God forbid!’ “","cn":"也许你会像我一样，最终成为律师。” “但愿不会这样！”"},{"en":"Lack of space forbids further treatment of the topic here.","cn":"由于篇幅所限，这里不能深入阐述这个问题。"}]},"fountain":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fountain__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fountain__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfaʊntən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a structure from which water is sent up into the air by a pump, used to decorate parks and gardens","cn":"人工喷泉；喷水池"},{"en":"a strong flow of liquid or of another substance that is forced into the air","cn":"（液体或其他物质的）喷射，涌流","ex":{"en":"The amplifier exploded in a fountain of sparks.","cn":"放大器爆炸，喷射出火星。"}},{"en":"a rich source or supply of something","cn":"丰富来源；源泉","ex":{"en":"Tourism is a fountain of wealth for the city.","cn":"旅游业是该市的重要收入来源。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"喷泉;喷水池","en":"A fountain is an ornamental feature in a pool or lake which consists of a long narrow stream of water that is forced up into the air by a pump."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"喷射;喷涌","en":"A fountain of a liquid is an amount of it which is sent up into the air and falls back.","ex":{"en":"The volcano spewed a fountain of molten rock 650 feet in the air.","cn":"这座火山喷射出的岩浆高达650英尺。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"源泉;根源;来源","en":"If you describe a person or thing as a fountain of something, you mean they are an important source of it and supply a lot of it.","ex":{"en":"You are a fountain of ideas.","cn":"你就是思想的源泉。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Tourism is a fountain of wealth for the city.","cn":"旅游业是该市的重要收入来源。"},{"en":"The amplifier exploded in a fountain of sparks.","cn":"放大器爆炸，喷射出火星。"}]},"foe":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foe__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foe__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an enemy","cn":"敌人；仇敌","ex":{"en":"She was unsure as yet whether he was friend or foe.","cn":"她还不确定他是敌是友。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"敌人;对头","en":"Someone's foe is their enemy."}]},"examples":[{"en":"Britain’s friends and foes","cn":"英国的朋友和敌人"}]},"for":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/for__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/for__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fə(r)","pos":"preposition","senses":[{"en":"used to show who is intended to have or use something or where something is intended to be put","cn":"（表示对象、用途等）给，对，供","ex":{"en":"There's a letter for you.","cn":"有你一封信。"}},{"en":"in order to help somebody/something","cn":"以帮助；为了","ex":{"en":"What can I do for you (= how can I help you)?","cn":"有什么事我可以为你效劳？"}},{"en":"used to show purpose or function","cn":"（表示目的或功能）","ex":{"en":"a machine for slicing bread","cn":"面包切片机"}},{"en":"used to show a reason or cause","cn":"因为；由于","ex":{"en":"The town is famous for its cathedral.","cn":"这个城镇以大教堂著名。"}},{"en":"in order to obtain something","cn":"为得到；为获取","ex":{"en":"He came to me for advice.","cn":"他来征求我的意见。"}},{"en":"used to show a length of time","cn":"（表示一段时间）","ex":{"en":"I'm going away for a few days.","cn":"我要离开几天。"}},{"en":"used to show a distance","cn":"（表示距离）","ex":{"en":"The road went on for miles and miles.","cn":"这条道路绵延到很远的地方。"}},{"en":"used to show where somebody/something is going","cn":"（表示去向）往，向","ex":{"en":"Is this the bus for Chicago?","cn":"这辆公共汽车是去芝加哥的吗？"}},{"en":"used to show that something is arranged or intended to happen at a particular time","cn":"（安排或预定）在…时","ex":{"en":"an appointment for May 12","cn":"5 月 12 日的一次约见"}},{"en":"used to show the occasion when something happens","cn":"（表示场合）","ex":{"en":"I'm warning you for the last time—stop talking!","cn":"我最后一次警告你，闭嘴！"}},{"en":"in exchange for something","cn":"换取","ex":{"en":"Copies are available for two dollars each.","cn":"两美元一份。"}},{"en":"employed by","cn":"受雇于","ex":{"en":"She's working for an insurance company.","cn":"她在一家保险公司工作。"}},{"en":"about; in connection with somebody/something","cn":"关于；对于","ex":{"en":"They are anxious for her safety.","cn":"他们为她的安全担心。"}},{"en":"as a representative of","cn":"代表","ex":{"en":"I am speaking for everyone in this department.","cn":"我代表这个部门全体人员讲话。"}},{"en":"meaning","cn":"意思是","ex":{"en":"Shaking your head for ‘No’ is not universal.","cn":"以摇头表示“不”，并非放诸四海而皆准。"}},{"en":"in support of somebody/something","cn":"支持；拥护","ex":{"en":"Are you for or against the proposal?","cn":"你支持还是反对这个建议？"}},{"en":"considering what can be expected from somebody/something","cn":"就…而言","ex":{"en":"The weather was warm for the time of year.","cn":"在一年的这个时节这天气算是暖和的了。"}},{"en":"used to say how difficult, necessary, pleasant, etc. something is that somebody might do or has done","cn":"对（某人）来说（困难、必需、愉快等）","ex":{"en":"It's useless for us to continue.","cn":"我们继续做下去也无用。"}},{"en":"used to show who can or should do something","cn":"（表示谁可以或应该做某事）","ex":{"en":"It's not for me to say why he left.","cn":"由我说出他离开的原因不合适。"}},{"en":"better, happier, etc. following something","cn":"…后（更好、更快乐等）","ex":{"en":"You'll feel better for a good night's sleep.","cn":"你晚上睡个好觉就会觉得好些。"}},{"en":"used to introduce the reason for something mentioned in the previous statement","cn":"因为；由于","ex":{"en":"We listened eagerly, for he brought news of our families.","cn":"我们急不可待地听着，因为他带来了我们家人的消息。"},"pos":"conjunction"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示对象)为了，给，对于","en":"If something is for someone, they are intended to have it or benefit from it.","ex":{"en":"Isn't that enough for you?","cn":"那对你来说不够吗？"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"受雇于","en":"If you work or do a job for someone, you are employed by them.","ex":{"en":"I knew he worked for a security firm","cn":"我知道他在一家保安公司工作。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"代表(群体或组织)","en":"If you speak or act for a particular group or organization, you represent them.","ex":{"en":"She appears nightly on the television news, speaking for the State Department.","cn":"她作为国务院的发言人，每晚都会出现在电视新闻中。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"帮助;为了","en":"If someone does something for you, they do it so that you do not have to do it.","ex":{"en":"If your pharmacy doesn't stock the product you want, have them order it for you","cn":"如果药店没有你想要的药品，让他们为你订购。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"替…(感到);为…(感到)","en":"If you feel a particular emotion for someone, you feel it on their behalf.","ex":{"en":"This is the best thing you've ever done – I am so happy for you!","cn":"这是你做得最棒的一件事——我为你感到高兴！"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示情感的对象)对","en":"If you feel a particular emotion for someone or something, they are the object of that emotion, and you feel it when you think about them.","ex":{"en":"John, I'm sorry for Steve, but I think you've made the right decisions","cn":"约翰，我为史蒂夫感到难过，但是我想你的决定是正确的。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"供…之用;为…所需","en":"You use for after words such as 'time', 'space', 'money', or 'energy' when you say how much there is or whether there is enough of it in order to be able to do or use a particular thing.","ex":{"en":"Many new trains have space for wheelchair users","cn":"许多新型列车为坐轮椅者留有空间。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"供(销售、租用等)","en":"If something is for sale, hire, or use, it is available to be sold, hired, or used.","ex":{"en":"...fishmongers displaying freshwater fish for sale","cn":"摆摊卖淡水鱼的鱼贩"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示用途或目的)为了，用来","en":"You use for when you state or explain the purpose of an object, action, or activity.","ex":{"en":"...drug users who use unsterile equipment for injections of drugs","cn":"使用未经消毒的注射器注射毒品的吸毒者"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(置于名词后)因为，由于","en":"You use for after nouns expressing reason or cause.","ex":{"en":"He's soon to make a speech in parliament explaining his reasons for going","cn":"他很快要在议会发表讲话，说明他辞职的原因。"}},{"pos":"CONJ-SUBORD 连词","cn":"(引导从句)因为，为了","en":"You can use for to introduce a clause which gives the reason why you made the statement in the main clause.","ex":{"en":"He had a great desire to have a home of his own for he had always lived with my grandmother.","cn":"他强烈渴望拥有一个属于自己的家，因为他一直和我祖母住在一起。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"因为;以…为原因","en":"You can use for to introduce the cause of the fact that you have just mentioned.","ex":{"en":"...doing jobs that others turn down for lack of skill","cn":"做别人不愿意做的没有技术含量的工作"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(用于条件句中)如果不是为了，要不是","en":"For is used in conditional sentences, in expressions such as 'if not for' and 'were it not for', to introduce the only thing which prevents the main part of the sentence from being true.","ex":{"en":"If not for John, Brian wouldn't have learned the truth","cn":"要不是因为约翰，布赖恩也不可能知道真相。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示时间)持续","en":"You use for to say how long something lasts or continues.","ex":{"en":"The toaster remained on for more than an hour","cn":"烤面包机持续开了一个多小时。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示距离)延伸","en":"You use for to say how far something extends.","ex":{"en":"We drove on for a few miles","cn":"我们继续往前开了几公里。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"花费;以…的价钱","en":"If something is bought, sold, or done for a particular amount of money, that amount of money is its price.","ex":{"en":"We got the bus back to Tange for 30 cents","cn":"我们花了 30 美分坐公共汽车回到坦格。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"在(指定的时间)","en":"If something is planned for a particular time, it is planned to happen then.","ex":{"en":"...the Welsh Boat Show, planned for July 30–August 1","cn":"预定于 7 月 30 日至 8 月 1 日期间举办的威尔士船展"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"在，为了(某个场合)","en":"If you do something for a particular occasion, you do it on that occasion or to celebrate that occasion.","ex":{"en":"He asked his daughter what she would like for her birthday","cn":"他问女儿过生日想要什么。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"去;前往","en":"If you leave for a particular place or if you take a bus, train, plane, or boat for a place, you are going there.","ex":{"en":"They would be leaving for Rio early the next morning.","cn":"他们第二天一早要去里约。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"对…来说","en":"You use for when you make a statement about something in order to say how it affects or relates to someone, or what their attitude to it is.","ex":{"en":"What matters for most scientists is money and facilities","cn":"对多数科学家来说，资金和设备是至关重要的。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(用于形容词、名词和动词短语后，引出其后动词不定式的主语)","en":"After some adjective, noun, and verb phrases, you use for to introduce the subject of the action indicated by the following infinitive verb.","ex":{"en":"It might be possible for a single woman to be accepted as a foster parent","cn":"有可能会接受单身女子作为领养人。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"就…而言(表示相对来说不寻常)","en":"You use for when you say that an aspect of something or someone is surprising in relation to other aspects of them.","ex":{"en":"He was tall for an eight-year-old","cn":"对一个 8 岁的孩子而言，他长得很高。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"愿意做;打算从事;想要","en":"If you say that you are for a particular activity, you mean that this is what you want or intend to do.","ex":{"en":"Right, who's for a toasted sandwich then?","cn":"好吧，谁想要吐司三明治？"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"为…喜欢;对…适合","en":"If you say that something is not for you, you mean that you do not enjoy it or that it is not suitable for you.","ex":{"en":"Wendy decided the sport was not for her","cn":"温迪认定这项运动不适合她。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(表示负有责任或享有权利)由…","en":"If it is for you to do something, it is your responsibility or right to do it.","ex":{"en":"I wish you would come back to Washington with us, but that's for you to decide","cn":"我希望你能和我们一起回华盛顿，但是这由你决定。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"支持;同意","en":"If you are for something, you agree with it or support it.","ex":{"en":"Are you for or against public transport?","cn":"你是支持还是反对公共交通？"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(用于 argue, case, evidence, vote 等词后，引出所支持或被证明之事)","en":"You use for after words such as 'argue', 'case', 'evidence', or 'vote' in order to introduce the thing that is being supported or proved.","ex":{"en":"Another union has voted for industrial action in support of a pay claim","cn":"另一个工会已经投票赞成采取要求加薪的劳工行动。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(置于某些名词、形容词或动词后，引出更多信息或与某性质、事物或行为相关的事物)","en":"For is the preposition that is used after some nouns, adjectives, or verbs in order to introduce more information or to indicate what a quality, thing, or action relates to.","ex":{"en":"Reduced-calorie cheese is a great substitute for cream cheese","cn":"低卡路里干酪是奶油干酪的极佳替代品。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"以…命名","en":"To be named for someone means to be given the same name as them.","ex":{"en":"The Brady Bill is named for former White House Press Secretary James Brady","cn":"布雷迪法案是以前白宫新闻秘书詹姆斯·布雷迪的名字命名的。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(与 every 连用，引出比率)每…(就有…)","en":"You use for with 'every' when you are stating a ratio, to introduce one of the things in the ratio.","ex":{"en":"For every farm job that is lost, two or three other jobs in the area are put at risk","cn":"在该地区每有一个农民失去工作，另外两到三个从事其他工作的人就会面临失业的危险。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(用于比较)每镑对每镑/每英里对每英里","en":"You can use for in expressions such as pound for pound or mile for mile when you are making comparisons between the values or qualities of different things.","ex":{"en":"...the Antarctic, mile for mile one of the planet's most lifeless areas","cn":"南极洲的每一寸土地和世界上其他地方相比都是最荒芜的"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(意思)相当于，等于","en":"If a word or expression has the same meaning as another word or expression, you can say that the first one is another word or expression for the second one.","ex":{"en":"The technical term for sunburn is erythema","cn":"晒斑的专业术语是红斑。"}},{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"(引出可在其他地方找到的信息)至于，对于","en":"You use for in a piece of writing when you mention information which will be found somewhere else.","ex":{"en":"For further information on the life of William James Sidis, see Amy Wallace, 'The Prodigy'.","cn":"想了解关于威廉·詹姆斯·西迪斯生平的更多信息，请参阅埃米·华莱士所著《神童》。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(尽管有不同意见或实际困难)完全赞成,坚信","en":"If you say that you are all for doing something, you agree or strongly believe that it should be done, but you are also often suggesting that other people disagree with you or that there are practical difficulties.","ex":{"en":"I am all for cutting carbon dioxide emissions, but that would be much more easily achieved by giving subsidies to windpower, than with nuclear power","cn":"我完全赞成减少二氧化碳的排放，但是，相比发展核能，对发展风能提供补贴更容易实现这一目标。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"会惹麻烦;要闯祸","en":"If you are in for it or, in British English, if you are for it, you are likely to get into trouble because of something you have done."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"首次/最后一次","en":"You use expressions such as for the first time and for the last time when you are talking about how often something has happened before. as for→see: ;","ex":{"en":"He was married for the second time, this time to a Belgian","cn":"他第二次结婚，这一次是和一个比利时人。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"but for→see: ; for all→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She might at least have called to explain. There's gratitude for you.","cn":"她本来至少可以来电话解释一下。她就这么表示感谢。"},{"en":"We listened eagerly, for he brought news of our families.","cn":"我们急不可待地听着，因为他带来了我们家人的消息。"}]},"fought":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Fought is the past tense and past participle of fight ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fought__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fought__us_1.mp3"}},"focal":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊkl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"central; very important; connected with or providing a focus","cn":"中心的；很重要的；焦点的；有焦点的","ex":{"en":"The Student Liaison Officer acts as a focal point for student political activity.","cn":"学生联络官充当学生政治活动的联络人。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"焦点的;有焦点的","en":"Focal is used to describe something that relates to the point where a number of rays or lines meet.","ex":{"en":"...the focal plane of the telescope.","cn":"望远镜的焦平面"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"重要的;中心的","en":"Focal is used to describe something that is very important.","ex":{"en":"...one of the focal centres of the Far East.","cn":"远东的中心地区之一"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/focal__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/focal__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"This issue has now become the focal centre of interest.","cn":"这一问题现已成为关注的焦点。"}]},"fourteenth":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fourteenth__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fourteenth__us_1.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ORD 序数词","cn":"第十四","en":"The fourteenth item in a series is the one that you count as number fourteen.","ex":{"en":"The Festival, now in its fourteenth year, has become a major international jazz event.","cn":"这个艺术节现在进行到第14届，已经成为国际爵士乐的一大盛会。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He used to work fourteen hours a day.","cn":""},{"en":"I started playing the guitar when I was fourteen (= 14 years old ) .","cn":""}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌfɔːˈtiːnθ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"each of fourteen equal parts of something","cn":"四"},{"en":"14th","cn":"十四","pos":"ordinal number"}]}},"foreign":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foreign__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foreign__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrən","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"in or from a country that is not your own","cn":"外国的","ex":{"en":"What foreign languages do you speak?","cn":"你会说哪几种外语？"}},{"en":"dealing with or involving other countries","cn":"涉外的；外交的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"This is a huge departure for the country's foreign policy.","cn":"这对于该国的外交政策来说是一个巨大的背离。"}},{"en":"not typical of somebody/something; not known to somebody/something and therefore seeming strange","cn":"非典型的；陌生的","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Dishonesty is foreign to his nature.","cn":"弄虚作假并非他的本性。"}},{"en":"an object that has entered something by accident and should not be there","cn":"异物；异体","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"Tears help to protect the eye from potentially harmful foreign bodies.","cn":"眼泪有助于保护眼睛去除可能有害的异物。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"外国的;来自国外的","en":"Something or someone that is foreign comes from or relates to a country that is not your own.","ex":{"en":"...in Frankfurt, where a quarter of the population is foreign","cn":"在有四分之一的人口是外来移民的法兰克福"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"外交的;外国的;对外的","en":"In politics and journalism, foreign is used to describe people, jobs, and activities relating to countries that are not the country of the person or government concerned.","ex":{"en":"...the German foreign minister","cn":"德国外交部长"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"异质的;外来的","en":"A foreign object is something that has got into something else, usually by accident, and should not be there.","ex":{"en":"The patient's immune system would reject the transplanted organ as a foreign object.","cn":"病人的免疫系统会对移植器官产生异质排斥反应。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"陌生的;不熟悉的;非典型的","en":"Something that is foreign to a particular person or thing is not typical of them or is unknown to them.","ex":{"en":"The very notion of price competition is foreign to many schools","cn":"价格竞争这个概念对于许多学校都很陌生。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Tears help to protect the eye from potentially harmful foreign bodies.","cn":"眼泪有助于保护眼睛去除可能有害的异物。"},{"en":"You could tell she was foreign by the way she dressed.","cn":"从她的穿着就可以看出她是外国人。"}]},"follow":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/follow__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/follow__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to come or go after or behind somebody/something","cn":"跟随；跟着","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"go after","ex":{"en":"Follow me please.","cn":"请跟我来。"}},{"en":"to come or go after or behind somebody in order to watch where they go and what they do","cn":"跟踪；追踪","g":"[transitive]","sc":"go after","ex":{"en":"I think we're being followed.","cn":"我觉得有人跟踪我们。"}},{"en":"to come after something/somebody else in time or order; to happen as a result of something else","cn":"（时间或顺序上）在…后发生；因…而发生","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"happen/do after","ex":{"en":"I remember little of the days that followed the accident.","cn":"那次事故以后的日子我记不大清楚了。"}},{"en":"to do something after something else","cn":"在…后做","g":"[transitive]","sc":"happen/do after","ex":{"en":"Give your contact details and follow this with a brief profile of yourself.","cn":"给出你的详细联系方式，然后简要介绍一下自己。"}},{"en":"to accept advice, instructions, etc. and do what you have been told or shown to do","cn":"接受，遵循，听从（忠告、指示等）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"advice/instructions","ex":{"en":"to follow rules/procedures/guidelines","cn":"遵循规则／程序／指南"}},{"en":"to accept somebody/something as a guide, a leader or an example; to copy somebody/something","cn":"接受…为指导（或领导、榜样）；追随；拥护；仿效","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"accept/copy","ex":{"en":"I encourage others to follow our example.","cn":"我鼓励其他人仿效我们。"}},{"en":"to click on a link in a website","cn":"点击（网络链接）","sc":"website","ex":{"en":"Follow the links to sign up for the webinar.","cn":"点击链接报名参加网络研讨会。"}},{"en":"to go along a road, path, etc.","cn":"沿着（道路、小径等）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"road/path","ex":{"en":"Follow this road until you get to the school, then turn left.","cn":"沿着这条路走到学校，然后向左拐。"}},{"en":"to go in the same direction as something or parallel to something","cn":"沿着…伸延；与…平行","g":"[transitive]","sc":"road/path","ex":{"en":"The lane follows the edge of a wood for about a mile.","cn":"小路沿树林边延伸约一英里。"}},{"en":"to be the logical result of something","cn":"是…的必然结果","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"be result","ex":{"en":"I don't see how that follows from what you've just said.","cn":"根据你刚才所说的，我不明白怎么会产生那样的结果。"}},{"en":"to understand an explanation or the meaning of something","cn":"理解，明白（说明或意思）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"understand","ex":{"en":"Sorry, I don't follow.","cn":"对不起，我不明白。"}},{"en":"to watch or listen to somebody/something very carefully","cn":"密切注视；倾听","g":"[transitive]","sc":"watch/listen","ex":{"en":"The children were following every word of the story intently.","cn":"孩子们一字不漏地专心听故事。"}},{"en":"to take an active interest in something and be aware of what is happening; to support a sports team","cn":"对…产生浓厚兴趣而关注；支持（某运动队）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"be interested in","ex":{"en":"We've been following this story for months.","cn":"我们已经关注这件事好几个月了。"}},{"en":"to choose to regularly see content from a person, company, etc. using a social media service","cn":"（在微博客上）关注（人、公司等）","g":"[transitive]","sc":"be interested in","ex":{"en":"I don’t follow many celebrities on Twitter any more.","cn":"我不再在推特上关注很多名人了。"}},{"en":"to be about the life or development of somebody/something","cn":"涉及…生活；有关…发展","g":"[transitive]","sc":"of book/movie","ex":{"en":"The novel follows the fortunes of a village community in Scotland.","cn":"小说叙述了苏格兰一个村落的变迁。"}},{"en":"to develop or happen in a particular way","cn":"按…方式（或方向）发展；以…方式发生","g":"[transitive]","sc":"pattern/course","ex":{"en":"The day followed the usual pattern.","cn":"这一天和平常过得一样。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"跟随;跟着","en":"If you follow someone who is going somewhere, you move along behind them because you want to go to the same place.","ex":{"en":"We followed him up the steps into a large hall","cn":"我们跟着他上楼来到一个很大的大厅。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"尾随;跟踪","en":"If you follow someone who is going somewhere, you move along behind them without their knowledge, in order to catch them or find out where they are going.","ex":{"en":"She realized that the Mercedes was following her","cn":"她意识到那辆奔驰在跟踪她。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"追随","en":"If you follow someone to a place where they have recently gone and where they are now, you go to join them there.","ex":{"en":"He followed Janice to New York, where she was preparing an exhibition.","cn":"他追随贾尼丝到了纽约，她正在那里准备一个展览。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"接着…发生;在…后发生","en":"An event, activity, or period of time that follows a particular thing happens or comes after that thing, at a later time.","ex":{"en":"...the rioting and looting that followed the verdict","cn":"判决宣布之后发生的暴乱和抢劫"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"在…后做(或说)","en":"If you follow one thing with another, you do or say the second thing after you have done or said the first thing.","ex":{"en":"Her first major role was in Martin Scorsese's 'Goodfellas' and she followed this with a part in Spike Lee's 'Jungle Fever'.","cn":"她主演的第一部影片是马丁·斯科塞斯的《好家伙》，之后接拍了斯派克·李的《丛林热》。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"可以推断出;由此得出","en":"If it follows that a particular thing is the case, that thing is a logical result of something else being true or being the case.","ex":{"en":"Just because a bird does not breed one year, it does not follow that it will fail the next","cn":"不能因为一只鸟某一年没有繁殖就断定它第二年也不会繁殖。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(文章或讲演)接下来是,后面的是，下面是","en":"If you refer to the words that follow or followed, you are referring to the words that come next or came next in a piece of writing or speech.","ex":{"en":"What follows is an eyewitness account","cn":"接下来的是目击者的陈述。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"循着，沿着(道路、标志等)","en":"If you follow a path, route, or set of signs, you go somewhere using the path, route, or signs to direct you.","ex":{"en":"If they followed the road, they would be certain to reach a village","cn":"如果他们沿着这条路走，就一定会到达一个村庄。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(小径、河流等)沿着，经过","en":"If something such as a path or river follows a particular route or line, it goes along that route or line.","ex":{"en":"Our route follows the Pacific coast through densely populated neighbourhoods","cn":"我们的路线沿着太平洋海岸，途经人口稠密的街区。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"注视(运动物体);(眼睛)跟随着","en":"If you follow something with your eyes, or if your eyes follow it, you watch it as it moves or you look along its route or course.","ex":{"en":"Ann's eyes followed a police car as it drove slowly past.","cn":"安注视着一辆缓缓驶过的警车。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"按照…方式发展;以…方式发生","en":"Something that follows a particular course of development happens or develops in that way.","ex":{"en":"His release turned out to follow the pattern set by that of the other six hostages.","cn":"最终他的获释方式也和其他 6名人质的获释如出一辙。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"接受，遵循(建议、指示等);按(菜谱)进行","en":"If you follow advice, an instruction, or a recipe, you act or do something in the way that it indicates.","ex":{"en":"Take care to follow the instructions carefully","cn":"注意严格按照说明进行。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"仿效;效仿","en":"If you follow what someone else has done, you do it too because you think it is a good thing or because you want to copy them.","ex":{"en":"His admiration for the athlete did not extend to the point where he would follow his example in taking drugs","cn":"他对于这个运动员的崇拜还没有达到要学他吸毒的程度。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"沿袭;继承","en":"If you follow someone in what you do, you do the same thing or job as they did previously.","ex":{"en":"He followed his father and became a surgeon","cn":"他子承父业，成为了一名外科医生。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"理解，跟得上(解释或故事情节)","en":"If you are able to follow something such as an explanation or the story of a film, you understand it as it continues and develops.","ex":{"en":"Can you follow the plot so far?","cn":"目前为止剧情你能看得懂吗？"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"追踪;对…感兴趣;关注","en":"If you follow something, you take an interest in it and keep informed about what happens.","ex":{"en":"...the millions of people who follow football because they genuinely love it","cn":"数以百万计的人关注足球，因为他们发自内心地热爱足球"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"以…为原型;讲述…的故事","en":"A story, film, or television programme that follows someone or something is about their experiences over a particular period of time.","ex":{"en":"The film follows the fortunes of two women.","cn":"这部电影讲述了两个女人的命运。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(欣赏节目的同时)对照看(脚本或乐谱)","en":"If you follow a score or written copy of a play, you read it while you listen to it being performed.","ex":{"en":"...an annotated version of Mozart's opera that allows the listener to follow the score.","cn":"使听者能够一边欣赏一边对照着看的莫扎特歌剧的注释乐谱"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"信奉;追随;支持;拥护","en":"If you follow a particular religion or political belief, you have that religion or belief.","ex":{"en":"'Do you follow any particular religion?' — 'Yes, we're all Hindus.'","cn":"“你们有自己的宗教信仰吗？”——“是的，我们都是印度教徒。”"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"如下;分别是","en":"You use as follows in writing or speech to introduce something such as a list, description, or explanation.","ex":{"en":"The winners are as follows: E. Walker; R. Foster; R. Gates; A. Mackintosh","cn":"优胜者分别是：E.沃克、R.福斯特、R.盖茨和A.麦金托什。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"紧随其后;其次是","en":"You use followed by to say what comes after something else in a list or ordered set of things.","ex":{"en":"Potatoes are still the most popular food, followed by white bread.","cn":"马铃薯仍然是最受欢迎的食物，其次是白面包。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"下一道菜","en":"After mentioning one course of a meal, you can mention the next course by saying what you will have to follow or what there will be to follow .","ex":{"en":"He decided on roast chicken and vegetables, with apple pie to follow.","cn":"他决定点烤鸡配蔬菜，然后是苹果派。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to follow in someone's footsteps→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to follow your nose→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to follow suit→see: ;"},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"探究;钻研;深入研究","en":"If you follow through an action, plan, or idea or follow through with it, you continue doing or thinking about it until you have done everything possible.","ex":{"en":"The leadership has been unwilling to follow through the implications of these ideas","cn":"领导层不愿意对这些想法的含意进行深入探究。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"追查;将…深入下去;对…采取进一步行动","en":"If you follow up something that has been said, suggested, or discovered, you try to find out more about it or take action about it.","ex":{"en":"State security police are following up several leads","cn":"国家安全警察正在追查几条线索。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：follow through follow up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The garage is a mile ahead up the hill — just follow your nose.","cn":"汽车修理站在前面一英里处的山坡上，一直往前走就可以到。"},{"en":"The police are following up several leads after their TV appeal for information.","cn":"警方在电视上呼吁提供信息后正沿着几条线索继续追查。"}]},"formal":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formal__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formal__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːml","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very correct and suitable for official or important occasions","cn":"适合正式场合的；正规的；庄重的","ex":{"en":"ladies in formal evening wear","cn":"穿晚礼服的女士们"}},{"en":"official; following an agreed or official way of doing things","cn":"正式的；合乎规矩的","ex":{"en":"formal legal processes","cn":"正式法律程序"}},{"en":"received in a school, college or university, with lessons, exams, etc., rather than gained just through practical experience","cn":"正规的","ex":{"en":"He has no formal teaching qualifications.","cn":"他没有正规的教学资历证明。"}},{"en":"connected with the way something is done rather than what is done","cn":"方式上的；做法上的；形式上的","ex":{"en":"Getting approval for the plan is a purely formal matter; nobody will seriously oppose it.","cn":"计划报批纯粹是一个形式上的问题，没有人会当真反对的。"}},{"en":"arranged in a regular manner, according to a clear, exact plan","cn":"整齐的；布置井然的","ex":{"en":"delightful formal gardens, with terraced lawns and an avenue of trees","cn":"精心布置的有片片草坪和林荫道的宜人花园"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"正式的;规范的;庄重的","en":"Formal speech or behaviour is very correct and serious rather than relaxed and friendly, and is used especially in official situations.","ex":{"en":"He wrote a very formal letter of apology to Douglas","cn":"他给道格拉斯写了一封非常正式的道歉信。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(行为、声明或要求)官方的，正式的","en":"A formal action, statement, or request is an official one.","ex":{"en":"UN officials said a formal request was passed to American authorities","cn":"联合国官员称正式请求已向美国当局转达。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(场合)正式的，合乎礼仪的","en":"Formal occasions are special occasions at which people wear smart clothes and behave according to a set of accepted rules.","ex":{"en":"One evening the film company arranged a formal dinner after the play.","cn":"一天晚上，电影公司在演出结束后安排了一个正式的晚宴。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(服饰)正规的，正式的，适合正式场合的","en":"Formal clothes are very smart clothes that are suitable for formal occasions.","ex":{"en":"They wore ordinary ties instead of the more formal high collar and cravat.","cn":"他们打着普通的领带，而不是更为正式的高领领结。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"整齐的;规矩的;井然有序的","en":"Something that is done, written, or studied in a formal way has a very ordered, organized method or style.","ex":{"en":"This does not encourage the child to analyse the environment in a formal way","cn":"这并不能鼓励孩子有条理地分析周围的环境。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(通常指学校教育)正规的","en":"Formal education or training is given officially, usually in a school, college, or university.","ex":{"en":"Although his formal education stopped after primary school, he was an avid reader","cn":"尽管小学毕业后就再没有受过正规的教育，他却十分爱读书。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(尤指按照某种设计规则)布局匀称的，布置整齐的","en":"A formal garden or room is arranged in a very regular and controlled way, especially according to certain rules of design.","ex":{"en":"...a formal herb garden","cn":"布局匀称的草药园"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Although not formally trained as an art historian, he is widely respected for his knowledge of the period.","cn":"虽然他不是科班出身的艺术史学家，但他对这一时期的知识却普遍为人尊重。"},{"en":"Getting approval for the plan is a purely formal matter; nobody will seriously oppose it.","cn":"寻求计划获得批准纯粹是一个形式上的问题，没有人会认真反对的。"}]},"forever":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forever__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forever__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fərˈevə(r)","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"used to say that a particular situation or state will always exist","cn":"永远","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"I'll love you forever!","cn":"我永远爱你！"}},{"en":"a very long time","cn":"长久地","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"It takes her forever to get dressed.","cn":"她穿衣打扮要用好长的时间。"}},{"en":"used with verbs in the progressive tenses to say that somebody does something very often and in a way that is annoying to other people","cn":"（与动词进行时连用）老是，没完没了地","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"She's forever going on about how poor they are.","cn":"她老是没完没了地讲他们有多穷。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"永远;永恒;永久","en":"If you say that something will happen or continue forever, you mean that it will always happen or continue.","ex":{"en":"I think that we will live together forever","cn":"我想我们会永远生活在一起。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"完全地;永恒地","en":"If something has gone or changed forever, it has gone or changed completely and permanently.","ex":{"en":"The old social order was gone forever","cn":"旧的社会秩序一去不复返了。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"长久地;无尽头地","en":"If you say that something takes forever or lasts forever, you are emphasizing that it takes or lasts a very long time, or that it seems to.","ex":{"en":"The drive seemed to take forever","cn":"车似乎永远也开不到头。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"老是;没完没了地","en":"If you say that someone is forever doing a particular thing, especially something which annoys or amuses you, you are emphasizing that they do it very often.","ex":{"en":"He was forever attempting to arrange deals","cn":"他老是想撮合交易。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"总是;始终","en":"You use forever to emphasize that someone always has or shows the quality mentioned.","ex":{"en":"Katherine was forever secretive","cn":"凯瑟琳总是神神秘秘的。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Just keep telling yourself that it won't last forever.","cn":"要不停地提醒自己，这不会永世长存的。"},{"en":"She's forever going on about how poor they are.","cn":"她老是没完没了地讲他们有多穷。"}]},"following":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/following__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/following__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that is/are going to be mentioned next","cn":"下述的；下列的","ex":{"en":"Answer the following questions.","cn":"回答下列问题。"}},{"en":"next in time","cn":"（时间上）接着的","ex":{"en":"the following afternoon/month/year/week","cn":"第二天下午；第二个月；第二年；第二周"}},{"en":"the thing or things that you will mention next; the person or people that you will mention next","cn":"下述；下列；如下","ex":{"en":"The following is a summary of events.","cn":"现将重大事件综述如下。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a group of supporters","cn":"（统称）拥护者，追随者","g":"[usually singular]","ex":{"en":"The band has a huge following in Italy.","cn":"这支乐队在意大利有一大批热心的追随者。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"after or as a result of a particular event","cn":"在（某事）以后；由于","ex":{"en":"He took charge of the family business following his father's death.","cn":"父亲死后他就接管了家族企业。"},"pos":"preposition"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"PREP 介词","cn":"在…之后;紧接着","en":"Following a particular event means after that event.","ex":{"en":"In the centuries following Christ's death, Christians genuinely believed the world was about to end","cn":"在耶稣死后的几个世纪里，基督徒们真的相信世界将要灭亡。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"接下来的;之后的","en":"The following day, week, or year is the day, week, or year after the one you have just mentioned.","ex":{"en":"The following day the picture appeared on the front pages of every newspaper in the world","cn":"第二天照片出现在全世界所有报纸的头版。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"接下来的;下面的","en":"You use following to refer to something that you are about to mention.","ex":{"en":"Write down the following information: name of product, type, date purchased and price","cn":"请写明如下信息：产品名称、类型、购买日期和价格。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(统称)支持者，拥护者","en":"A person or organization that has a following has a group of people who support or admire their beliefs or actions.","ex":{"en":"Australian rugby league enjoys a huge following in New Zealand.","cn":"澳大利亚橄榄球联盟在新西兰有众多支持者。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(风向)顺的;顺风的","en":"If a boat or vehicle has a following wind, the wind is moving in the same direction as the boat or vehicle.","ex":{"en":"The following wind and eastward running tide had given us a very pleasant, lazy sail.","cn":"顺风和向东的潮水使我们的航行很惬意、很省力。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The following have been chosen to take part: Watts, Hodges and Lennox.","cn":"已选定下列人员参加：沃茨、霍奇斯和伦诺克斯。"},{"en":"They arrived on Monday evening and we got there the following day.","cn":"他们是星期一晚上到的，我们次日也抵达那里。"}]},"fool":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fool__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fool__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fuːl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who you think behaves or speaks in a way that lacks intelligence or good judgement","cn":"蠢人；傻瓜","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Don't be such a fool!","cn":"别这么傻了！"}},{"en":"(in the past) a man employed by a king or queen to entertain people by telling jokes, singing songs, etc.","cn":"（旧时国王或王后豢养供人娱乐的）小丑，弄臣","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"court fools who used to provide entertainment in the royal court","cn":"旧时在皇宫里逗乐的宫廷小丑"}},{"en":"a cold light dessert (= a sweet dish) made from fruit that is cooked to make it soft and mixed with cream or custard","cn":"奶油果泥，蛋奶果泥（甜食）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"rhubarb fool","cn":"奶油大黄泥"}},{"en":"to trick somebody into believing something that is not true","cn":"欺骗；愚弄","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"You don't fool me!","cn":"不要骗我！"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to say or do stupid or silly things, often in order to make people laugh","cn":"说蠢话，干傻事（常为逗乐）","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Stop fooling around and sit down!","cn":"别干傻事了，坐下来！"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"showing a lack of intelligence or good judgement","cn":"傻的；愚蠢的","ex":{"en":"That was a damn fool thing to do!","cn":"干那种事真蠢！"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"傻子;蠢人;白痴","en":"If you call someone a fool, you are indicating that you think they are not at all sensible and show a lack of good judgment.","ex":{"en":"'You fool!' she shouted","cn":"“你这个白痴!”她大叫道。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"傻的;愚蠢的","en":"Fool is used to describe an action or person that is not at all sensible and shows a lack of good judgment.","ex":{"en":"What a damn fool thing to do!","cn":"做的什么蠢事啊!"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"愚弄;欺骗","en":"If someone fools you, they deceive or trick you.","ex":{"en":"Art dealers fool a lot of people","cn":"艺术经纪人能欺骗很多人。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"瞎弄;瞎折腾;糊弄","en":"If you say that a person is fooling with something or someone, you mean that the way they are behaving is likely to cause problems.","ex":{"en":"What are you doing fooling with such a staggering sum of money?","cn":"你拿着这么一大笔钱瞎折腾什么呢？"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(旧时国王或王后豢养的)弄臣，小丑","en":"In the courts of kings and queens in medieval Europe, the fool was the person whose job was to do silly things in order to make people laugh."},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"奶油果泥;蛋奶果泥","en":"Fool is a dessert made by mixing soft cooked fruit with whipped cream or with custard.","ex":{"en":"...gooseberry fool.","cn":"奶油醋栗泥"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"让…出丑;戏弄","en":"If you make a fool of someone, you make them seem silly by telling people about something stupid that they have done, or by tricking them.","ex":{"en":"Your brother is making a fool of you","cn":"你哥哥在戏弄你。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"出丑;让人看笑话","en":"If you make a fool of yourself, you behave in a way that makes other people think that you are silly or lacking in good judgment.","ex":{"en":"He was drinking and making a fool of himself.","cn":"他在喝酒，让自己出尽了丑。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"那样做真傻","en":"If you say to someone 'More fool you' when they tell you what they have done or what they plan to do, you are indicating that you think that it is silly and shows a lack of judgment.","ex":{"en":"Most managers couldn't care less about information technology. More fool them.","cn":"多数的经理管理者根本不关心信息技术，他们真的很傻。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"扮傻逗乐","en":"If you play the fool or act the fool, you behave in a playful, childish, and foolish way, usually in order to make other people laugh.","ex":{"en":"They used to play the fool together, calling each other silly names and giggling.","cn":"他们过去常在一起胡闹，互相取笑。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to suffer fools gladly→see: ;"},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"吊儿郎当;游荡;鬼混","en":"If you fool around, you behave in a silly, dangerous, or irresponsible way.","ex":{"en":"They were fooling around on an Army firing range","cn":"他们在军队的射击训练场里闲晃。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"有私情;乱搞","en":"If someone fools around with another person, especially when one of them is married, they have a casual sexual relationship.","ex":{"en":"Never fool around with the clients' wives","cn":"永远不要和客户的妻子乱搞。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"犯傻;扮傻逗乐","en":"If you fool around, you behave in a playful, childish, and silly way, often in order to make people laugh. In British English, you can also say you fool about .","ex":{"en":"Stop fooling about, man","cn":"不要再扮傻充愣了，老兄。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：fool about fool around"}]},"examples":[{"en":"You're fooling yourself if you think none of this will affect you.","cn":"你要是认为此事一点也不会影响你，那就是欺骗自己。"},{"en":"He told me he was an actor and I was fool enough to believe him.","cn":"他告诉我他是演员，而我真傻，竟相信了他的话。"}]},"fostering":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒstə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to encourage sth to develop","cn":"促进；助长；培养；鼓励"},{"en":"( especially BrE ) to take another person's child into your home for a period of time, without becoming his or her legal parents","cn":"代养，抚育，照料（他人子女一段时间）"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foster__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foster__us_1.mp3"}},"foods":{"oxford":{"phon":"fuːd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"things that people or animals eat","cn":"食物"},{"en":"a particular type of food （","cn":"某种）食物"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/food__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/food__us_1.mp3"}},"foster":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foster__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foster__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒstə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to encourage something to develop","cn":"促进；助长；培养；鼓励","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"The club's aim is to foster better relations within the community.","cn":"俱乐部的宗旨是促进团体内部的关系。"}},{"en":"to take another person’s child into your home for a period of time, without becoming his or her legal parents","cn":"代养，抚育，照料（他人子女一段时间）","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"They have fostered over 60 children during the past ten years.","cn":"在过去十年间，他们抚育了 60 多个儿童。"}},{"en":"used with some nouns in connection with the fostering of a child","cn":"（与某些代养有关的名词连用）","ex":{"en":"a foster mother/father/family","cn":"代养母亲／父亲；代养的家庭"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"寄养的;代养的","en":"Foster parents are people who officially take a child into their family for a period of time, without becoming the child's legal parents. The child is referred to as their foster child.","ex":{"en":"Little Jack was placed with foster parents","cn":"小杰克和养父母住在一起。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"寄养;代养","en":"If you foster a child, you take it into your family for a period of time, without becoming its legal parent.","ex":{"en":"She has since gone on to find happiness by fostering more than 100 children.","cn":"从那以后她代养了 100 多个孩子，并从中得到快乐。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"促进;鼓励;培养","en":"To foster something such as an activity or idea means to help it to develop.","ex":{"en":"He said that developed countries had a responsibility to foster global economic growth to help new democracies","cn":"他说，发达国家有责任促进全球经济增长，以帮助新兴民主国家。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"They have fostered over 60 children during the past ten years.","cn":"在过去十年间，他们抚育了 60 多个儿童。"},{"en":"We couldn't adopt a child, so we decided to foster.","cn":"我们不能领养孩子，所以决定代养一个。"}]},"foam":{"media":{"img":["media/pic/froth_comp.jpg","media/thumb/foam.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/foam__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foam__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a soft light rubber material, full of small holes, that is used for seats, mattresses, etc.","cn":"泡沫橡胶；海绵橡胶","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a foam mattress","cn":"泡沫橡胶床垫"}},{"en":"a mass of very small air bubbles on the surface of a liquid","cn":"泡沫","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a glass of beer with a good head of foam","cn":"一杯表面有厚厚一层泡沫的啤酒"}},{"en":"a chemical substance that forms or produces a soft mass of very small bubbles, used for washing, shaving (= cutting hair from the skin), or putting out fires, for example","cn":"泡沫剂（用于洗涤、剃须、灭火等）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"a bottle of bath foam","cn":"一瓶沐浴露"}},{"en":"to have or produce a mass of small bubbles","cn":"有泡沫；起泡沫","ex":{"en":"She looked down at the foaming white water.","cn":"她低头看着泛着泡沫的白水。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"泡沫;气泡","en":"Foam consists of a mass of small bubbles that are formed when air and a liquid are mixed together.","ex":{"en":"The water curved round the rocks in great bursts of foam.","cn":"水流撞击岩石，产生大量泡沫。"}},{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"泡沫剂;泡沫产品","en":"Foam is used to refer to various kinds of manufactured products which have a soft, light texture like a thick liquid.","ex":{"en":"...shaving foam.","cn":"剃须泡沫"}},{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"泡沫橡胶;海绵式橡胶","en":"Foam or foam rubber is soft rubber full of small holes which is used, for example, to make mattresses and cushions.","ex":{"en":"...modern three-piece suites filled with foam rubber","cn":"有泡沫橡胶填充物的现代家具三件套"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(液体)产生泡沫，起沫","en":"If a liquid foams, it is full of small bubbles and keeps moving slightly.","ex":{"en":"I let the water run into it and we watched as it foamed and bubbled.","cn":"我把水引进去，然后我们看着它起沫、冒泡。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"大怒;暴怒;大发雷霆","en":"If you say that someone is foaming at the mouth, you mean that they are very angry.","ex":{"en":"Stewart was foaming at the mouth about an incident the previous afternoon.","cn":"斯图尔特正为头天下午的事件而大发脾气。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"a glass of beer with a good head of foam","cn":"一杯表面有厚厚一层泡沫的啤酒"},{"en":"The breaking waves left the beach covered with foam.","cn":"浪花四溅，海滩上满是泡沫。"}]},"foggy":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foggy__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foggy__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒɡi","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not clear because of fog","cn":"有雾的；雾茫茫的","ex":{"en":"foggy conditions","cn":"有雾的天气"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有雾的","en":"When it is foggy, there is fog.","ex":{"en":"It's quite foggy now","cn":"现在雾很大。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"一点儿也不知道;根本没什么概念","en":"If you say that you haven't the foggiest or you haven't the foggiest idea, you are emphasizing that you do not know something.","ex":{"en":"I did not have the foggiest idea what he meant","cn":"我根本不知道他是什么意思。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘Do you know where she is?’ ‘Sorry, I haven't the foggiest.’ “","cn":"你知道她在哪儿吗？” “对不起，我一点也不知道。”"},{"en":"a foggy road","cn":"雾茫茫的道路"}]},"former":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/former__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/former__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmə(r)","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that existed in earlier times","cn":"以前的","ex":{"en":"This fine ruin was, in former times, a royal castle.","cn":"这个保留完好的遗址以前是座皇家城堡。"}},{"en":"that used to have a particular position or status in the past","cn":"昔日的；前","ex":{"en":"the 41-year-old former world champion","cn":"41岁的前世界冠军"}},{"en":"used to refer to the first of two things or people mentioned","cn":"（两者中）前者的","ex":{"en":"The former option would be much more sensible.","cn":"前一种选择要明智得多。"}},{"en":"the first of two things or people mentioned","cn":"（两者中的）前者","ex":{"en":"He had to choose between giving up his job and giving up his principles. He chose the former.","cn":"他得在放弃工作和放弃原则二者中择其一。他选择了前者。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a person or thing that forms something","cn":"形成者；构成物","ex":{"en":"opinion formers and policy makers","cn":"意见领袖和政策制定者"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"前任的;先前的","en":"Former is used to describe someone who used to have a particular job, position, or role, but no longer has it.","ex":{"en":"The unemployed executives include former sales managers, directors and accountants.","cn":"被解雇的管理人员包括前销售经理、主管和会计。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(国家)原先的，先前的","en":"Former is used to refer to countries which no longer exist or whose boundaries have changed.","ex":{"en":"...the former Soviet Union.","cn":"前苏联"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"昔日的;旧时的;曾经的","en":"Former is used to describe something which used to belong to someone or which used to be a particular thing.","ex":{"en":"...the former home of Sir Christopher Wren.","cn":"克里斯托弗·雷恩爵士的旧居"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"早先的;从前的","en":"Former is used to describe a situation or period of time which came before the present one.","ex":{"en":"He would want you to remember him as he was in former years.","cn":"他可能会希望你记住他早年的样子。"}},{"pos":"PRON 代词","cn":"前者;前一个","en":"When two people, things, or groups have just been mentioned, you can refer to the first of them as the former . →see usage note at:","ex":{"en":"Given the choice between a pure white T-shirt and a more expensive, dirty cream one, most people can be forgiven for choosing the former","cn":"如果要在一件纯白的 T 恤和一件更贵的脏兮兮的米色 T 恤之间选择的话，多数人都会选前者，这是无可厚非的。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He had to choose between giving up his job and giving up his principles. He chose the former.","cn":"他得在放弃工作和放弃原则二者中择其一。他选择了前者。"},{"en":"This beautiful old building has been restored to its former glory.","cn":"这座美丽的老建筑物已恢复了昔日的壮观。"}]},"forecast":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːkɑːst","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a statement about what will happen in the future, based on information that is available now","cn":"预测；预报","ex":{"en":"The sales forecasts are encouraging.","cn":"这些销售预测令人鼓舞。"}},{"en":"to say what you think will happen in the future based on information that you have now","cn":"预测；预报","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"Experts are forecasting a recovery in the economy.","cn":"专家预测经济将复苏。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"预报;预测","en":"A forecast is a statement of what is expected to happen in the future, especially in relation to a particular event or situation.","ex":{"en":"...a forecast of a 2.25 per cent growth in the economy","cn":"经济增长 2.25% 的预测"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"预测;预言","en":"If you forecast future events, you say what you think is going to happen in the future.","ex":{"en":"They forecast a humiliating defeat for the Prime Minister","cn":"他们预言首相将遭遇惨败。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forecast__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forecast__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The report forecasts that prices will rise by 3% next month.","cn":"报告预测下月物价将上涨 3%。"},{"en":"It is difficult to forecast how the markets will react.","cn":"很难预测市场会有什么样的反应。"}]},"forward-looking":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːwəd lʊkɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"planning for the future; willing to consider modern ideas and methods","cn":"向前看的；有远见的；有进步思想的","ex":{"en":"a forward-looking company","cn":"有远见的公司"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有远见的;向前看的;进步的","en":"If you describe a person or organization as forward-looking, you approve of the fact that they think about the future or have modern ideas.","ex":{"en":"...the need for the party to be forward-looking, to identify with changing attitudes among voters.","cn":"政党应该放眼未来并与选民态度变化保持一致的需要"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forward_looking_1_gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forward_looking_1_us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a forward-looking Russian statesman","cn":"一位有远见的俄罗斯政治家"}]},"folk":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/folk__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/folk__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"people in general","cn":"人们","g":"[plural]","lab":"especially in North American English","ex":{"en":"ordinary working-class folk","cn":"普通劳动大众"}},{"en":"a friendly way of addressing more than one person","cn":"各位；大伙儿","g":"[plural]","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"Well, folks, what are we going to do today?","cn":"喂，伙计们，我们今天要干什么？"}},{"en":"the members of your family, especially your parents","cn":"亲属；家属；（尤指）爹妈","g":"[plural]","lab":"informal, especially North American English，，","ex":{"en":"How are your folks?","cn":"你爸妈好吗？"}},{"en":"people from a particular country or region, or who have a particular way of life","cn":"（某国、某地区或某生活方式的）普通百姓","g":"[plural]","ex":{"en":"country folk","cn":"乡下人"}},{"en":"music in the traditional style of a country or community","cn":"民间音乐","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"a folk festival/concert","cn":"民间音乐节／音乐会"}},{"en":"traditional and typical of the ordinary people of a country or community","cn":"传统民间的；民俗的","ex":{"en":"We visited an exhibition of folk art.","cn":"我们参观了民间艺术展览。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"based on the beliefs of ordinary people","cn":"流传民间的；普通百姓的","ex":{"en":"folk wisdom","cn":"民间智慧"},"pos":"adjective"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"人们;大家","en":"You can refer to people as folk or folks .","ex":{"en":"Country folk can tell you that there are certain places which animals avoid","cn":"老乡会告诉你有些地方动物是不会去的。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"亲人;家人;(尤指)双亲","en":"You can refer to your close family, especially your mother and father, as your folks .","ex":{"en":"I've been avoiding my folks lately.","cn":"我近来一直在避开家人。"}},{"pos":"N-VOC 称呼名词","cn":"(与人交谈时的称呼)大伙儿，诸位","en":"You can use folks as a term of address when you are talking to several people.","ex":{"en":"'It's a question of money, folks,' I announced","cn":"“诸位，这是一个钱的问题，”我郑重其事地说。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(艺术或习俗)大众的，民俗的","en":"Folk art and customs are traditional or typical of a particular community or nation.","ex":{"en":"...South American folk art.","cn":"南美洲的民间艺术"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(音乐)大众的，民间的","en":"Folk music is music which is traditional or typical of a particular community or nation.","ex":{"en":"...Irish folk music.","cn":"爱尔兰民间音乐"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"大众的;普通百姓的","en":"Folk can be used to describe something that relates to the beliefs and opinions of ordinary people.","ex":{"en":"Jack was a folk hero in the Greenwich Village bars","cn":"在格林尼治村的酒吧里杰克是人们心目中的英雄。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I'd like a job working with old folk or kids.","cn":"我喜欢与老人或小孩打交道的工作。"},{"en":"Well, folks, what are we going to do today?","cn":"喂，伙计们，我们今天要干什么？"}]},"folder":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊldə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a cover made of stiff card or plastic for holding loose papers, etc.","cn":"文件夹","ex":{"en":"There were two new buff folders on my desk.","cn":"我桌上有两个崭新的浅褐色文件夹。"}},{"en":"(in some computer systems) a way of organizing and storing computer files","cn":"（某些计算机系统中的）文件夹"},{"en":"a printed sheet of paper or a few printed pages folded into a small book","cn":"文件夹","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"The full specification of this remarkable car can be found in the information folder.","cn":"这辆非凡汽车的完整规格可以在信息文件夹中找到。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"活页夹","en":"A folder is a thin piece of cardboard in which you can keep loose papers."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(计算机系统中的)文件夹","en":"A folder is a group of files that are stored together on a computer."}]},"media":{"img":["media/pic/stationery_supplies_comp.jpg","media/thumb/folder.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/folder__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/folder__us_1.mp3"}},"foolishly":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"showing a total lack of good sense or good judgment. Stupid sounds very strong and is often used when you are annoyed or strongly criticizing someone’s behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"doing or saying things that are not sensible or serious, and that may make you feel embarrassed later. Silly sounds much gentler than stupid","cn":""}]},"examples":[{"en":"I’ve never heard anything so foolish in all my life.","cn":"","src":"ld"},{"en":"It would be foolish to ignore his advice.","cn":"","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foolishly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foolishly__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfuːlɪʃli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a way that shows a lack of good sense or judgement","cn":"愚蠢的；傻的","ex":{"en":"We foolishly thought that everyone would speak English.","cn":"我们愚蠢地以为所有人都将说英语。"}}]}},"formally":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːməli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in a very correct way that is suitable for official or important occasions","cn":"适合正式场合的；正规的；庄重的","ex":{"en":"‘How do you do?’ she said formally.","cn":"“你好！”她很正式地说。"}},{"en":"officially; in a way that follows an agreed or official way of doing things","cn":"正式的；合乎规矩的","ex":{"en":"The accounts were formally approved by the board.","cn":"账目已由董事会正式批准。"}},{"en":"through lessons, exams, etc. received in a school, college or university rather than just through practical experience","cn":"正规的","ex":{"en":"Although not formally trained as an art historian, he is widely respected for his knowledge of the period.","cn":"虽然他不是科班出身的艺术史学家，但因对这一时期的通晓而受到广泛尊重。"}},{"en":"in the way that something appears or is presented","cn":"正式地：以某种形式出现或呈现的方式","ex":{"en":"Formally, the distinction between town and country workers was clear, but in practice there was some overlap.","cn":"形式上，城镇工人和乡村工人之间的区别是明确的，但实际上存在一些重叠。"}},{"en":"in a regular manner, according to a clear, exact plan","cn":"整齐的；布置井然的","ex":{"en":"The gardens were formally arranged.","cn":"花园被正式布置。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formally__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formally__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Although not formally trained as an art historian, he is widely respected for his knowledge of the period.","cn":"虽然他不是科班出身的艺术史学家，但他对这一时期的知识却普遍为人尊重。"},{"en":"The accounts were formally approved by the board.","cn":"账目已由董事会正式批准。"}]},"forested":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forested__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forested__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrɪstɪd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"covered in forest","cn":"满是森林的；林木覆盖的","ex":{"en":"thickly forested hills","cn":"森林密布的丘陵"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"遍地树木的;森林覆盖的","en":"A forested area is an area covered in trees growing closely together.","ex":{"en":"The road snaked through forested mountains, past the village of San Antonio.","cn":"这条路在林木覆盖的山上蜿蜒前行，经过圣安东尼奥村。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The province is heavily forested and sparsely populated.","cn":"该省森林茂密，人烟稀少。"},{"en":"thickly forested hills","cn":"森林密布的丘陵"}]},"foundation":{"media":{"img":["media/pic/makeup_comp.jpg","media/thumb/foundation.jpg"],"uk":"media/uk/foundation__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foundation__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"faʊnˈdeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a principle, an idea or a fact that something is based on and that it grows from","cn":"基本原理；根据；基础","g":"[countable, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Respect and friendship provide a solid foundation for marriage.","cn":"尊重和友爱是婚姻的牢固基础。"}},{"en":"an organization that is established to provide money for a particular purpose, for example for scientific research or charity","cn":"基金会","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The money will go to the San Francisco AIDS Foundation.","cn":"这笔钱将交给旧金山艾滋病基金会。"}},{"en":"the act of starting a new institution or organization","cn":"（机构或组织的）创建，创办","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The organization has grown enormously since its foundation in 1955.","cn":"该组织自 1955 年创建以来已有重大的发展。"}},{"en":"a layer of stone, concrete, etc. that forms the solid underground base of a building","cn":"地基；房基；基础","g":"[countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"The builders are now beginning to lay the foundations of the new school.","cn":"建筑工人正开始给新校舍打地基。"}},{"en":"a skin-coloured cream that is put on the face under other make-up","cn":"（化妆打底用的）粉底霜","g":"[uncountable]"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"基础;根基","en":"The foundation of something such as a belief or way of life is the things on which it is based.","ex":{"en":"Best friends are the foundation of my life","cn":"好朋友是我生命的支柱。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"地基;房基","en":"The foundations of a building or other structure are the layer of bricks or concrete below the ground that it is built on."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"基金会","en":"A foundation is an organization which provides money for a special purpose such as research or charity.","ex":{"en":"...the National Foundation for Educational Research.","cn":"全国教育研究基金会"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"依据;根据","en":"If a story, idea, or argument has no foundation, there are no facts to prove that it is true.","ex":{"en":"The allegations were without foundation","cn":"这些指控没有根据。"}},{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"粉底霜","en":"Foundation is a skin-coloured cream that you put on your face before putting on the rest of your make-up."}]},"examples":[{"en":"The organization has grown enormously since its foundation in 1955.","cn":"该组织自 1955 年创建以来已有重大的发展。"},{"en":"This issue has shaken the foundations of French politics.","cn":"这个问题从根本上动摇了法国的政治。"}]},"formerly":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formerly__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formerly__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːməli","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"in the past","cn":"以前；从前","ex":{"en":"Namibia, formerly known as South West Africa","cn":"纳米比亚，旧称西南非洲"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"从前;原来;以前","en":"If something happened or was true formerly, it happened or was true in the past.","ex":{"en":"He had formerly been in the Navy.","cn":"他从前在海军服役。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"John Marsh, formerly of London Road, Leicester, now living in France","cn":"约翰 · 马什，以前家在莱斯特市伦敦路，现居住在法国"},{"en":"I learnt that the house had formerly been an inn.","cn":"我得知这座房子以前是家客栈。"}]},"fortunes":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtʃuːn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"chance or luck, especially in the way it affects people's lives （","cn":"尤指影响人生的）机会，运气"},{"en":"a large amount of money","cn":"大笔的钱；巨款"}]}},"force":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/force__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/force__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"violent physical action used to obtain or achieve something","cn":"武力；暴力","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"violent action","ex":{"en":"The release of the hostages could not be achieved without the use of force.","cn":"不使用武力不可能使人质获释。"}},{"en":"physical strength, especially as shown when something hits something else","cn":"力；力量","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"physical strength","ex":{"en":"the force of the explosion/impact","cn":"爆炸力；冲击力"}},{"en":"the strong effect or influence of something","cn":"强大效力；巨大影响","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"strong effect","ex":{"en":"They realized the force of her argument.","cn":"他们领悟到了她那论据的威力。"}},{"en":"a person or thing that has a lot of power or influence","cn":"力量大的人（或事物）；影响大的人（或事物）","g":"[countable]","sc":"somebody/something with power","ex":{"en":"the forces of good/evil","cn":"善／恶的力量"}},{"en":"the authority of something","cn":"权力；效力","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"authority","ex":{"en":"The court ruled that these standards have force in English law.","cn":"法院裁定，这些标准在英格兰法律中有效。"}},{"en":"a group of people who have been organized for a particular purpose","cn":"（为某目的组织起来的）一群人","g":"[countable + singular or plural verb]","sc":"group of people","ex":{"en":"a member of the sales force","cn":"销售团队中的一员"}},{"en":"a trained and organized group of police, soldiers or other military personnel","cn":"（警察、军队等）武装力量","g":"[countable + singular or plural verb]","sc":"military","ex":{"en":"Rebel forces now control most of the capital.","cn":"叛军现在已控制首都的大部份地区。"}},{"en":"the army, navy and air force","cn":"兵力，武装力量（陆海空三军）","g":"[plural]","lab":"British English","sc":"military","ex":{"en":"life in the forces","cn":"部队生活"}},{"en":"the weapons and soldiers that an army, etc. has, considered as things that may be used","cn":"武装力量","g":"[plural]","sc":"military","ex":{"en":"strategic nuclear forces.","cn":"战略核部队"}},{"en":"the police force","cn":"警察部门","g":"[singular]","sc":"police","ex":{"en":"He joined the force twenty years ago.","cn":"他二十年前加入了警队。"}},{"en":"an effect that causes things to move in a particular way","cn":"力","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"physics","ex":{"en":"The moon exerts a force on the earth.","cn":"月球对地球有引力。"}},{"en":"a unit for measuring the strength of the wind on the Beaufort scale","cn":"蒲福风级","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"of wind","ex":{"en":"a force 9 gale","cn":"9 级大风"}},{"en":"to make somebody do something that they do not want to do","cn":"强迫，迫使（某人做某事）","g":"[often passive]","lab":"informal, humorous，，","sc":"make somebody do something","ex":{"en":"The President was forced into resigning.","cn":"总统被迫辞职。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to use physical strength to move somebody/something into a particular position","cn":"用力，强行（把…移动）","sc":"use physical strength","ex":{"en":"to force a lock/window/door (= to break it open using force)","cn":"强行打开锁／窗／门"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make something happen, especially before other people are ready","cn":"使发生（尤指趁他人尚未准备好）","sc":"make something happen","ex":{"en":"He was in a position where he had to force a decision.","cn":"他当时的处境是，不得不强行通过一项决定。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make yourself smile, laugh, etc. rather than doing it naturally","cn":"强作笑颜；强装欢笑","sc":"a smile/laugh","ex":{"en":"She managed to force a smile.","cn":"她勉强笑笑。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make fruit, plants, etc. grow or develop faster than normal by keeping them in special conditions","cn":"人工催长；加速（水果、植物等）生长；催熟","lab":"figurative","sc":"fruit/plants","ex":{"en":"forced rhubarb","cn":"人工催长的大黄"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"强迫;强制","en":"If someone forces you to do something, they make you do it even though you do not want to, for example by threatening you.","ex":{"en":"He was charged with abducting a taxi driver and forcing him to drive a bomb to Downing Street","cn":"他被控劫持一名出租车司机并强迫他开车把一颗炸弹送到唐宁街。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"迫使;使必须","en":"If a situation or event forces you to do something, it makes it necessary for you to do something that you would not otherwise have done.","ex":{"en":"A back injury forced her to withdraw from Wimbledon","cn":"背部受伤使她不得不退出温布尔登赛事。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"把…强加给","en":"If someone forces something on or upon you, they make you accept or use it when you would prefer not to.","ex":{"en":"To force this agreement on the nation is wrong.","cn":"把这份协定强加给这个国家是错误的。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"用力使…移动","en":"If you force something into a particular position, you use a lot of strength to make it move there.","ex":{"en":"They were forcing her head under the icy waters, drowning her.","cn":"他们用力把她的头按到冰冷的水中，想淹死她。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"强行打开(锁、门等)","en":"If someone forces a lock, a door, or a window, they break the lock or fastening in order to get into a building without using a key.","ex":{"en":"That evening police forced the door of the flat and arrested Mr Roberts","cn":"那一晚，警察强行打开公寓大门，逮捕了罗伯茨先生。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"暴力;武力","en":"If someone uses force to do something, or if it is done by force, strong and violent physical action is taken in order to achieve it.","ex":{"en":"The government decided against using force to break-up the demonstrations.","cn":"政府决定不使用暴力驱散示威人群。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"力量;力气;威力","en":"Force is the power or strength which something has.","ex":{"en":"The force of the explosion shattered the windows of several buildings","cn":"爆炸的冲力震碎了几栋楼房的玻璃窗。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"力量;影响力","en":"If you refer to someone or something as a force in a particular type of activity, you mean that they have a strong influence on it.","ex":{"en":"For years the army was the most powerful political force in the country","cn":"多年来，军队一直是这个国家最强大的政治力量。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"影响力;威力;势力","en":"The force of something is the powerful effect or quality that it has.","ex":{"en":"He changed our world through the force of his ideas","cn":"他通过自己观念的力量改变了我们的世界。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"自然力;非人力","en":"You can use forces to refer to processes and events that do not appear to be caused by human beings, and are therefore difficult to understand or control.","ex":{"en":"...the protection of mankind against the forces of nature: epidemics, predators, floods, hurricanes","cn":"保护人类抵御自然力——传染病、食肉动物、洪水和飓风"}},{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(物理学上的)力","en":"In physics, a force is the pulling or pushing effect that something has on something else.","ex":{"en":"...the earth's gravitational force.","cn":"地球的重力"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(置于数字前表示风力的)级数","en":"Force is used before a number to indicate a wind of a particular speed or strength, especially a very strong wind.","ex":{"en":"The airlift was conducted in force ten winds","cn":"空运在 10 级大风中进行。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"勉强做出(微笑等)","en":"If you force a smile or a laugh, you manage to smile or laugh, but with an effort because you are unhappy.","ex":{"en":"Joe forced a smile, but underneath he was a little disturbed","cn":"乔强颜欢笑，但内心里感到有些不安。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"军事力量;兵力","en":"Forces are groups of soldiers or military vehicles that are organized for a particular purpose.","ex":{"en":"...the deployment of American forces in the region.","cn":"美国武装力量在这一地区的部署"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"军队(指陆海空三军之一或三军)","en":"The forces means the army, the navy, or the air force, or all three.","ex":{"en":"The more senior you become in the forces, the more likely you are to end up in a desk job.","cn":"在部队里级别越高，最后就越有可能去做文职工作。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"警察机关;警察部门","en":"The force is sometimes used to mean the police force.","ex":{"en":"It was hard for a police officer to make friends outside the force.","cn":"警官很难与警队外面的人交朋友。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"由于;迫于;通过…手段","en":"If something happens by force of a particular quality, action, or set of circumstances, it happens because of the nature or intensity of that quality, action, or set of circumstances.","ex":{"en":"...converting the sceptics by force of argument.","cn":"通过辩论说服提出质疑者"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"习惯使然;出于习惯","en":"If you do something from force of habit, you do it because you have always done it in the past, rather than because you have thought carefully about it.","ex":{"en":"He looked around from force of habit, but nobody paid any attention to him","cn":"他出于习惯环顾四周，但是没人注意他。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(法律、规定或体系)在实施，生效","en":"A law, rule, or system that is in force exists or is being used.","ex":{"en":"Although the new tax is already in force, you have until November to lodge an appeal.","cn":"尽管新的税法已经生效，你需要等到 12 月才能提出上诉。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"大规模地;大量","en":"When people do something in force, they do it in large numbers.","ex":{"en":"Voters turned out in force for their first taste of multi-party elections.","cn":"大批选民前来参加他们的第一次多党选举。"}},{"pos":"PHR-RECIP 相互短语","cn":"联合;联手;合力","en":"If you join forces with someone, you work together in order to achieve a common aim or purpose.","ex":{"en":"Both groups joined forces to persuade voters to approve a tax break for the industry","cn":"两个团体联合游说投票者赞成给予这个行业税收优惠。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"挤进;闯出;强行通过","en":"If you force your way through or into somewhere, you have to push or break things that are in your way in order to get there.","ex":{"en":"The miners were armed with clubs as they forced their way through a police cordon","cn":"矿工们手持棍棒冲过了警戒线。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to force someone's hand→see: ;"},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"强忍,忍住(情感或欲望)","en":"If you force back an emotion or desire, you manage, with an effort, not to experience it.","ex":{"en":"Nancy forced back tears. She wasn't going to cry in front of all those people.","cn":"南希强忍泪水。她不会在那些人面前哭的。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：force back"}]},"examples":[{"en":"to force your attentions/opinions/company on sb","cn":"强行对（某人）献殷勤；把意见强加给（某人）；硬要陪伴（某人）"},{"en":"I was forced to take a taxi because the last bus had left.","cn":"最后一班公共汽车已经开走，所以我只好叫了一辆出租汽车。"}]},"foreground":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foreground__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foreground__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːɡraʊnd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the part of a view, picture, etc. that is nearest to you when you look at it","cn":"（景物、图画等的）前景","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"The figure in the foreground is the artist's mother.","cn":"图画前景中的人是画家的母亲。"}},{"en":"an important position that is noticed by people","cn":"瞩目地位；重要位置","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"Inflation and interest rates will be very much in the foreground of their election campaign.","cn":"通货膨胀和利率将很可能是他们竞选的重点问题。"}},{"en":"used to refer to tasks or processes that the user is actively working on at the present time","cn":"前台（指界面中显示正在运行的程序）","g":"[singular]","lab":"computing","ex":{"en":"Normally, the user runs the program in the foreground.","cn":"通常，用户在前台运行程序。"}},{"en":"to give particular importance to something","cn":"强调；突出","ex":{"en":"The play foregrounds the relationship between father and daughter.","cn":"这部戏剧凸显了父女之间的关系。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(照片、景物等的)前景","en":"The foreground of a picture or scene you are looking at is the part or area of it that appears nearest to you.","ex":{"en":"He is the bowler-hatted figure in the foreground of Orpen's famous painting.","cn":"他是奥彭那幅名画中位于前景的戴圆顶硬礼帽的那个人物。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"受到关注;引人注目","en":"If something or someone is in the foreground, or comes to the foreground, they receive a lot of attention.","ex":{"en":"This is another worry that has come to the foreground in recent years.","cn":"这是近年来开始备受关注的另一个令人忧虑的问题。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"强调;使突出","en":"To foreground certain features of a situation means to make them the most important part of a description or account.","ex":{"en":"His book foregrounds three events in which police relations with the media were central.","cn":"他的书重点讲了 3 个事件，以警察和媒体的关系为中心展开。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Inflation and interest rates will be very much in the foreground of their election campaign.","cn":"通货膨胀和利率将很可能是他们竞选的重点问题。"},{"en":"The play foregrounds the relationship between father and daughter.","cn":"这部戏剧凸显了父女之间的关系。"}]},"forestall":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forestall__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forestall__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈstɔːl","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to prevent something from happening or somebody from doing something by doing something first","cn":"防止；在（他人）之前行动；先发制人","ex":{"en":"Try to anticipate what your child will do and forestall problems.","cn":"尽量预见你的孩子会干什么，并预先阻止问题发生。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"预先阻止;抢在…之前行动","en":"If you forestall someone, you realize what they are likely to do and prevent them from doing it.","ex":{"en":"O'Leary made to open the door, but Bunbury forestalled him by laying a hand on his arm","cn":"奥利里想去开门，但是邦伯里抢先一把摁住了他的胳膊。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Try to anticipate what your child will do and forestall problems.","cn":"尽量预见你的孩子会干什么，并预先阻止问题发生。"},{"en":"a measure intended to forestall further attacks","cn":"意在预先阻止进一步攻击的措施"}]},"fold":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fold__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fold__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊld","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to bend something, especially paper or cloth, so that one part lies on top of another part","cn":"折叠，对折（纸、织物等）","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"First, fold the paper in half/in two.","cn":"首先，把纸对折起来。"}},{"en":"to bend something so that it becomes smaller or flatter and can be stored or carried more easily; to bend or be able to bend in this way","cn":"折小，叠平，可折小，可叠平（以便贮存或携带）","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","lab":"figurative","ex":{"en":"The bed can be folded away during the day.","cn":"这张床在白天可以折叠收起。"}},{"en":"to wrap something around somebody/something","cn":"包；裹","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"She gently folded the baby in a blanket.","cn":"她轻轻地把婴儿裹在毯子里。"}},{"en":"to close because it is not successful","cn":"倒闭；停演；结束","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The new musical folded after only twenty performances.","cn":"这部新音乐剧只演出了二十场就宣告失败。"}},{"en":"multiplied by; having the number of parts mentioned","cn":"乘以；…倍；由…部分组成","ex":{"en":"to increase tenfold","cn":"增加到十倍"},"pos":"suffix"},{"en":"a part of something, especially cloth, that is folded or hangs as if it had been folded","cn":"褶；褶层；折叠部分","g":"[countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"the folds of her dress","cn":"她的连衣裙上的褶"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a mark or line made by folding something, or showing where something should be folded","cn":"褶痕；褶缝；褶线","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Why is the place I want to find always on the fold of the map?","cn":"为什么我想找的地方总是在地图的褶缝上？"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"an area in a field surrounded by a fence or wall where animals, especially sheep, are kept for safety","cn":"畜棚；羊栏；羊圈","g":"[countable]","pos":"noun"},{"en":"a group of people who share the same ideas or beliefs","cn":"志趣相同的人们；同一信仰的人们","g":"[singular]","ex":{"en":"He called on former Republican voters to return to the fold.","cn":"他号召昔日拥护共和党的选民重新回到支持共和党的行列。"},"pos":"noun"},{"en":"a curve or bend in the line of the layers of rock in the earth’s crust","cn":"（地壳岩石层的）褶皱","g":"[countable]","lab":"geology","pos":"noun"},{"en":"a hollow place among hills or mountains","cn":"山坳；山洼；山谷","g":"[countable]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"It was a solitary spot in a fold between two hills.","cn":"这是个人迹罕至的地方，隐藏在两座山之间的山坳里。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"折叠;折起;叠起","en":"If you fold something such as a piece of paper or cloth, you bend it so that one part covers another part, often pressing the edge so that it stays in place.","ex":{"en":"He folded the paper carefully","cn":"他把纸小心地折起来。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"褶缝;褶痕;折叠线","en":"A fold in a piece of paper or cloth is a bend that you make in it when you put one part of it over another part and press the edge.","ex":{"en":"Make another fold and turn the ends together.","cn":"再折一下，把末端对齐。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(布料的)褶皱，褶痕","en":"The folds in a piece of cloth are the curved shapes which are formed when it is not hanging or lying flat.","ex":{"en":"The priest fumbled in the folds of his gown.","cn":"牧师胡乱整了整长袍上的褶皱。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"折叠;折起","en":"If a piece of furniture or equipment folds or if you can fold it, you can make it smaller by bending or closing parts of it.","ex":{"en":"The back of the bench folds forward to make a table","cn":"长凳的靠背可以向前翻折成一张桌子。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"交叉，交叠(双手或双臂)","en":"If you fold your arms or hands, you bring them together and cross or link them, for example over your chest.","ex":{"en":"Meer folded his arms over his chest and turned his head away","cn":"米尔双臂交叉在胸前，把头转到一边。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(企业或组织)停业，关门","en":"If a business or organization folds, it is unsuccessful and has to close.","ex":{"en":"But as other shops fold, the march of the superstores continues","cn":"但在其他商店纷纷关门倒闭之时，大型超市的强劲扩张势头却依旧不减。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"队伍;同一群体的人","en":"When someone joins an organization or group, you can say that they have come into the fold. When they leave the organization or group, you can say that they leave the fold .","ex":{"en":"The EU wanted to bring the US back into the fold","cn":"欧盟想要让美国重新回到他们的阵营之中。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"(烹饪时将调料)调入，加入","en":"In cooking, if you fold in an ingredient or fold it into the other ingredients, you mix it very gently into the other ingredients.","ex":{"en":"Fold in the flour","cn":"拌入面粉。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"把…折叠起来","en":"If you fold something up, you make it into a smaller, neater shape by folding it, usually several times.","ex":{"en":"She folded it up, and tucked it into her purse","cn":"她将其折叠起来，塞进了钱包里。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：fold in fold up"}]},"examples":[{"en":"He called on former Republican voters to return to the fold.","cn":"他号召昔日拥护共和党的选民重新回到支持共和党的行列。"},{"en":"( figurative ) When she heard the news, her legs just folded under her (= she fell).","cn":"她听到这消息时双腿发软（倒在地上）。"}]},"follow-up":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊ ʌp","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"continuing something that has already started; coming after something similar that was done earlier","cn":"后续行动；后续事物","ex":{"en":"follow-up treatment at the local hospital","cn":"当地医院后续治疗"}},{"en":"an action or a thing that continues something that has already started or comes after something similar that was done earlier","cn":"后续行动；后续事物","ex":{"en":"The book is a follow-up to her excellent television series.","cn":"这本书是继她的优秀电视系列片之后的又一力作。"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"继续;后续","en":"A follow-up is something that is done to continue or add to something done previously.","ex":{"en":"They are recording a follow-up to their successful 1989 album","cn":"他们正在灌录他们 1989 年畅销专辑的续篇。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/follow_up_1_gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/follow_up_1_us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The book is a follow-up to her excellent television series.","cn":"这本书是继她的优秀电视系列片之后的又一力作。"},{"en":"a follow-up study","cn":"进一步的研究"}]},"found":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/found__gb_2.mp3","us":"media/us/found__us_2.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"faʊnd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to start something, such as an organization or an institution, especially by providing money","cn":"创建，创办（组织或机构，尤指提供资金）","ex":{"en":"to found a club/company/school","cn":"创办俱乐部／公司／学校"}},{"en":"to be the first to start building and living in a town or country","cn":"建立，兴建（城镇或国家）","ex":{"en":"The town was founded by English settlers in 1790.","cn":"这座城镇是英格兰移民于 1790 年建立的。"}},{"en":"to base something on something","cn":"把…基于；把…建立在","g":"[usually passive]","ex":{"en":"Their marriage was founded on love and mutual respect.","cn":"他们的婚姻建立在爱情和互相尊重的基础上。"}},{"en":"to melt metal and pour it into a mould; to make objects using this process","cn":"熔铸；铸造","lab":"specialist"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Found is the past tense and past participle of find ."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"建立;成立;创立","en":"When an institution, company, or organization is founded by someone or by a group of people, they get it started, often by providing the necessary money.","ex":{"en":"The Independent Labour Party was founded in Bradford on January 13, 1893","cn":"独立工党1893年1月13日在布拉德福德成立。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"建成;兴建","en":"When a town, important building, or other place is founded by someone or by a group of people, they cause it to be built.","ex":{"en":"The town was founded in 1610.","cn":"这个镇建于 1610 年。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The town was founded by English settlers in 1790.","cn":"这座城镇是英格兰移民于 1790 年建立的。"},{"en":"Her family founded the college in 1895.","cn":"她的家族于 1895 年创办了这所学院。"}]},"food":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/food__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/food__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fuːd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"things that people or animals eat","cn":"食物","ex":{"en":"Pat had prepared food and drink for the work party.","cn":"帕特已经为工作聚会准备了食物和饮料。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-MASS 物质名词","cn":"食物;食品","en":"Food is what people and animals eat.","ex":{"en":"Enjoy your food.","cn":"用餐愉快。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(常指因生病)不想吃东西，厌食","en":"If you are off your food, you do not want to eat, usually because you are ill.","ex":{"en":"It's not like you to be off your food.","cn":"胃口不好，这可不像你了。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"引人深思;发人深省","en":"If you give someone food for thought, you make them think carefully about something.","ex":{"en":"Lord Fraser's speech offers much food for thought","cn":"弗雷泽勋爵的讲演发人深省。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Do you like Italian food?","cn":"你喜欢意大利食物吗？"},{"en":"He's off his food (= he does not want to eat anything).","cn":"他不想吃东西。"}]},"forage":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forage__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forage__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrɪdʒ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to search widely for food","cn":"四处觅食","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The female only leaves the young when she forages for food.","cn":"雌性只有在觅食时才会离开幼崽。"}},{"en":"to search for something, especially using the hands","cn":"（尤指用手）搜寻（东西）","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Her assistant was foraging in a cupboard for some envelopes.","cn":"她的助手正在橱柜里找信封。"}},{"en":"food for horses and cows","cn":"（牛马的）饲料","ex":{"en":"forage crops/grass","cn":"饲料作物；饲草"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"搜查;搜寻","en":"If someone forages for something, they search for it in a busy way.","ex":{"en":"They were forced to forage for clothing and fuel.","cn":"他们不得不去寻找衣服和燃料。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(动物)觅食","en":"When animals forage, they search for food.","ex":{"en":"We disturbed a wild boar that had been foraging by the roadside","cn":"我们惊动了一只一直在路边觅食的野猪。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"饲料;草料","en":"Forage is crops that are grown as food for cattle and horses.","ex":{"en":"...the amount of forage needed to feed one cow and its calf.","cn":"喂养一头母牛和小牛犊所需要的饲料"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"forage crops/grass","cn":"饲料作物；饲草"},{"en":"People are being forced to forage for food and fuel.","cn":"人们只得四处寻找食物和燃料。"}]},"fond":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fond__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fond__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɒnd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having warm or loving feelings for somebody, especially somebody you have known for a long time","cn":"喜爱（尤指认识已久的人）","ex":{"en":"Over the years, I have grown quite fond of her.","cn":"经过这么多年，我已相当喜欢她了。"}},{"en":"finding something pleasant, especially something you have liked or enjoyed for a long time","cn":"喜爱（尤指长期喜爱的事物）","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"fond of music/cooking","cn":"喜好音乐／烹饪"}},{"en":"liking to do something that other people find annoying or unpleasant, and doing it often","cn":"喜欢（做令人不快的事）","ex":{"en":"Sheila's very fond of telling other people what to do.","cn":"希拉爱对别人指手画脚。"}},{"en":"kind and loving","cn":"深情的；温情的；慈爱的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"a fond look/embrace/farewell","cn":"慈爱的目光；温情的拥抱；深情的告别"}},{"en":"a hope about something that is not likely to happen","cn":"（指希望）难以实现的；痴想的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"I waited all day in the fond hope that she would change her mind.","cn":"我整天等待，痴心地希望她会回心转意。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"喜欢;喜爱","en":"If you are fond of someone, you feel affection for them.","ex":{"en":"I am very fond of Michael","cn":"我很喜欢迈克尔。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"深情的;温情的","en":"You use fond to describe people or their behaviour when they show affection.","ex":{"en":"...a fond father","cn":"慈父"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"喜欢…的;爱做…的","en":"If you are fond of something, you like it or you like doing it very much.","ex":{"en":"He was fond of marmalade","cn":"他爱吃橘子酱。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(回忆)愉快的,愉悦的","en":"If you have fond memories of someone or something, you remember them with pleasure.","ex":{"en":"I have very fond memories of living in our village.","cn":"我对乡村生活有着十分美好的回忆。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(期望、愿望、信仰等)愚蠢的，不切实际的","en":"You use fond to describe hopes, wishes, or beliefs which you think are foolish because they seem unlikely to be fulfilled.","ex":{"en":"My fond hope is that we will be ready by Christmastime.","cn":"我痴想着希望我们可以在圣诞假期前准备就绪。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"We had grown fond of the house and didn't want to leave.","cn":"我们已经喜欢上了这座房子，不想搬家。"},{"en":"I waited all day in the fond hope that she would change her mind.","cn":"我整天等待，痴迷地希望她会回心转意。"}]},"forgave":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Forgave is the past tense of forgive ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgave__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgave__us_1.mp3"}},"forced":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forced__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forced__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːst","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"happening or done against somebody’s will","cn":"被迫的；不得已的","ex":{"en":"victims of forced marriage","cn":"强迫婚姻的受害者"}},{"en":"not sincere; not the result of real emotions","cn":"勉强的；不真诚的","ex":{"en":"She said she was enjoying herself but her smile was forced.","cn":"她说自己很快活，但是她的笑容很勉强。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"被迫的;强迫的;非自愿的","en":"A forced action is something that you do because someone else makes you do it.","ex":{"en":"A system of forced labour was used on the cocoa plantations.","cn":"可可种植园中曾实行强迫劳役制。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"不得已的;不得不做的","en":"A forced action is something that you do because circumstances make it necessary.","ex":{"en":"He made a forced landing on a highway.","cn":"他迫降在了公路上。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"不自然的;勉强的","en":"If you describe something as forced, you mean it does not happen naturally and easily.","ex":{"en":"...a forced smile","cn":"强挤出来的微笑"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She said she was enjoying herself but her smile was forced.","cn":"她说自己很快活，但是她的笑容很勉强。"},{"en":"forced relocation to a job in another city","cn":"不得已迁移至另一城市工作"}]},"folds":{"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊld","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to bend sth, especially paper or cloth, so that one part lies on top of another part","cn":"折叠，对折（纸、织物等）"},{"en":"to bend sth so that it becomes smaller or flatter and can be stored or carried more easily; to bend or be able to bend in this way","cn":"折小，叠平，可折小，可叠平（以便贮存或携带）"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fold__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fold__us_1.mp3"}},"focused":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/focused__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/focused__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊkəst","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"with your attention directed to what you want to do; with very clear aims","cn":"注意力集中的；目标明确的","ex":{"en":"focused ambitions","cn":"集中的野心"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有明确目标的;注意力集中的","en":"If you describe someone or something as focused, you approve of the fact that they have a clear and definite purpose.","ex":{"en":"I spent the next year just wandering. I wasn't focused","cn":"接下来的一年我一直在闲逛。没有什么明确的目标。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"She should do well in her studies this year — she's very focused.","cn":"今年她的功课应该学得好，她的注意力很集中。"}]},"founder":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/founder__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/founder__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfaʊndə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who starts an organization, institution, etc. or causes something to be built","cn":"（组织、机构等的）创建者，创办者，发起人","ex":{"en":"the founder and president of the company","cn":"公司的创办人和总裁"}},{"en":"to fail, especially because of a particular problem or difficulty","cn":"失败；破产","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The project foundered after problems with funding.","cn":"这个项目因资金不足而告吹。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to fill with water and sink","cn":"沉没","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Our boat foundered on a reef.","cn":"我们的船触礁沉没。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"创办人;创立者;奠基者","en":"The founder of an institution, organization, or building is the person who got it started or caused it to be built, often by providing the necessary money.","ex":{"en":"He was one of the founders of the university's medical faculty.","cn":"他是该大学医学院的创建人之一。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"失败;崩溃;垮掉","en":"If something such as a plan or project founders, it fails because of a particular point, difficulty, or problem.","ex":{"en":"The talks have foundered, largely because of the reluctance of some members of the government to do a deal with criminals.","cn":"对话已经破裂了，原因主要是因为一些政府成员不愿意和犯罪分子达成协议。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(船只)沉没","en":"If a ship founders, it fills with water and sinks.","ex":{"en":"Three ships foundered in heavy seas.","cn":"三艘船在波涛汹涌的海面上沉没了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The peace talks foundered on a basic lack of trust.","cn":"由于缺乏基本信任，和平谈判搁浅。"},{"en":"the founder and president of the company","cn":"公司的创办人和总裁"}]},"form":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/form__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/form__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type or variety of something","cn":"类型；种类","g":"[countable]","sc":"type","ex":{"en":"all the millions of different life forms on the planet today","cn":"当今地球上所有的几百万生命种类"}},{"en":"a way of writing or saying a word that shows, for example, if it is plural or in a particular tense","cn":"词形；形式","g":"[countable]","sc":"of word","ex":{"en":"the infinitive form of the verb","cn":"动词不定式"}},{"en":"the particular way something is, seems, looks or is presented","cn":"形式；外表；样子","g":"[countable, uncountable]","sc":"way something is/looks","ex":{"en":"The disease can take several different forms.","cn":"这种疾病可能有几种不同的形式。"}},{"en":"an official document containing questions and spaces for answers","cn":"表格","g":"[countable]","lab":"especially British English","sc":"document","ex":{"en":"an application/entry/order form","cn":"申请表；报名表；订货单"}},{"en":"the shape of somebody/something; a person or thing of which only the shape can be seen","cn":"形状；体形","g":"[countable]","sc":"shape","ex":{"en":"The human form has changed little over the last 30 000 years.","cn":"3 万多年以来，人的体形没有多大变化。"}},{"en":"the arrangement of parts in a whole, especially in a work of art or piece of writing","cn":"（尤指艺术作品或文章的）结构，形式","g":"[uncountable]","sc":"arrangement of parts","ex":{"en":"Shape and form are of greater importance to me than colour.","cn":"对我来说，形状和形式比颜色更重要。"}},{"en":"how fit and healthy somebody is; the state of being fit and healthy","cn":"体能；良好的健康状态","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English","sc":"being fit/healthy","ex":{"en":"After six months' training the whole team is in superb form.","cn":"经过半年的训练，全队状态极佳。"}},{"en":"how well somebody/something is performing; the fact that somebody/something is performing well","cn":"表现状态；良好表现","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English","sc":"performance","ex":{"en":"Midfielder Elliott has shown disappointing form recently.","cn":"中场队员埃利奥特近来表现令人失望。"}},{"en":"the usual way of doing something","cn":"惯常做法；常规；习俗","g":"[uncountable, countable]","lab":"especially British English","sc":"way of doing things","ex":{"en":"What's the form when you apply for a research grant?","cn":"申请科研补助金按常规应该怎么办？"}},{"en":"the way of doing things that is socially acceptable/not socially acceptable","cn":"礼貌；礼节","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"old-fashioned, British English，，","sc":"way of doing things","ex":{"en":"When I was a boy it was always considered bad form to talk about food or money.","cn":"当我还是个孩子的时候，谈论食物或金钱总是被认为是不礼貌的。"}},{"en":"a class in a school","cn":"年级","lab":"British English, old-fashioned，，","sc":"in school","ex":{"en":"Who's your form teacher?","cn":"你们的年级老师是谁？"}},{"en":"a student in the form mentioned at school","cn":"…年级学生","lab":"British English, old-fashioned，，","sc":"in school","ex":{"en":"a third-former","cn":"三年级学生"}},{"en":"to produce something in a particular way or make it have a particular shape","cn":"（使）成形，组成；制作","g":"[transitive]","sc":"make shape/form","ex":{"en":"Bend the wire so that it forms a ‘V’.","cn":"把铁丝弯成 V 形。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to move or arrange objects or people so that they are in a group with a particular shape; to become arranged in a group like this","cn":"（使）排列成，排成","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"make shape/form","ex":{"en":"First get students to form groups of four.","cn":"首先让学生分成四人一组。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to begin to exist and gradually develop into a particular shape; to make something begin to exist in a particular shape","cn":"（使）出现，产生","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"start to exist","ex":{"en":"Flowers appeared, but fruits failed to form.","cn":"开了花，但没有结果。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to start to exist and develop; to make something start to exist and develop","cn":"（使）形成","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"start to exist","ex":{"en":"A plan formed in my head.","cn":"一个计划在我的头脑中形成。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to start a group of people, such as an organization, a committee, etc.; to come together in a group of this kind","cn":"组织；建立","g":"[transitive, intransitive]","sc":"organization","ex":{"en":"They hope to form the new government.","cn":"他们希望组建新政府。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to be something; to have a particular function or pattern","cn":"构成；有…功能；有…模式","sc":"have function/role","ex":{"en":"The castle forms the focal point of the city.","cn":"这座城堡是城市的中心。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to have an influence on the way that something develops","cn":"对…的发展有影响","g":"[transitive]","sc":"have influence on","ex":{"en":"Positive and negative experiences form a child's character.","cn":"正反两方面的经历都影响儿童性格的形成。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"类型;类别;种类","en":"A form of something is a type or kind of it.","ex":{"en":"He contracted a rare form of cancer","cn":"他得了一种罕见的癌症。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(存在的)形态，形式","en":"When something can exist or happen in several possible ways, you can use form to refer to one particular way in which it exists or happens.","ex":{"en":"Valleys often take the form of deep canyons","cn":"山谷经常以深峡谷的形态存在。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"形成;(使)排列成;组成…形状","en":"When a particular shape forms or is formed, people or things move or are arranged so that this shape is made.","ex":{"en":"A queue forms outside Peter's study","cn":"彼得书房外面排起了队。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"形状;外形","en":"The form of something is its shape.","ex":{"en":"...the form of the body.","cn":"体形"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"轮廓;外形","en":"You can refer to something that you can see as a form if you cannot see it clearly, or if its outline is the clearest or most striking aspect of it.","ex":{"en":"She thought she'd never been so glad to see his bulky form.","cn":"她想她从来没有因看到他那肥胖的身躯而如此高兴。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"形成;变成","en":"If something is arranged or changed so that it becomes similar to a thing with a particular structure or function, you can say that it forms that thing.","ex":{"en":"These panels folded up to form a screen some five feet tall","cn":"这些嵌板折起来组成了一个约 5 英尺高的屏风。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"构成;是…的组成部分","en":"If something consists of particular things, people, or features, you can say that they form that thing.","ex":{"en":"...the articles that formed the basis of Randolph's book","cn":"构成伦道夫此书的基础的那些文章"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"组建;组成;建立","en":"If you form an organization, group, or company, you start it.","ex":{"en":"They tried to form a study group on human rights","cn":"他们试图组建一个人权问题研究小组。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"存在;(使)形成","en":"When something natural forms or is formed, it begins to exist and develop.","ex":{"en":"The stars must have formed 10 to 15 billion years ago","cn":"这些恒星一定是形成于 100 到 150 亿年前。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)(关系、习惯或想法)形成;(使)产生","en":"If you form a relationship, a habit, or an idea, or if it forms, it begins to exist and develop.","ex":{"en":"This should help him form lasting relationships","cn":"这应该能帮助他建立持久的关系。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"陶冶;培养;培育","en":"If you say that something forms a person's character or personality, you mean that it has a strong influence on them and causes them to develop in a particular way.","ex":{"en":"Anger at injustice formed his character.","cn":"对不公正现象的愤怒塑造了他的性格。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(运动员或参赛动物的)竞技状态,表现状态","en":"In sport, form refers to the ability or success of a person or animal over a period of time.","ex":{"en":"His form this season has been brilliant","cn":"他这一赛季状态非常不错。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"表格","en":"A form is a paper with questions on it and spaces marked where you should write the answers. Forms usually ask you to give details about yourself, for example when you are applying for a job or joining an organization.","ex":{"en":"You will be asked to fill in a form with details of your birth and occupation.","cn":"你将需要填写一张有关生日和职业详情的表格。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"讨厌的行为;不礼貌的行为","en":"If you say that it is bad form to behave in a particular way, you mean that it is rude and impolite.","ex":{"en":"It was thought bad form to discuss business on social occasions.","cn":"在社交场合讨论生意被认为是不礼貌的。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"身体健康;情况良好;心情愉悦","en":"If you say that someone is in good form, you mean that they seem healthy and cheerful."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"状态不好;表现失常","en":"If you say that someone is off form, you think they are not performing as well as they usually do."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"状态良好;表现出色;发挥正常","en":"If you say that someone is on form, you think that they are performing their usual activity very well.","ex":{"en":"Robert Redford is back on form in his new movie 'Sneakers'.","cn":"罗伯特·雷德福在新片《通天神偷》中恢复了表演水准。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"成形","en":"When something takes form, it develops or begins to be visible.","ex":{"en":"As plans took form in her mind, she realized the need for an accomplice","cn":"随着计划在脑海里逐渐成形，她意识到需要找一个帮手。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"一如既往;和平常一样","en":"If someone or something behaves true to form, they do what is expected and is typical of them.","ex":{"en":"Before the train had left the outskirts of London he behaved true to form and began a conversation","cn":"一如往常，列车还没驶出伦敦郊区，他就开始和别人聊起天来。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He's right on form (= performing well) as a crazy science teacher in his latest movie.","cn":"他在最近的一部电影中扮演疯狂的理科教师，表现出色。"},{"en":"I didn't see enough of the play to form an opinion about it.","cn":"我对这部戏剧了解得不够，说不出什么意见。"}]},"forethought":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forethought__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forethought__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːθɔːt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"careful thought to make sure that things are successful in the future","cn":"深谋远虑","ex":{"en":"Some forethought and preparation are necessary before you embark on the project.","cn":"你着手进行这个项目之前必须有所考虑，有所准备。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"事先的考虑;深谋远虑","en":"If you act with forethought, you think carefully before you act about what will be needed, or about what the consequences will be.","ex":{"en":"With a little forethought many accidents could be avoided.","cn":"如果事先稍微多想想，许多事故是可以避免的。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Some forethought and preparation are necessary before you embark on the project.","cn":"你着手进行这个项目之前必须有所考虑，有所准备。"},{"en":"No one had the forethought to bring a map.","cn":"谁也没有事先想到带一张地图。"}]},"focusing":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊkəs","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give attention, effort, etc. to one particular subject, situation or person rather than another","cn":"集中（注意力、精力等）于"},{"en":"to adapt or be adjusted so that things can be seen clearly; to adjust sth so that you can see things clearly （","cn":"使）调节焦距"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/focus__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/focus__us_1.mp3"}},"followings":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"next in time （","cn":"时间上）接着的"},{"en":"that is/are going to be mentioned next","cn":"下述的；下列的"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/following__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/following__us_1.mp3"}},"foolhardy":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foolhardy__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foolhardy__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfuːlhɑːdi","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"taking unnecessary risks","cn":"莽撞的；有勇无谋的","ex":{"en":"It would be foolhardy to sail in weather like this.","cn":"这种天气出航就是瞎冒险。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"有勇无谋的;蛮干的","en":"If you describe behaviour as foolhardy, you disapprove of it because it is extremely risky.","ex":{"en":"When he tested an early vaccine on himself, some described the act as foolhardy","cn":"当他在自己身上试验还处在初级阶段的疫苗时，有些人说他的行为是蛮干。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"It would be foolhardy to sail in weather like this.","cn":"这种天气出航就是瞎冒险。"},{"en":"a foolhardy attempt to capture more territory","cn":"想占领更多地盘的鲁莽行为"}]},"forgotten":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Forgotten is the past participle of forget ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgotten__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgotten__us_1.mp3"}},"formless":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formless__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formless__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmləs","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"without a clear or definite shape or structure","cn":"无明确形状的；无定形的；结构不清的","ex":{"en":"formless dreams","cn":"杂乱的梦"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"没有清楚结构的;无定形的","en":"Something that is formless does not have a clear or definite structure or shape.","ex":{"en":"A series of largely formless images rushed across the screen.","cn":"一连串相当混乱的影像在屏幕上闪过。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"formless dreams","cn":"杂乱的梦"},{"en":"To the listener, this music is incoherent and formless.","cn":"对于听众来说﹐这个曲子既不连贯又无章法。"}]},"fortunate":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fortunate__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fortunate__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtʃənət","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"having or bringing an advantage, an opportunity, a piece of good luck, etc.","cn":"幸运的；交好运的；吉利的","ex":{"en":"Remember those less fortunate than yourselves.","cn":"要记住那些不如你们幸运的人。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"幸运的;有幸的","en":"If you say that someone or something is fortunate, you mean that they are lucky.","ex":{"en":"He was extremely fortunate to survive","cn":"他能活下来真是万幸。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"I have been fortunate enough to visit many parts of the world as a lecturer.","cn":"我很有福气，去过世界许多地方作演讲。"},{"en":"Remember those less fortunate than yourselves.","cn":"要记住那些不如你们幸运的人。"}]},"foresee":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foresee__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foresee__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈsiː","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to think something is going to happen in the future; to know about something before it happens","cn":"预料；预见；预知","ex":{"en":"We do not foresee any problems.","cn":"我们预料不会出任何问题。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"预见;预知;预料","en":"If you foresee something, you expect and believe that it will happen.","ex":{"en":"He did not foresee any problems","cn":"他没有预见到任何问题。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"No one could have foreseen (that) things would turn out this way.","cn":"谁都没有预料到事情的结果会这样。"},{"en":"I just didn't foresee that happening.","cn":"我只是没预料到会发生那种事。"}]},"fosters":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒstə(r)","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to encourage sth to develop","cn":"促进；助长；培养；鼓励"},{"en":"( especially BrE ) to take another person's child into your home for a period of time, without becoming his or her legal parents","cn":"代养，抚育，照料（他人子女一段时间）"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foster__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foster__us_1.mp3"}},"footprint":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/footprint__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/footprint__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/footprint.jpg"]},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtprɪnt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a mark left on a surface by a person’s foot or shoe or by an animal’s foot","cn":"脚印；足迹","g":"[usually plural]","ex":{"en":"footprints in the sand","cn":"沙地足迹"}},{"en":"a measure of the amount of the earth’s resources used by a person or a population that lives in a particular way","cn":"生态足迹（测定个人或群体生活所消耗地球资源的指标）","ex":{"en":"These countries are so populous that they can have a very big footprint.","cn":"这些国家人口过多, 可能对环境造成巨大影响。"}},{"en":"the amount of space that something fills","cn":"（某物所占的）空间，面积","ex":{"en":"The warehouse system holds an extensive amount of product in a very small footprint because it was built five levels high.","cn":"由于仓库系统建有五层高，因此其占地面积非常小，可容纳大量产品。"}},{"en":"the area on the earth in which a signal from a communications satellite can be received","cn":"（通信卫星）覆盖区"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"足迹;脚印","en":"A footprint is a mark in the shape of a foot that a person or animal makes in or on a surface."}]},"examples":[{"en":"muddy footprints on the kitchen floor","cn":"厨房地板上的泥脚印"},{"en":"footprints in the sand","cn":"沙地足迹"}]},"formation":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈmeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the action of forming something; the process of being formed","cn":"组成；形成","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"the formation of a new government","cn":"组成新政府"}},{"en":"a thing that has been formed, especially in a particular place or in a particular way","cn":"组成物；形成物","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Massive rock formations rise abruptly some 1 500 feet above the canyon floor.","cn":"巨大的岩层突然升起，高出峡谷底部约 1 500 英尺。"}},{"en":"a particular arrangement or pattern","cn":"编队；队形","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"formation flying","cn":"编队飞行"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"创建;设立;创造","en":"The formation of something is the starting or creation of it.","ex":{"en":"...the formation of a new government.","cn":"新政府的组建"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"形成;养成;建立","en":"The formation of an idea, habit, relationship, or character is the process of developing and establishing it.","ex":{"en":"My profession had an important influence in the formation of my character and temperament.","cn":"我的职业对我性格和脾气的形成有重要的影响。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"编队;列队","en":"If people or things are in formation, they are arranged in a particular pattern as they move.","ex":{"en":"He was flying in formation with seven other jets","cn":"他和其他7架喷气机一起列队飞行。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"形成物;组成物;(岩或云)层","en":"A rock or cloud formation is rock or cloud of a particular shape or structure.","ex":{"en":"...a vast rock formation shaped like a pillar","cn":"柱状的巨大岩层"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formation__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formation__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The team usually plays in a 4-4-2 formation.","cn":"这支球队比赛通常排出的是 4–4–2 阵形。"},{"en":"evidence of recent star formation in the galaxy","cn":"银河系新恒星形成的证据"}]},"fortnight":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fortnight__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fortnight__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtnaɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"two weeks","cn":"两星期","ex":{"en":"a fortnight’s holiday","cn":"两周的假期"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"两周;十四天","en":"A fortnight is a period of two weeks.","ex":{"en":"I hope to be back in a fortnight.","cn":"我希望在两周内赶回来。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"He's had three accidents in the past fortnight.","cn":"在过去两周他出了三次事故。"},{"en":"in a fortnight's time","cn":"在两周的时间内"}]},"foot":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foot__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foot__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fʊt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the lowest part of the leg, below the ankle, on which a person or an animal stands","cn":"（人或动物的）脚，足","g":"[countable]","lab":"informal","sc":"part of body","ex":{"en":"My feet are aching.","cn":"我的脚疼。"}},{"en":"having or using the type or number of foot/feet mentioned","cn":"有…脚（或足的）；有…只脚（的）；用…脚（或足的）","sc":"-footed","ex":{"en":"bare-footed","cn":"赤脚的"}},{"en":"the part of a sock, stocking, etc. that covers the foot","cn":"（袜子的）足部","g":"[countable, usually singular]","sc":"part of sock"},{"en":"a unit for measuring length equal to 12 inches or 30.48 centimetres","cn":"英尺（= 12 英寸或 30.48 厘米）","sc":"measurement","ex":{"en":"a six-foot high wall","cn":"六英尺高的墙"}},{"en":"the lowest part of something; the base or bottom of something","cn":"最下部；基础；底部","g":"[singular]","lab":"British English","sc":"base/bottom/end","ex":{"en":"The city now reaches to the foot of the surrounding mountains.","cn":"现在，该城市已经延伸到周边山脉的山脚下。"}},{"en":"the further or lower end of something","cn":"尾部；底部","sc":"base/bottom/end","ex":{"en":"The nurse hung a chart at the foot of the bed (= the part of the bed where your feet normally are when you are lying in it).","cn":"护士在床尾挂了一张表。"}},{"en":"a unit of rhythm in a line of poetry containing one stressed syllable and one or more syllables without stress. Each of the four divisions in the following line is a foot","cn":"音步（诗行中的节奏单位，每个音步中有一个重读音节）","g":"[singular]","lab":"specialist","sc":"in poetry","ex":{"en":"For men / may come / and men / may go.","cn":"（此诗行四个部分有四个音步）"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"脚;足","en":"Your feet are the parts of your body that are at the ends of your legs, and that you stand on.","ex":{"en":"She stamped her foot again.","cn":"她又跺了跺脚。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"最下部;基部;底部","en":"The foot of something is the part that is farthest from its top.","ex":{"en":"David called to the children from the foot of the stairs","cn":"戴维在楼梯下面喊孩子们。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"床尾;床脚","en":"The foot of a bed is the end nearest to the feet of the person lying in it.","ex":{"en":"Friends stood at the foot of the bed, looking at her with serious faces.","cn":"朋友们站在床脚处，神情严肃地看着她。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"英尺(相当于 12 英寸或 30.48 厘米)","en":"A foot is a unit for measuring length, height, or depth, and is equal to 12 inches or 30.48 centimetres. When you are giving measurements, the form 'foot' is often used as the plural instead of the plural form 'feet'.","ex":{"en":"This beautiful and curiously shaped lake lies at around fifteen thousand feet","cn":"这个形状奇特的美丽湖泊周长约有15,000英尺。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(刹车或泵)用脚操作的，脚踏的","en":"A foot brake or foot pump is operated by your foot rather than by your hand.","ex":{"en":"I tried to reach the foot brakes but I couldn't.","cn":"我试图去够脚刹，但是没能踩到。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"(巡逻队)步行的;步(兵)的","en":"A foot patrol or foot soldiers walk rather than travelling in vehicles or on horseback.","ex":{"en":"Paratroopers and foot-soldiers entered the building on the government's behalf.","cn":"伞兵和步兵代表政府进入大楼。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(诗歌的)音步","en":"In poetry, a foot is one of the basic units of rhythm into which a line is divided."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"害怕;胆怯;裹足不前","en":"If you get cold feet about something, you become nervous or frightened about it because you think it will fail.","ex":{"en":"The Government is getting cold feet about the reforms.","cn":"政府对改革缩手缩脚。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"站稳脚跟;变得自信;能独立行动","en":"If you say that someone is finding their feet in a new situation, you mean that they are starting to feel confident and to deal with things successfully.","ex":{"en":"I don't know anyone in England but I am sure I will manage when I find my feet","cn":"我在英格兰不认识什么人，但是我相信自己一旦站稳脚跟就可以独当一面。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"脚踏实地;踏踏实实","en":"If you say that someone has their feet on the ground, you approve of the fact that they have a sensible and practical attitude towards life, and do not have unrealistic ideas.","ex":{"en":"In that respect he needs to keep his feet on the ground and not get carried away","cn":"在那一方面他需要脚踏实地，不能飘飘然。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"步行;走路去","en":"If you go somewhere on foot, you walk, rather than using any form of transport.","ex":{"en":"We rowed ashore, then explored the island on foot for the rest of the day.","cn":"我们划船到了岸边，之后余下的时间步行在岛上探险。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"站立;站着","en":"If you are on your feet, you are standing up.","ex":{"en":"Everyone was on their feet applauding wildly.","cn":"每个人都站起身来热烈鼓掌。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"恢复体力;身体康复","en":"If you say that someone or something is on their feet again after an illness or difficult period, you mean that they have recovered and are back to normal.","ex":{"en":"You need someone to take the pressure off and help you get back on your feet","cn":"你需要有人为你分担压力，帮你恢复元气。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"运气好;走运","en":"If you say that someone always falls or lands on their feet, you mean that they are always successful or lucky, although they do not seem to achieve this by their own efforts.","ex":{"en":"He has good looks and charm, and always falls on his feet","cn":"他长得很帅，也有魅力，总是走好运。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"一只脚踏进了坟墓;行将就木","en":"If you say that someone has one foot in the grave, you mean that they are very old or very ill and will probably die soon."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"情况完全逆转;事实恰恰相反","en":"If you say, in British English, the boot is on the other foot or, mainly in American English, the shoe is on the other foot, you mean that a situation has been reversed completely, so that the person who was in the better position before is now in the worse one.","ex":{"en":"You're not in a position to remove me. The boot is now on the other foot.","cn":"你没有权力开除我。相反，我现在可以开除你。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"全力以赴;尽最大努力","en":"If you put your best foot forward, you act in a cheerful, determined way.","ex":{"en":"Put your best foot forward and work on the assumption that there is an acceptable solution to every problem you are likely to face.","cn":"要尽力而为，要相信你可能遇到的每一个问题都会有一个适当的解决方案。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"拿定主意阻止;执意反对","en":"If someone puts their foot down, they use their authority in order to stop something happening.","ex":{"en":"He had planned to go skiing on his own in March but his wife had decided to put her foot down.","cn":"他原本打算在 3 月独自去滑雪，但是他的太太决定让他打消这个念头。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"猛踩油门;开快车","en":"If someone puts their foot down when they are driving, they drive as fast as they can.","ex":{"en":"I asked the driver to put his foot down for Nagchukha.","cn":"我要求司机加大油门去那曲。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(行为或言语)使人尴尬,冒犯别人","en":"If someone puts their foot in it or puts their foot in their mouth, they accidentally do or say something which embarrasses or offends people.","ex":{"en":"Our chairman has really put his foot in it, poor man, though he doesn't know it.","cn":"我们的主席真的让人很尴尬，可怜的人，尽管他自己没意识到。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"(尤指架起双脚)坐下(或躺下)休息，放松","en":"If you put your feet up, you relax or have a rest, especially by sitting or lying with your feet supported off the ground.","ex":{"en":"After supper he'd put his feet up and read. It was a pleasant prospect.","cn":"晚饭后他会支起双腿，歇一歇，看看书。那真是件很惬意的事情。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"做错事;犯错误","en":"If you never put a foot wrong, you never make any mistakes.","ex":{"en":"When he's around, we never put a foot wrong","cn":"他在的时候，我们从来不会出错。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"踏上，涉足(某地)","en":"If you say that someone sets foot in a place, you mean that they enter it or reach it, and you are emphasizing the significance of their action. If you say that someone never sets foot in a place, you are emphasizing that they never go there.","ex":{"en":"...the day the first man set foot on the moon","cn":"人类首次登上月球的那一天"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"自食其力;独立","en":"If someone has to stand on their own two feet, they have to be independent and manage their lives without help from other people.","ex":{"en":"My father didn't mind whom I married, so long as I could stand on my own two feet and wasn't dependent on my husband.","cn":"只要我能够自食其力，不依附于自己的丈夫，嫁给谁我父亲倒是并不介意。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"站起;起身","en":"If you get or rise to your feet, you stand up.","ex":{"en":"Malone got to his feet and followed his superior out of the suite","cn":"马隆站起身来，跟在他的上司后面走出了套房。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"缠人;碍手碍脚","en":"If you say that someone is under your feet, you are annoyed because they are with you or near you, and are bothering you.","ex":{"en":"The children were running about under everybody's feet.","cn":"孩子们在周围乱跑，让所有人都很烦。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"一开始就不对;出师不利","en":"If someone gets off on the wrong foot in a new situation, they make a bad start by doing something in completely the wrong way.","ex":{"en":"Even though they called the election and had been preparing for it for some time, they got off on the wrong foot.","cn":"尽管他们召集了选举，也为此做了一段时间的准备，但是一开始就走错了。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to foot the bill→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"feet of clay→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"foot in the door→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"drag your feet→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"hand and foot→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":". to shoot yourself in the foot→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to sweep someone off their feet→see: ;"},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"to vote with your feet→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘Ian can't come because he's tired.’ ‘Tired my foot! Lazy more like!’ “","cn":"伊恩不能来，因为他累了。” “累个屁！说懒还差不多！”"},{"en":"I always wanted to work in TV but it took me two years to get a foot in the door.","cn":"我一直想做电视工作，但花了两年才进了这个圈子。"}]},"foolishness":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"showing a total lack of good sense or good judgment. Stupid sounds very strong and is often used when you are annoyed or strongly criticizing someone’s behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"doing or saying things that are not sensible or serious, and that may make you feel embarrassed later. Silly sounds much gentler than stupid","cn":""}]},"examples":[{"en":"I’ve never heard anything so foolish in all my life.","cn":"","src":"ld"},{"en":"It would be foolish to ignore his advice.","cn":"","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foolishness__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foolishness__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfuːlɪʃnəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"behaviour that shows a lack of good sense or judgement","cn":"愚蠢的；傻的","ex":{"en":"Jenny had to laugh at her own foolishness.","cn":"珍妮只能嘲笑自己蠢。"}}]}},"fondness":{"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"to like someone very much, especially when you have known them for a long time and almost feel love for them","cn":""},{"en":"to like something, especially something you have liked for a long time","cn":""}]},"examples":[{"en":"Joe’s quite fond of her, isn’t he?","cn":"","src":"ld"},{"en":"Over the years we’ve grown very fond of each other.","cn":"","src":"ld"}],"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fondness__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fondness__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒndnəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a feeling of love or liking for somebody, especially somebody you have known for a long time","cn":"喜爱（尤指认识已久的人）","ex":{"en":"He will be remembered by the staff with great fondness.","cn":"全体员工都会深深地怀念他。"}},{"en":"pleasure, especially relating to something you have liked or enjoyed for a long time","cn":"喜爱（尤指长期喜爱的事物）","ex":{"en":"a fondness for animals","cn":"对动物的喜爱"}}]}},"forgot":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"Forgot is the past tense of forget ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forgot__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forgot__us_1.mp3"}},"forget":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forget__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forget__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈɡet","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to not remember to do something that you ought to do, or to bring or buy something that you ought to bring or buy","cn":"忘记做（或带、买等）","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"to do something","ex":{"en":"‘Why weren't you at the meeting?’ ‘Sorry—I forgot.’","cn":"“你为什么没有参加会议？”“对不起，我忘了。”"}},{"en":"to be unable to remember something that has happened in the past or information that you knew in the past","cn":"忘记；遗忘","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"events/facts","ex":{"en":"Oh, I almost forgot—there was a call for you.","cn":"噢，我差点儿忘了，你有个电话。"}},{"en":"to deliberately stop thinking about somebody/something","cn":"不再想；不再把…放在心上","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"stop thinking about something","ex":{"en":"Try to forget about what happened.","cn":"尽量不再想发生过的事情。"}},{"en":"to stop thinking that something is a possibility","cn":"不再考虑…的可能","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","sc":"stop thinking about something","ex":{"en":"If I lose this job, we can forget about buying a new car.","cn":"要是我丢掉这份工作，我们就别想买新车。"}},{"en":"to behave in a way that is not socially acceptable","cn":"（举止）不得体","g":"[transitive]","sc":"yourself","ex":{"en":"I'm forgetting myself. I haven't offered you a drink yet!","cn":"我真是不成体统。还没有让您喝点什么呢！"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"忘记;遗忘","en":"If you forget something or forget how to do something, you cannot think of it or think how to do it, although you knew it or knew how to do it in the past.","ex":{"en":"Sometimes I improvise and change the words because I forget them","cn":"有时，我临场发挥改了词，因为我把原来的词给忘了。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"忘记;忘了(做)","en":"If you forget something or forget to do it, you fail to think about it or fail to remember to do it, for example because you are thinking about other things.","ex":{"en":"She never forgets her daddy's birthday","cn":"她从来不会忘记老爸的生日。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"忘记带;落下","en":"If you forget something that you had intended to bring with you, you do not bring it because you did not think about it at the right time.","ex":{"en":"Once when we were going to Paris, I forgot my passport.","cn":"有一次我们准备去巴黎时，我忘了带护照。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"不放在心上;不去想","en":"If you forget something or someone, you deliberately put them out of your mind and do not think about them any more.","ex":{"en":"I hope you will forget the bad experience you had today","cn":"我希望你不要把今天遇到的倒霉事放在心上。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"忘乎所以;举止不得体","en":"If you forget yourself, you behave in an uncontrolled or unacceptable way, which is not the way in which you usually behave.","ex":{"en":"He was so fascinated by her beauty that he forgot himself and leaned across to touch her.","cn":"他为她的美貌所倾倒，以至于忘乎所以地靠上前去触摸她。"}},{"pos":"CONVENTION 惯用语","cn":"没关系;不必在意;不要再提了","en":"You say 'Forget it' in reply to someone as a way of telling them not to worry or bother about something, or as an emphatic way of saying no to a suggestion.","ex":{"en":"'Sorry, Liz. I think I was a bit rude to you.' —","cn":""}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"还有;还包括","en":"You say not forgetting a particular thing or person when you want to include them in something that you have already talked about.","ex":{"en":"The first thing is to support as many shows as one can, not forgetting the small local ones.","cn":"首先要尽可能多地支持演出，这其中也包括当地的小型演出。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"‘Any chance of you helping out here?’ ‘Forget it, I've got too much to do.’ “","cn":"这儿你能帮个忙吗？” “不可能，我还有一大堆活要干呢。”"},{"en":"‘Now, what were you saying about John?’ ‘Forget it, it doesn't matter.’ “","cn":"嗳，你刚才说约翰什么来着？” “别提了，那无关紧要。”"}]},"formality":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈmæləti","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a thing that you must do as a formal or official part of a legal process, a social situation, etc.","cn":"正式手续","g":"[countable, usually plural]","ex":{"en":"to go through all the formalities necessary in order to get a gun licence","cn":"办理取得持枪执照的全部必要手续"}},{"en":"a thing that you must do as part of an official process, but that has little meaning and will not affect what happens","cn":"例行公事","g":"[countable, usually singular]","ex":{"en":"He already knows he has the job so the interview is a mere formality.","cn":"他已经知道自己得到了这个工作，所以面试仅仅是走走过场。"}},{"en":"correct and formal behaviour","cn":"遵守礼节","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"Different levels of formality are appropriate in different situations.","cn":"不同规格的礼节适用于不同场合。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"形式;仪式;俗套","en":"If you say that an action or procedure is just a formality, you mean that it is done only because it is normally done, and that it will not have any real effect on the situation.","ex":{"en":"With the Cold War almost over, the talks were a mere formality.","cn":"随着冷战即将结束，对话就只是一种形式了。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"程序;正式手续","en":"Formalities are formal actions or procedures that are carried out as part of a particular activity or event.","ex":{"en":"They are whisked through the immigration and customs formalities in a matter of minutes.","cn":"给他们办理入境和通关手续只用了短短几分钟时间。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/formality__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/formality__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He already knows he has the job so the interview is a mere formality.","cn":"他已知道得到了这个工作，所以面试仅仅是走走过场。"},{"en":"Let's skip the formalities and get down to business.","cn":"咱们省去繁文缛节，开始讨论实质问题吧。"}]},"format":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/format__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/format__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmæt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the general arrangement, plan, design, etc. of something","cn":"呈现方式；编排；形式","ex":{"en":"The format of the new quiz show has proved popular.","cn":"事实证明新的知识竞赛节目的形式很受欢迎。"}},{"en":"the shape and size of a book, magazine, etc.","cn":"（出版物的）开本","ex":{"en":"They've brought out the magazine in a new format.","cn":"他们用新的开本出版这一杂志。"}},{"en":"the way in which data is stored or held to be worked on by a computer","cn":"格式","lab":"computing","ex":{"en":"The images are stored in a digital format within the database.","cn":"图像以数字格式存储在数据库中。"}},{"en":"to arrange text in a particular way on a page or a screen","cn":"安排…的版式","lab":"specialist","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to prepare a computer disk for storing digital information","cn":"格式化","lab":"computing","pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"版式;格式;形式","en":"The format of something is the way or order in which it is arranged and presented.","ex":{"en":"I had met with him to explain the format of the programme and what we had in mind.","cn":"我已经和他当面解释了我们节目的形式以及我们的想法。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(电脑软件或音乐的)载体形式","en":"The format of a piece of computer software or a musical recording is the type of equipment on which it is designed to be used or played. For example, possible formats for a musical recording are CD and cassette.","ex":{"en":"His latest album is available on all formats.","cn":"他的最新专辑有各种载体形式。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"格式化(磁盘)","en":"To format a computer disk means to run a program so that the disk can be written on."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"编排(计算机文本或图表)的格式","en":"To format a piece of computer text or graphics means to arrange the way in which it appears when it is printed or is displayed on a screen.","ex":{"en":"When text is saved from a Web page, it is often very badly formatted with many short lines.","cn":"从网页上转存文本时，往往会出现许多短行，格式也乱了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The format of the new quiz show has proved popular.","cn":"新的智力竞赛节目的总体安排结果证明很受欢迎。"},{"en":"They've brought out the magazine in a new format.","cn":"他们用新的版式出版这杂志。"}]},"four":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/four__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/four__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔː(r)","pos":"","senses":[{"en":"4","cn":"四","ex":{"en":"There are only four cookies left.","cn":"只剩下四块饼干了。"}},{"en":"a group of four people or things","cn":"四个人（或事物）的一组","ex":{"en":"to make up a four at tennis","cn":"凑成四个人打网球"}},{"en":"a hit that scores four runs (= points)","cn":"得四分的一击"},{"en":"a team of four people who row a long narrow boat in races; the boat that they row","cn":"四人赛艇队；四人赛艇"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"NUM 数词","cn":"(数字)4","en":"Four is the number 4.","ex":{"en":"Judith is married with four children.","cn":"朱迪丝已经结婚了，有四个孩子。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(板球中)得 4 分的一击","en":"In cricket, if a player hits a four, they score four runs by hitting the ball along the ground so that it crosses the boundary at the edge of the playing area.","ex":{"en":"Taylor hit 13 fours and batted for 140 minutes.","cn":"泰勒打了 13 个 4 分球，击球时间为 140 分钟。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"四人赛艇","en":"A four is a narrow racing boat that is rowed by a team of four people."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"四肢着地;趴着","en":"If you are on all fours, your knees, feet, and hands are on the ground.","ex":{"en":"She crawled on all fours over to the window.","cn":"她爬到窗边。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Don't let this go further than these four walls (= Don't tell anyone else who is not in the room now).","cn":"走出屋外这事就不要再谈了。"},{"en":"a coach and four (= four horses)","cn":"四匹马拉的四轮大马车"}]},"forge":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːdʒ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to put a lot of effort into making something successful or strong so that it will last","cn":"艰苦干成；努力加强","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"a move to forge new links between management and workers","cn":"努力建立新劳资关系的措施"}},{"en":"to make an illegal copy of something in order to cheat people","cn":"伪造；假冒","g":"[transitive]","lab":"British English","ex":{"en":"to forge a passport/banknote/document","cn":"伪造护照／钞票／文件"}},{"en":"to shape metal by heating it in a fire and hitting it with a hammer; to make an object in this way","cn":"锻造；制作","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"swords forged from steel","cn":"用钢锻造的刀剑"}},{"en":"to move forward in a steady but powerful way","cn":"稳步前进","g":"[intransitive]","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"He forged through the crowds to the front of the stage.","cn":"他挤过人群稳步走到台前。"}},{"en":"a place where objects are made by heating and shaping pieces of metal, especially one where a blacksmith works","cn":"铁匠铺","pos":"noun"},{"en":"a large piece of equipment used for heating metals in; a building or part of a factory where this is found","cn":"锻铁炉；锻造车间；锻造工厂","pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"V-RECIP 相互动词","cn":"缔造;建立","en":"If one person or institution forges an agreement or relationship with another, they create it with a lot of hard work, hoping that it will be strong or lasting.","ex":{"en":"The Prime Minister is determined to forge a good relationship with America's new leader","cn":"首相决意要和美国的新任领导人建立良好的关系。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"创造;开创","en":"If you say that a person has forged something that you approve of, you mean that you admire them for having done something difficult.","ex":{"en":"The project will help inmates forge new careers","cn":"这项计划会帮助犯人开始新的职业。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"伪造，仿造(钞票、文件、绘画作品等)","en":"If someone forges something such as a banknote, a document, or a painting, they copy it or make it so that it looks genuine, in order to deceive people.","ex":{"en":"He admitted seven charges including forging passports","cn":"他承认了7项罪名，其中包括伪造护照。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"铁匠铺;锻造厂","en":"A forge is a place where someone makes metal goods and equipment by heating pieces of metal and then shaping them.","ex":{"en":"...the blacksmith's forge.","cn":"铁匠铺"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"炼;锻造","en":"If someone forges an object out of metal, they heat the metal and then hammer and bend it into the required shape.","ex":{"en":"To forge a blade takes great skill.","cn":"锻造刀刃需要很高超的技巧。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"取得进展;稳步推进","en":"If you forge ahead with something, you continue with it and make a lot of progress with it.","ex":{"en":"He again pledged to forge ahead with his plans for reform","cn":"他再次承诺会稳步推进自己的改革计划。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：forge ahead"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forge__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forge__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He's getting good at forging his mother's signature.","cn":"他把母亲的签名伪造得越来越维妙维肖了。"},{"en":"Strategic alliances are being forged with major European companies.","cn":"正与欧洲主要公司设法结成战略同盟。"}]},"forbidden":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forbidden__gb_2.mp3","us":"media/us/forbidden__us_2.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈbɪdn","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not allowed","cn":"禁止的；不准的","ex":{"en":"Photography is strictly forbidden in the museum.","cn":"博物馆内禁止摄影。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"禁止的;不准的","en":"If something is forbidden, you are not allowed to do it or have it.","ex":{"en":"Smoking was forbidden everywhere","cn":"到处都禁止吸烟。"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"禁止进入的;谢绝参观的","en":"A forbidden place is one that you are not allowed to visit or enter.","ex":{"en":"This was a forbidden area for foreigners.","cn":"这里曾经禁止外国人进入。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"令人反感的;忌讳的","en":"Forbidden is used to describe things that people strongly disapprove of or feel guilty about, and that are not often mentioned or talked about.","ex":{"en":"The war was a forbidden subject","cn":"战争曾经是人们避讳的话题。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The conversation was in danger of wandering into forbidden territory (= topics that they were not allowed to talk about).","cn":"谈话很可能离题而涉及禁止讨论的领域。"},{"en":"Photography is strictly forbidden in the museum.","cn":"博物馆内禁止摄影。"}]},"fog":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fog__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fog__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɒɡ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a thick cloud of very small drops of water in the air close to the land or sea that is very difficult to see through","cn":"雾","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"Dense/thick fog is affecting roads in the north and visibility is poor.","cn":"浓雾影响了北部的公路，能见度很低。"}},{"en":"a state in which things are not clear and seem difficult to understand","cn":"不明朗；迷惑不解","ex":{"en":"He went through the day with his mind in a fog.","cn":"整整一天，他的头脑都是昏昏沉沉的。"}},{"en":"if a glass surface fogs or is fogged up, it becomes covered in steam or small drops of water so that you cannot see through","cn":"（使）雾气笼罩","g":"[intransitive, transitive]","pos":"verb"},{"en":"to make somebody/something confused or less clear","cn":"使迷惘；使困惑","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"I tried to clear the confusion that was fogging my brain.","cn":"我试图解除使我迷茫的困惑。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"雾","en":"When there is fog, there are tiny drops of water in the air which form a thick cloud and make it difficult to see things.","ex":{"en":"The crash happened in thick fog","cn":"浓雾中发生了撞车。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"烟雾;尘雾","en":"A fog is an unpleasant cloud of something such as smoke inside a building or room.","ex":{"en":"...a fog of stale cigarette smoke.","cn":"一股难闻的香烟烟雾"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"迷惑;迷雾","en":"You can use fog to refer to a situation which stops people from being able to notice things, understand things, or think clearly.","ex":{"en":"The most basic facts about him are lost in a fog of mythology","cn":"关于他的那些最基本信息离奇地湮没无踪了。"}},{"pos":"V-ERG 及物/不及物动词","cn":"(使)(窗户、镜子等)起雾;(使)变模糊","en":"If a window, mirror, or other glass surface fogs or is fogged, it becomes covered with very small drops of water so that you cannot see things clearly through it or in it.","ex":{"en":"The windows fogged immediately","cn":"窗户立刻被雾气笼罩了。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"Dense/thick fog is affecting roads in the north and visibility is poor.","cn":"浓雾影响了北部的公路，能见度很低。"},{"en":"Patches of fog will clear by mid-morning.","cn":"上午十时左右，部分地区的雾将散去。"}]},"forehead":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forehead__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forehead__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːhed","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the part of the face above the eyes and below the hair","cn":"额；前额","lab":"informal","ex":{"en":"He wiped the sweat from his forehead.","cn":"他擦去额头上的汗。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"前额;额头","en":"Your forehead is the area at the front of your head between your eyebrows and your hair."}]}},"forum":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːrəm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an event or medium where people can exchange opinions and ideas on a particular issue; a meeting organized for this purpose","cn":"公共讨论场所；论坛；讨论会","ex":{"en":"to hold an international forum on drug abuse","cn":"举行药物滥用问题国际论坛"}},{"en":"a website or web page where users can put comments about a particular issue or topic and reply to other users' comments","cn":"（网络）论坛，讨论区","ex":{"en":"an internet forum","cn":"互联网论坛"}},{"en":"(in ancient Rome) a public place where meetings were held","cn":"（古罗马）公共集会场所"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指讨论重大公共问题的)论坛，会议场所，讨论会","en":"A forum is a place, situation, or group in which people exchange ideas and discuss issues, especially important public issues.","ex":{"en":"Members of the council agreed that it still had an important role as a forum for discussion","cn":"理事会成员一致认为它仍然发挥着论坛的重要作用。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(古罗马城镇中讨论商业和政治问题的)广场","en":"In ancient Roman towns, the forum was a square where people met to discuss business and political matters."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forum__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forum__us_1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Television is now an important forum for political debate.","cn":"电视现在成了政治辩论的重要平台。"},{"en":"to hold an international forum on drug abuse","cn":"举行药物滥用问题国际论坛"}]},"fox":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fox__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fox__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/fox.jpg"]},"oxford":{"phon":"fɒks","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a wild animal of the dog family, with red-brown fur, a pointed face and a thick heavy tail","cn":"狐；狐狸","g":"[countable]"},{"en":"the skin and fur of the fox, used to make coats, etc.","cn":"狐皮","g":"[uncountable]"},{"en":"a person who is clever and able to get what they want by influencing or tricking other people","cn":"狡猾的人；老狐狸；老滑头","g":"[countable]","lab":"often disapproving","ex":{"en":"He's a wily old fox.","cn":"他是个诡计多端的老狐狸。"}},{"en":"a very attractive person, usually a young woman","cn":"靓女","g":"[countable]","lab":"North American English, informal，，"},{"en":"to be too difficult for somebody to understand or solve; to trick or confuse somebody","cn":"使猜不透；把…难住；使上当；使迷惑","ex":{"en":"The last question foxed even our panel of experts.","cn":"最后这个问题甚至把我们的专家小组都难倒了。"},"pos":"verb"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"狐狸","en":"A fox is a wild animal which looks like a dog and has reddish-brown fur, a pointed face and ears, and a thick tail. Foxes eat smaller animals."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"难住;使困惑","en":"If you are foxed by something, you cannot understand it or solve it.","ex":{"en":"I admit I was foxed for some time","cn":"我承认我一度被难住了。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"老狐狸;狡猾的人","en":"If you describe someone as a fox, you mean they are very clever and deceitful.","ex":{"en":"Enrico was too good, an old fox, cunning.","cn":"恩里科很有心计，是一只狡猾的老狐狸。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"The last question foxed even our panel of experts.","cn":"最后这个问题甚至把我们的专家小组都难倒了。"},{"en":"He's a wily old fox.","cn":"他是个诡计多端的老狐狸。"}]},"forecaster":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forecaster__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forecaster__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːkɑːstə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who says what is expected to happen, especially somebody whose job is to predict the weather","cn":"预测者；（尤指）天气预报员，气象预报员","ex":{"en":"a weather forecaster","cn":"天气预报员"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"预报员;预测者","en":"A forecaster is someone who uses detailed knowledge about a particular activity in order to work out what they think will happen in that activity in the future.","ex":{"en":"Some of the nation's top economic forecasters say the economic recovery is picking up speed.","cn":"这个国家的一些顶尖经济预测专家称经济复苏正在加速。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"an economic forecaster","cn":"经济预测专家"},{"en":"a weather forecaster","cn":"天气预报员"}]},"fortune":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtʃuːn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large amount of money","cn":"大笔的钱；巨款","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"He made a fortune in real estate.","cn":"他在房地产上发了财。"}},{"en":"chance or luck, especially in the way it affects people’s lives","cn":"（尤指影响人生的）机会，运气","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"I have had the good fortune to work with some brilliant directors.","cn":"我有幸与一些卓越的主管人员共事。"}},{"en":"the good and bad things that happen to a person, family, country, etc.","cn":"（个人、家庭、国家等的）发展变化的趋势，命运，际遇","g":"[countable, usually plural, uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The share price tends to follow the changing fortunes of the film industry.","cn":"股价往往随着电影业的浮沉而涨跌。"}},{"en":"a person’s fate or future","cn":"（个人的）命运，前途","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"She can tell your fortune by looking at the lines on your hand.","cn":"她可凭看手纹替你算命。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"大笔的钱;巨款","en":"You can refer to a large sum of money as a fortune or a small fortune to emphasize how large it is.","ex":{"en":"We had to eat out all the time. It ended up costing a fortune","cn":"我们不得不总在外面吃饭，结果花了很多钱。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"财富;财产","en":"Someone who has a fortune has a very large amount of money.","ex":{"en":"He made his fortune in car sales","cn":"他靠卖车发了财。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"运气;机遇","en":"Fortune or good fortune is good luck. Ill fortune is bad luck.","ex":{"en":"Government ministers are starting to wonder how long their good fortune can last.","cn":"政府部长们开始怀疑他们的好运还能够持续多久。"}},{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"时运;运势","en":"If you talk about someone's fortunes or the fortunes of something, you are talking about the extent to which they are doing well or being successful.","ex":{"en":"The electoral fortunes of the Liberal Democratic party may decline","cn":"自由民主党的选举运势可能会下降。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"运气;命运","en":"If you talk about the way someone or something is treated by fortune, you are referring to the good or bad luck that they have.","ex":{"en":"He is certainly being smiled on by fortune.","cn":"现在他一定是得到了命运的垂青。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"算命;算卦","en":"When someone tells your fortune, they tell you what they think will happen to you in the future, which they say is shown, for example, by the lines on your hand."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fortune__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fortune__us_2.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She is hoping her US debut will be the first step on the road to fame and fortune.","cn":"她希望她在美国的首次演出将是她走上名利双收之路的第一步。"},{"en":"You don't have to spend a fortune to give your family tasty, healthy meals.","cn":"让家里人吃味道好又健康的餐食并不需要花许多钱。"}]},"font":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɒnt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large stone bowl in a church that holds water for the ceremony of baptism","cn":"圣洗池（设于教堂中，常为石造）","ex":{"en":"the baptismal font","cn":"洗礼字体"}},{"en":"the particular size and style of a set of letters that are used in printing, etc.","cn":"字体；字型","lab":"specialist"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"字体","en":"In printing, a font is a set of characters of the same style and size."},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"洗礼盆，圣水盂(教堂中洗礼用)","en":"In a church, a font is a bowl which holds the water used for baptisms."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/font__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/font__us_1.mp3"}},"foregoing":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/foregoing__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/foregoing__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːɡəʊɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"used to refer to something that has just been mentioned","cn":"上述的；前述的","ex":{"en":"the foregoing discussion","cn":"上述讨论"}},{"en":"what has just been mentioned","cn":"前面所提到的事物；以上所述","g":"[singular + singular or plural verb]","ex":{"en":"The foregoing is a description of the proposed plan.","cn":"以上是对拟议计划的描述。"}}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"PRON 代词","cn":"前述内容","en":"You can refer to what has just been stated or mentioned as the foregoing .","ex":{"en":"You might think from the foregoing that the French want to phase accents out. Not at all.","cn":"根据前文所述，你们可能以为法国人打算废除各种口音。事实并非如此。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"the foregoing discussion","cn":"上述讨论"},{"en":"The foregoing examples illustrate this point.","cn":"上述例证阐明了这个观点。"}]},"forward":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/forward__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/forward__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːwəd","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"towards a place or position that is in front","cn":"向前","lab":"especially in British English","ex":{"en":"She leaned forward and kissed him on the cheek.","cn":"她倾身向前，吻了他的面颊。"}},{"en":"towards the future; ahead in time","cn":"向将来；往后","lab":"especially in British English","ex":{"en":"Looking forward, we hope to expand our operations in several of our overseas branches.","cn":"展望未来，我们希望拓展几家海外分公司的业务。"}},{"en":"towards a good result","cn":"进展；前进","ex":{"en":"We consider this agreement to be an important step forward.","cn":"我们认为，这项协定是向前迈出了重要的一步。"}},{"en":"earlier; sooner","cn":"提前","ex":{"en":"It was decided to bring the meeting forward two weeks.","cn":"已决定把会议提前两周。"}},{"en":"in or towards the front part of a ship or plane","cn":"在（或向）船头；在（或向）机首","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"The main cabin is situated forward of (= in front of) the mast.","cn":"主舱在桅杆的前面。"}},{"en":"directed or moving towards the front","cn":"向前的；前进的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"The door opened, blocking his forward movement.","cn":"门开了，挡住他前进的路。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"located in front, especially on a ship, plane or other vehicle","cn":"（尤指船、飞机或其他交通工具）前部的，前面的","g":"[only before noun]","lab":"specialist","ex":{"en":"the forward cabins","cn":"前部舱室"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"relating to the future","cn":"未来的；将来的","ex":{"en":"the forward movement of history","cn":"历史的向前发展"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"behaving towards somebody in a manner that is too confident or too informal","cn":"鲁莽的；冒失的；无礼的","ex":{"en":"I hope you don't think I'm being too forward.","cn":"我希望你不要认为我太冒失。"},"pos":"adjective"},{"en":"to send or pass goods or information to somebody","cn":"发送，寄（商品或信息）","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"We will be forwarding our new catalogue to you next week.","cn":"我们将于下星期给你寄上新的商品目录。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to send a letter, etc. received at the address a person used to live at to their new address","cn":"（按新地址）转寄，转投，转交","ex":{"en":"Could you forward any mail to us in New York?","cn":"你能不能把所有信件转寄到纽约给我们？"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to help to improve or develop something","cn":"促进；有助于…的发展；增进","lab":"formal","ex":{"en":"He saw the assignment as a way to forward his career.","cn":"他把这项任务看作事业发展的途径。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"an attacking player whose position is near the front of a team in some sports","cn":"（运动队的）前锋","pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"朝前;向前","en":"If you move or look forward, you move or look in a direction that is in front of you. In British English, you can also move or look forwards .","ex":{"en":"He came forward with his hand out. 'Mr and Mrs Selby?' he enquired","cn":"他走上前去伸出手来。“是塞尔比先生和夫人吗？”他问道。"}},{"pos":"ADV-GRADED 副词","cn":"靠近前面;在前面","en":"Forward means in a position near the front of something such as a building or a vehicle.","ex":{"en":"The best seats are in the aisle and as far forward as possible","cn":"最好的座位在过道处，越靠前越好。"}},{"pos":"PREP-PHRASE 短语介词","cn":"(尤指在轮船或飞机上)靠近…前面的，在…前面的","en":"If one thing is forward of another, especially on a ship or aircraft, the first thing is in front of the second thing or further ahead.","ex":{"en":"Forward of the main cabin are the guest cabins","cn":"主舱前面是客舱。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"向前(看);向将来(看)","en":"If you say that someone looks forward, you approve of them because they think about what will happen in the future and plan for it. In British English, you can also say that someone looks forwards .","ex":{"en":"Now the leadership wants to look forward, and to outline a strategy for the rest of the century","cn":"现在领导层想要展望未来，为本世纪余下的时间勾画出战略纲要。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(把钟表)调前地，拨快地","en":"If you put a clock or watch forward, you change the time shown on it so that it shows a later time, for example when the time changes to summer time or daylight saving time.","ex":{"en":"When we put the clocks forward in March we go into British Summer Time.","cn":"我们3月份把表调快时，就进入了英国夏令时。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"自从…;从…起;自…以来","en":"When you are referring to a particular time, if you say that something was true from that time forward, you mean that it became true at that time, and continued to be true afterwards.","ex":{"en":"Velazquez's work from that time forward was confined largely to portraits of the royal family.","cn":"委拉斯开兹的作品从那时起大多局限于皇室成员画像。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"向前地;前进地;有进展地","en":"You use forward to indicate that something progresses or improves. In British English, you can also use forwards .","ex":{"en":"And by boosting economic prosperity in Mexico, Canada and the United States, it will help us move forward on issues that concern all of us","cn":"促进墨西哥、加拿大和美国的经济繁荣将有助于解决与我们大家息息相关的诸多问题。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"推进;促进","en":"If you forward something, you cause it to progress or improve.","ex":{"en":"The music is used to forward the plot, not simply to keep the toes tapping.","cn":"音乐用来推进情节发展，而不仅仅是保持节奏感。"}},{"pos":"ADV 副词","cn":"(提)出;(推)出;(现)出","en":"If something or someone is put forward, or comes forward, they are suggested or offered as suitable for a particular purpose.","ex":{"en":"Over the years several similar theories have been put forward","cn":"几年来已经有好几个类似理论相继提出。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"转交;转发;转接","en":"If a letter or message is forwarded to someone, it is sent to the place where they are, after having been sent to a different place earlier.","ex":{"en":"When he's out on the road, office calls are forwarded to the cellular phone in his truck","cn":"他在路上时，打到办公室的电话会转接到卡车里的移动电话上。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"鲁莽的;冒失的;自负的","en":"If you describe someone as forward, you mean that they speak very confidently and honestly but they do not always show enough respect for the person they are talking to.","ex":{"en":"He's very forward and confident and chats happily to other people.","cn":"他很自以为是，喜欢和别人攀谈。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(足球、篮球或曲棍球等运动的)前锋","en":"In football, basketball, or hockey, a forward is a player whose usual position is in the opponents' half of the field, and whose usual job is to attack or score goals."},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"backwards and forwards→see: ;"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Looking forward, we hope to expand our operations in several of our overseas branches.","cn":"展望未来，我们希望拓展其中几家海外分公司的业务。"},{"en":"We consider this agreement to be an important step forward.","cn":"我们认为，这项协定是向前迈出了重要的一步。"}]},"forged":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːdʒ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to put a lot of effort into making sth successful or strong so that it will last","cn":"艰苦干成；努力加强"},{"en":"to make an illegal copy of sth in order to cheat people","cn":"伪造；假冒"}]}},"folding":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊldɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"that can be folded, so that it can be carried or stored in a small space","cn":"折叠式的；可折叠的","ex":{"en":"a folding chair/bike/knife","cn":"折叠椅／自行车／刀"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/folding__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/folding__us_1.mp3","img":["media/ldoce/img/folding_chair.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"a foldaway bed","cn":"折叠床"},{"en":"a folding chair","cn":"折椅"}]},"focuses":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊkəs","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to give attention, effort, etc. to one particular subject, situation or person rather than another","cn":"集中（注意力、精力等）于"},{"en":"to adapt or be adjusted so that things can be seen clearly; to adjust sth so that you can see things clearly （","cn":"使）调节焦距"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/uk/focus__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/focus__us_1.mp3"}},"fourth":{"media":{"uk":"media/uk/fourth__gb_1.mp3","us":"media/us/fourth__us_1.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːθ","pos":"ordinal number","senses":[{"en":"4th","cn":"第四","ex":{"en":"Today is the fourth (of May).","cn":"今天是五月四日。"}},{"en":"one of four equal parts of something","cn":"四等份之一","lab":"especially North American English","ex":{"en":"a fourth of the city population","cn":"城市人口的四分之一"},"pos":"noun"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ORD 序数词","cn":"第四","en":"The fourth item in a series is the one that you count as number four.","ex":{"en":"Last year's winner Greg Lemond of the United States is in fourth place.","cn":"去年的冠军、来自美国的格雷格·莱蒙德现在排名第 4。"}},{"pos":"FRACTION 分数词","cn":"四分之一","en":"A fourth is one of four equal parts of something.","ex":{"en":"Three-fourths of the public say they favor a national referendum on the issue.","cn":"四分之三的公众表示希望就这个问题进行全民公决。"}}]},"examples":[{"en":"in the fourth century","cn":"在四世纪"},{"en":"her fourth birthday","cn":"她的四岁生日"}]},"fountains":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfaʊntən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a structure from which water is sent up into the air by a pump , used to decorate parks and gardens/yards","cn":"人工喷泉；喷水池"},{"en":"a strong flow of liquid or of another substance that is forced into the air","cn":"喷泉；（液体或其他物质的）喷射，涌流"}]}},"forests":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrɪst","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large area of land that is thickly covered with trees","cn":"森林；林区"},{"en":"a mass of tall narrow objects that are close together （","cn":"森林似的）一丛，一片"}]}},"forms":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type or variety of sth","cn":"类型；种类"},{"en":"the particular way sth is, seems, looks or is presented","cn":"形式；外表；样子"}]}},"follows":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to come or go after or behind sb/sth","cn":"跟随；跟着"},{"en":"to come after sth/sb else in time or order; to happen as a result of sth else （","cn":"时间或顺序上）在 … 后发生；因 … 而发生"}]}},"foresees":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈsiː","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to think sth is going to happen in the future; to know about sth before it happens","cn":"预料；预见；预知"}]}},"founded":{"oxford":{"phon":"faʊnd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to start sth, such as an organization or an institution, especially by providing money","cn":"创建，创办（组织或机构，尤指提供资金）"},{"en":"to be the first to start building and living in a town or country","cn":"建立，兴建（城镇或国家）"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"建于…之上的;以…为基础的","en":"If something is founded on a particular thing, it is based on it.","ex":{"en":"The criticisms are founded on facts as well as on convictions","cn":"这些批评是基于事实和信念。"}}]}},"foothills":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊthɪl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a hill or low mountain at the base of a higher mountain or range of mountains","cn":"山麓小丘"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-PLURAL 复数名词","cn":"山麓小丘","en":"The foothills of a mountain or a range of mountains are the lower hills or mountains around its base.","ex":{"en":"Pasadena lies in the foothills of the San Gabriel mountains.","cn":"帕萨迪纳坐落于圣加布里埃尔山麓的丘陵地带。"}}]}},"forties":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːti","pos":"number","senses":[{"en":"40","cn":"四十"},{"en":"numbers, years or temperatures from 40 to 49","cn":"四十几；四十年代"}]}},"foundations":{"oxford":{"phon":"faʊnˈdeɪʃn","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a layer of bricks, concrete, etc. that forms the solid underground base of a building","cn":"地基；房基；基础"},{"en":"a principle, an idea or a fact that sth is based on and that it grows from","cn":"基本原理；根据；基础"}]}},"forwards":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːwəd","pos":"adverb","senses":[{"en":"towards a place or position that is in front","cn":"向前"},{"en":"towards a good result","cn":"进展；前进"}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/forwards0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/forwards.mp3"},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"}]}},"fortifying":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtɪfaɪ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to make a place more able to resist attack, especially by building high walls","cn":"筑防御工事；（尤指）筑城防御"},{"en":"to make sb/yourself feel stronger, braver, etc. （","cn":"在物质或精神上）加强，增强"}]}},"formed":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type or variety of sth","cn":"类型；种类"},{"en":"the particular way sth is, seems, looks or is presented","cn":"形式；外表；样子"}]}},"footfalls":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtfɔːl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"( literary ) the sound of the steps made by sb walking","cn":"脚步声"},{"en":"( BrE ) ( business","cn":"商 ) the number of people that visit a particular shop/store, shopping centre, etc. over a period of time 客流，人流（商店、购物中心在一"}]}},"followed":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to come or go after or behind sb/sth","cn":"跟随；跟着"},{"en":"to come after sth/sb else in time or order; to happen as a result of sth else （","cn":"时间或顺序上）在 … 后发生；因 … 而发生"}]}},"founders":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfaʊndə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who starts an organization, institution, etc. or causes sth to be built （","cn":"组织、机构等的）创建者，创办者，发起人"},{"en":"to fail because of a particular problem or difficulty","cn":"失败；破产"}]}},"footed":{"oxford":{"phon":"fʊt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the lowest part of the leg, below the ankle, on which a person or an animal stands （","cn":"人或动物的）脚，足"},{"en":"( in adjectives and adverbs","cn":"构成形容词和副词 ) having or using the type or number of foot/feet mentioned 有 … 脚（或足的）；有 … 只脚（的）；用 … 脚（或足的）"}]}},"footsteps":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtstep","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the sound or mark made each time your foot touches the ground when you are walking or running","cn":"脚步声；足迹"}]}},"forewarned":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈwɔːn","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"( formal ) to warn sb about sth bad or unpleasant before it happens","cn":"预先警告；事先告诫"},{"en":"( saying ) if you know about problems, dangers, etc. before they happen, you can be better prepared for them","cn":"预警即预备；有备无患"}]}},"forming":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːm","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a type or variety of sth","cn":"类型；种类"},{"en":"the particular way sth is, seems, looks or is presented","cn":"形式；外表；样子"}]}},"forays":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒreɪ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an attempt to become involved in a different activity or profession （","cn":"改变职业、活动的）尝试"},{"en":"a short sudden attack made by a group of soldiers","cn":"突袭；闪电式袭击"}]}},"follies":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒli","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a lack of good judgement; the fact of doing sth stupid; an activity or idea that shows a lack of judgement","cn":"愚蠢；愚笨；愚蠢的想法（或事情、行为）"},{"en":"a building that has no practical purpose but was built in the past for decoration, often in the garden of a large country house （","cn":"常见于旧时乡间豪宅花园中的）装饰性建筑"}]}},"forces":{"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"violent physical action used to obtain or achieve sth","cn":"武力；暴力"},{"en":"the physical strength of sth that is shown as it hits sth else","cn":"力；力量"}]}},"foreman":{"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmən","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a male worker who is in charge of a group of other factory or building workers","cn":"工头","ex":{"en":"He got a job as foreman of a building site.","cn":"他得到了一份工作，在建筑工地当工头。"}},{"en":"a man who acts as the leader of a jury in court","cn":"陪审团团长"}]},"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指男性)领班，工头","en":"A foreman is a person, especially a man, in charge of a group of workers.","ex":{"en":"He still visited the dairy daily, but left most of the business details to his manager and foreman.","cn":"他仍然每天到乳品场看看，但把生意上大部分琐碎事务交给经理和工头打理。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"陪审团主席","en":"The foreman of a jury is the person who is chosen as their leader.","ex":{"en":"There was applause from the public gallery as the foreman of the jury announced the verdict.","cn":"陪审团团长宣布判决结果时，旁听席响起了掌声。"}}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/foreman_las3_br.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/foreman.mp3"}},"folded":{"oxford":{"phon":"fəʊld","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to bend sth, especially paper or cloth, so that one part lies on top of another part","cn":"折叠，对折（纸、织物等）"},{"en":"to bend sth so that it becomes smaller or flatter and can be stored or carried more easily; to bend or be able to bend in this way","cn":"折小，叠平，可折小，可叠平（以便贮存或携带）"}]}},"formula":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"原则;规划;方案","en":"A formula is a plan that is invented in order to deal with a particular problem.","ex":{"en":"It is difficult to imagine how the North and South could ever agree on a formula to unify the divided peninsula.","cn":"很难想象南北双方在统一半岛的方案上究竟怎样才能达成一致。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"方案;方法","en":"A formula for a particular situation, usually a good one, is a course of action or a combination of actions that is certain or likely to result in that situation.","ex":{"en":"After he was officially pronounced the world's oldest man, he offered this simple formula for a long and happy life","cn":"在他被正式宣布为世界上最年长的人后，他给出了这样一个简单的快乐长寿的秘诀。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"公式;方程式","en":"A formula is a group of letters, numbers, or other symbols which represents a scientific or mathematical rule.","ex":{"en":"He developed a mathematical formula describing the distances of the planets from the Sun.","cn":"他研究出了一个用于计算行星与太阳之间距离的数学公式。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"分子式;结构式","en":"In science, the formula for a substance is a list of the amounts of various substances which make up that substance, or an indication of the atoms that it is composed of."},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(赛车的)级，方程式","en":"Formula is used followed by a number to indicate a particular type of racing car or something relating to that type of car.","ex":{"en":"...Formula 1 racing cars.","cn":"一级方程式赛车"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"配方奶;代乳品","en":"Formula is a powder which you mix with water to make artificial milk for babies.","ex":{"en":"...bottles of formula.","cn":"几瓶配方奶"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an organized set of ideas, methods, actions etc that you use to do something","cn":""},{"en":"a series of actions that are done in order to achieve a particular result","cn":""},{"en":"the official or usually agreed way of doing something","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n 3 n","senses":[{"en":"A formula is generally a fixed pattern that is used to achieve consistent results. It might be made up of words, numbers, or ideas that work together to define a procedure to be followed for the desired outcome."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. complex, complicated | simple | algebraic, chemical, mathematical, scientific","VERB + FORMULA devise, work out A simple mathematical formula has been devised to allow you to calculate the interest due. | apply, use","PREP. ~ for Do you know the formula for finding the area of a circle? 2 method of solving a problem","ADJ. good, magic, successful, winning | time-honoured, traditional | face-saving The government was forced to find a face-saving formula to ","VERB + FORMULA have No one has a magic formula for keeping youngsters away from crime. | come up with, devise, find, hit on, provide, work o","PREP. ~ for What is their formula for success?"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/ld44formula.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/a/formula.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"They're trying to work out a peace formula acceptable to both sides in the dispute.","cn":"他们正在设法制订出一个争执双方都可以接受的和平方案。"},{"en":"The minister keeps coming out with the same tired formulas.","cn":"这个牧师开口便是千篇一律、使人厌倦的套话。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmjələ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a series of letters, numbers or symbols that represent a rule or law","cn":"公式；方程式；计算式","g":"[countable]","lab":"mathematics","ex":{"en":"This formula is used to calculate the area of a circle.","cn":"这个公式用于计算圆的面积。"}},{"en":"letters and symbols that show the parts of a chemical compound, etc.","cn":"分子式","g":"[countable]","lab":"chemistry","ex":{"en":"CO is the formula for carbon monoxide.","cn":"CO 是一氧化碳的分子式。"}},{"en":"a particular method of doing or achieving something","cn":"方案；方法","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"They're trying to work out a peace formula acceptable to both sides in the dispute.","cn":"他们正在设法制订出一个争执双方都可以接受的和平方案。"}},{"en":"a list of the things that something is made from, giving the amount of each substance to use","cn":"配方；处方；药方","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"the secret formula for the blending of the whisky","cn":"调配威士忌的秘方"}},{"en":"a type of liquid food for babies, given instead of breast milk","cn":"配方奶（母乳的替代品）","g":"[uncountable, countable]"},{"en":"a class of racing car, based on engine size, etc.","cn":"方程式（按发动机大小等对赛车的分级）","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Formula One™ racing","cn":"一级方程式赛车"}},{"en":"a fixed form of words used in a particular situation","cn":"（特定场合的）惯用词语，套话","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"What are the correct legal formulae for this kind of letter?","cn":"写这种信用的正确法律用语是什么呢？"}}]}},"forthright":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"直抒己见的;坦率的;坦诚的","en":"If you describe someone as forthright, you admire them because they show clearly and strongly what they think and feel."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"saying what you really think and not hiding the truth or the facts","cn":""},{"en":"honest and saying what you really think","cn":""},{"en":"willing to talk about what you think, feel etc in an honest way, rather than trying to hide it","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adv adj","senses":[{"en":"When a person is being forthright , they're being direct, clear, or even straight-up. The opposite of forthright might be evasive, shifty, indirect or circuitous. But we're not here to talk about those. We're here to talk about forthright ."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, seem","ADV. very | pretty | characteristically MacTavish was characteristically forthright in his reply.","PREP. about She's always been very forthright about her preferences."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/forthright0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/forthright.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a woman of forthright views","cn":"观点明确的女子"},{"en":"She answered in her usual forthright manner .","cn":"她以一贯的直率作了回答。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːθraɪt","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"direct and honest in manner and speech","cn":"直率的；直截了当的；坦诚的","ex":{"en":"a woman of forthright views","cn":"观点明确的女子"}}]}},"fort":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT; N-IN-NAMES 名称名词；名称名词","cn":"堡垒;要塞;城堡","en":"A fort is a strong building or a place with a wall or fence around it where soldiers can stay and be safe from the enemy."},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"替人照料;代为负责","en":"If you hold the fort for someone, or, in American English, if you hold down the fort, you look after things for them while they are somewhere else or are busy doing something else.","ex":{"en":"His business partner is holding the fort while he is away.","cn":"他不在的时候，其生意伙伴代为负责。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a strong building or group of buildings used by soldiers or an army for defending an important place","cn":"堡垒﹐城堡"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. hill | Iron Age, Roman, Saxon, etc. an Iron Age hill fort","VERB + FORT attack, besiege | hold Government forces managed to hold the fort.","FORT + VERB be/come under attack, be/come under siege The fort was under attack for three days. | fall The fort finally fell after a week of","PREP. at/in a/the ~ All was calm at the fort that night."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/brelasdefort.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/fort1.mp3","img":["media/thumb/fort.jpg"]},"examples":[{"en":"Why not have a day off? I'll hold the fort for you.","cn":"干吗不休息一天？我来为你代管。"},{"en":"Fort Drum","cn":"德鲁姆堡"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a building or buildings built in order to defend an area against attack","cn":"要塞；堡垒；城堡","ex":{"en":"the remains of a Roman fort","cn":"罗马要塞的遗址"}},{"en":"a place where soldiers live and have their training","cn":"兵营；军营；营地","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"Fort Drum","cn":"德拉姆堡"}}]}},"folly":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"愚蠢;荒唐","en":"If you say that a particular action or way of behaving is folly or a folly, you mean that it is foolish.","ex":{"en":"It's sheer folly to build nuclear power stations in a country that has dozens of earthquakes every year.","cn":"在每年会发生几十次地震的国家建造核电站简直就是愚蠢至极。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指旧时英国花园等中的)装饰性建筑","en":"A folly is a small tower or other unusual building that is built as a decoration in a large garden or park, especially in Britain in former times."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a very stupid thing to do, especially one that is likely to have serious results 〔","cn":"尤指可能导致严重后果的〕蠢事﹐荒唐事"},{"en":"an unusual building that was built in the past as a decoration, not to be used or lived in 〔","cn":"旧时无实用价值的〕风格独特的装饰性建筑"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Folly is a noun that means \"foolish or crazy behavior,\" like the folly of an unprepared student, showing up to take the finals exam without a pencil, paper or eyeglasses."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. absolute, sheer | ultimate | youthful | human | economic, political","VERB + FOLLY realize, recognize, see Suddenly she saw the folly of it all. | demonstrate, show These facts demonstrate the folly of the poli","PHRASES an act of folly That would be an act of sheer folly! | the folly of your ways They have finally seen the folly of their ways. | the ","ADJ. Gothic, Victorian | monumental | architectural","VERB + FOLLY build"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/8/folly_las3_br.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/folly.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Giving up a secure job seems to be the height of folly.","cn":"放弃一份安定的工作似乎愚蠢至极。"},{"en":"It would be folly to turn the offer down.","cn":"拒绝这个建议是愚蠢之举。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒli","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a lack of good judgement; the fact of doing something stupid; an activity or idea that shows a lack of judgement","cn":"愚蠢；愚笨；愚蠢的想法（或事情、行为）","g":"[uncountable, countable]","ex":{"en":"an act of sheer folly","cn":"纯粹愚蠢的行动"}},{"en":"a building that has no practical purpose but was built in the past for decoration, often in the garden of a large country house","cn":"（常见于旧时乡间豪宅花园中的）装饰性建筑","g":"[countable]"}]}},"forestry":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"林学;林业","en":"Forestry is the science or skill of growing and taking care of trees in forests, especially in order to obtain wood."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the science or skill of looking after large areas of trees","cn":"林学﹔林业"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. commercial, plantation | sustainable | tropical","FORESTRY + NOUN plantation | practice | track | worker | industry, management | policy, programme, project, strategy | department"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/0/forestry0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/forestry.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒrɪstri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the science or practice of planting and taking care of trees and forests","cn":"林学；林业"}]}},"forgo":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"→see: ;"}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to choose or decide not to have something, especially because there is not enough of it, because you need to save money, or for religious reasons","cn":""},{"en":"to not do or have things you enjoy because you think this will be good for you","cn":""},{"en":"to not do something that you usually do or that you want to do, especially for health or moral reasons","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 v","senses":[{"en":"The verb forgo means to give up or lose the right to something."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. willingly She would willingly forgo a birthday treat if only her warring parents would declare a truce.","VERB + FORGO have to Time to prepare was a luxury he would have to forgo. | decide to | be prepared to, be willing to"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/forgo0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/laadforgo.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"No one was prepared to forgo their lunch hour to attend the meeting.","cn":"谁都不愿意放弃午餐时间出席会议。"},{"en":"I had to forgo lunch.","cn":"我只得放弃午餐。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈɡəʊ","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to decide not to have or do something that you would like to have or do","cn":"放弃，弃绝（想做的事或想得之物）","ex":{"en":"No one was prepared to forgo their lunch hour to attend the meeting.","cn":"谁都不愿意放弃午餐时间出席会议。"}}]}},"foliage":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(植物的)叶，枝叶","en":"The leaves of a plant are referred to as its foliage .","ex":{"en":"...shrubs with grey or silver foliage.","cn":"长着灰色或银色叶子的灌木丛"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the leaves of a plant 〔","cn":"植物的〕叶子﹐叶"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 n 2 n","senses":[{"en":"Foliage refers to the leafy parts of a tree or plant. \"Don't eat the foliage on the rhubarb plant because the leaves are poisonous and eating them can be fatal; the stems, on the other hand, are tasty.\""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. bright | dense, heavy, luxuriant | dead | evergreen, year-round | grassy | spring, summer, etc. | tropical"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/foliage0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/foliage.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"dense green foliage","cn":"茂密的绿叶"},{"en":"dark green foliage","cn":"墨绿色的叶子"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊliɪdʒ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the leaves of a tree or plant; leaves and branches together","cn":"（植物的）叶；枝叶","ex":{"en":"dense green foliage","cn":"茂密的绿叶"}}]}},"forthcoming":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"即将来临的;即将发生的","en":"A forthcoming event is planned to happen soon.","ex":{"en":"...his opponents in the forthcoming elections.","cn":"他在即将来临的选举中的对手们"}},{"pos":"ADJ 形容词","cn":"会发生的;现成的;可得到的","en":"If something that you want, need, or expect is forthcoming, it is given to you or it happens.","ex":{"en":"They promised that the money would be forthcoming","cn":"他们承诺钱会到位。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"乐于提供信息的;愿意提供帮助的","en":"If you say that someone is forthcoming, you mean that they willingly give information when you ask them."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"if something that you are hoping for is in sight , you think it will probably happen soon","cn":""},{"en":"if something is around the corner , it might happen very soon but you cannot be completely sure","cn":""},{"en":"to be likely to happen soon, although you do not know exactly when","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 adj 2 adj 3 adj","senses":[{"en":"You know when you go to a movie and they show the previews under the heading \"coming soon?\" They could just as well say forthcoming , because it means the same thing. Only who would want to see that stuffy movie?"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be Help was duly forthcoming.","ADV. duly | readily | immediately 2 willing to give information","VERBS be","ADV. unusually | not very","PREP. about She wasn't very forthcoming about where she'd been."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/forthcoming0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/2/ld44forthcoming.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She's never very forthcoming about her plans.","cn":"她一直不很愿意说出自己的计划。"},{"en":"Financial support was not forthcoming.","cn":"财政支援尚未到手。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˌfɔːθˈkʌmɪŋ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"going to happen, be published, etc. very soon","cn":"即将发生（或出版等）的","g":"[only before noun]","ex":{"en":"the forthcoming elections","cn":"即将举行的选举"}},{"en":"ready or made available when needed","cn":"现成；随要随有","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"Financial support was not forthcoming.","cn":"财政支援尚未到手。"}},{"en":"willing to give information about something","cn":"乐于提供信息","g":"[not before noun]","ex":{"en":"She's never very forthcoming about her plans.","cn":"她一直不大愿意说出自己的计划。"}}]}},"fork":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"叉;餐叉","en":"A fork is a tool used for eating food which has a row of three or four long metal points at the end.","ex":{"en":"...knives and forks.","cn":"刀叉"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"用叉子叉","en":"If you fork food into your mouth or onto a plate, you put it there using a fork.","ex":{"en":"Ann forked some fish into her mouth","cn":"安用叉子叉了点儿鱼肉放进嘴里。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"叉，耙(园艺工具)","en":"A garden fork is a tool used for breaking up soil which has a row of three or four long metal points at the end."},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"叉运，叉掘(肥料、干草等)","en":"If you fork something such as manure or hay, you move it from one place to another using a large garden fork.","ex":{"en":"They started me off in the gardens as a handyman. Digging, forking manure, that kind of thing","cn":"他们让我先在园子里干些杂活，挖土、叉粪肥之类的。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(道路、河流等的)分岔处，分流处;分岔;岔路","en":"A fork in a road, path, or river is a point at which it divides into two parts and forms a 'Y' shape.","ex":{"en":"We arrived at a fork in the road","cn":"我们到达了一个岔路口。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"(道路、河流等)分岔","en":"If a road, path, or river forks, it forms a fork.","ex":{"en":"Beyond the village the road forked","cn":"过了村子之后路分了岔。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"走岔路","en":"If you fork in a particular direction when you are travelling along a road or path, you choose one of the forks in it and travel down it.","ex":{"en":"Just before the town boundary fork left onto a minor road.","cn":"快到城镇边界时要走岔路的左边一条小路。"}},{"pos":"PHRASAL VERB 短语动词","cn":"付钱;大把花钱","en":"If you fork out for something, you spend a lot of money on it.","ex":{"en":"He will have to fork out for private school fees for Nina","cn":"他得为尼娜付一大笔私立学校的学费。"}},{"pos":"","cn":"","en":"相关词组：fork out"}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a tool you use for picking up and eating food, with a handle and three or four points","cn":"餐叉﹐叉子"},{"en":"a garden tool used for digging, with a handle and three or four points","cn":"叉﹔耙"},{"en":"a place where a road, river, or tree divides into two parts, or one of the parts it divides into 〔","cn":"路的〕岔口﹔〔河流的〕分流处﹔〔树的〕分杈（处）"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. toasting","VERB + FORK pick up | put down | use","PREP. on a/the ~ She impaled a piece of meat on her fork. | with a ~ Mash the mixture with a fork.","PHRASES a knife and fork He put the knives and forks on the table. 2 place where sth divides into two parts","ADJ. left/left-hand, right/right-hand","VERB + FORK take As you pass the farm, take the right fork of the track up the hill.","PREP. at a/the ~ Bear left at the fork in the road. | ~ in sitting in the fork of the tree"]},"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/cutlery.jpg","media/thumb/fork.jpg"],"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/7/fork_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/fork1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Shortly before dusk they reached a fork and took the left-hand track.","cn":"快到黄昏时，他们来到一个岔路口，沿着左边的小径走去了。"},{"en":"Why fork out for a taxi when there's a perfectly good bus service?","cn":"有挺好的公共汽车，干吗要多掏钱坐出租汽车？"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a tool with a handle and three or four sharp points (called prongs), used for picking up and eating food","cn":"餐叉","ex":{"en":"to eat with a knife and fork","cn":"用刀叉吃东西"}},{"en":"a garden tool with a long or short handle and three or four sharp metal points, used for digging","cn":"叉（挖掘用的园艺工具）"},{"en":"a place where a road, river, etc. divides into two parts; either of these two parts","cn":"（道路、河流等的）分岔处，分流处，岔口，岔路","ex":{"en":"Take the right fork.","cn":"走右边的岔路。"}},{"en":"a thing that is like a fork in shape, with two or more long parts","cn":"叉状物","ex":{"en":"a jagged fork of lightning","cn":"锯齿状闪电"}},{"en":"either of two metal supporting pieces into which a wheel on a bicycle or motorcycle is fitted","cn":"（自行车或摩托车的）车叉子"},{"en":"to divide into two parts that lead in different directions","cn":"分岔；岔开两条分支","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"The path forks at the bottom of the hill.","cn":"小径在山丘脚下分岔。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to turn left or right where a road, etc. divides into two","cn":"走岔路中的一条","g":"[intransitive]","ex":{"en":"Fork right after the bridge.","cn":"过桥后走右边那条岔路。"},"pos":"verb"},{"en":"to move, carry or dig something using a fork","cn":"叉运；叉掘","g":"[transitive]","ex":{"en":"Clear the soil of weeds and fork in plenty of compost.","cn":"清除土中的杂草，然后叉入大量堆肥。"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"forlorn":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"孤苦伶仃的;愁苦的","en":"If someone is forlorn, they feel alone and unhappy.","ex":{"en":"One of the demonstrators, a young woman, sat forlorn on the pavement","cn":"一名年轻的女示威者独自一人坐在人行路上。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"无人居住的;荒凉的;废弃的","en":"If a place is forlorn, it is deserted and not cared for, or has little in it.","ex":{"en":"They headed inland on a forlorn road that was rutted and pocked","cn":"他们沿着一条坑坑洼洼布满车辙印的荒凉小路向内地进发。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(希望、尝试等)没有成功机会的，无谓的","en":"A forlorn hope or attempt is one that you think has no chance of success.","ex":{"en":"Peasants have left the land in the forlorn hope of finding a better life in cities.","cn":"农民离开土地，希望能在城市找到更好的生活，却不知道这根本难以实现。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"seeming lonely and unhappy","cn":"孤苦伶仃的﹐愁苦的﹐凄凉的"},{"en":"a place that is forlorn seems empty and sad, and is often in bad condition 〔","cn":"地方〕荒凉的"},{"en":"a forlorn hope, attempt, or struggle etc is not going to be successful","cn":"难以实现的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"Sniff, sniff, boo-hoo... use the adjective forlorn to express loneliness and feeling left out."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, feel, look, seem, sound, stand The house stood forlorn and empty. | become","ADV. very | quite, utterly She didn't belong, and felt utterly forlorn. | almost | rather, somewhat"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/d/forlorn0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/forlorn.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"His father smiled weakly in a forlorn attempt to reassure him that everything was all right.","cn":"他父亲淡淡地一笑，枉然地试图要他放心，一切都安然无恙。"},{"en":"She waited in the forlorn hope that he would one day come back to her.","cn":"她几乎毫无指望地等待他有一天会回到她的身边。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈlɔːn","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"appearing lonely and unhappy","cn":"孤苦伶仃的；孤独凄凉的","ex":{"en":"She looked so forlorn, standing there in the rain.","cn":"她站在雨中，显得孤苦伶仃。"}},{"en":"not cared for and with no people in it","cn":"凄凉的；荒芜的","ex":{"en":"Empty houses quickly take on a forlorn look.","cn":"空无一人的房屋很快就显得凄凉。"}},{"en":"unlikely to succeed, come true, etc.","cn":"不大可能成功的；难以实现的","ex":{"en":"She waited in the forlorn hope that he would one day come back to her.","cn":"她几乎毫无指望地等待他有一天会回到她的身边。"}}]}},"footwork":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(舞蹈)步法;(体育运动的)脚功，脚法","en":"Footwork is the way in which you move your feet, especially in sports such as boxing, football, or tennis, or in dancing.","ex":{"en":"This exercise improves your coordination, balance, timing and footwork.","cn":"这项锻炼可以提高协调能力、平衡力、把握时机的能力和脚法。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(应对困境的)策略，应变能力，手腕","en":"If you refer to someone's footwork in a difficult situation, you mean the clever way they deal with it.","ex":{"en":"In the end, his brilliant legal footwork paid off.","cn":"最后，他高明的法律手腕使他如愿以偿。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"skilful use of your feet when dancing or playing a sport 〔","cn":"舞蹈﹑运动中的〕步法﹐腿脚功夫"},{"en":"skilful methods that you use to achieve something","cn":"策略"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. deft, fancy, fine, good, neat, nimble","VERB + FOOTWORK show She showed some nimble footwork and looked a promising player."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/ld41footwork.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/footwork.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"It was going to take some deft political footwork to save the situation.","cn":"当时得采取一些巧妙的政治手段以挽回局势。"},{"en":"The England keeper revealed some fancy footwork in the victory over Nottingham Forest.","cn":"这位英格兰国门在战胜诺丁汉森林队的那场比赛中展现了出色的脚法。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtwɜːk","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the way in which a person moves their feet when playing a sport or dancing","cn":"（体育、舞蹈的）步法，脚步动作","ex":{"en":"Both dancers displayed some fancy footwork.","cn":"两名舞者都展示了炫丽的脚步动作。"}},{"en":"the ability to react quickly and with skill to a difficult situation","cn":"（应对困境的）策略，应变能力","ex":{"en":"It was going to take some deft political footwork to save the situation.","cn":"当时得采取一些巧妙的政治手段以挽回局势。"}}]}},"formulate":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"规划;策划;构想","en":"If you formulate something such as a plan or proposal, you invent it, thinking about the details carefully.","ex":{"en":"Little by little, he formulated his plan for escape.","cn":"他一点一点地设计构思出了逃跑的方案。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"明确表达;系统阐述","en":"If you formulate a thought, opinion, or idea, you express it or describe it using particular words.","ex":{"en":"I was impressed by the way he could formulate his ideas.","cn":"他陈述观点的方式让我印象深刻。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to think carefully about something you are going to do, and decide how you will do it","cn":""},{"en":"to think about and talk about something that you intend to do, especially something that needs to be carefully planned","cn":""},{"en":"to organize the details of an event or trip, such as the times in which things will happen","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"v","senses":[{"en":"To formulate is to come up with a plan. If you are locked out of your house, you'll need to formulate a plan to get back inside — preferably one that doesn't involving kicking in the door."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADV. fully | carefully, properly His ideas are always very carefully formulated. | clearly, explicitly | consciously He claims that Marx nev","VERB + FORMULATE try to | help (to)"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/formulate_las3_br.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/formulate.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"This new kitchen cleaner is formulated to cut through grease and dirt.","cn":"这种新的厨房清洁剂能去除油渍和污垢。"},{"en":"She has lots of good ideas, but she has difficulty formulating them.","cn":"她有很多好主意，但就是不善于表达。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːmjuleɪt","pos":"verb","senses":[{"en":"to create or prepare something carefully, giving particular attention to the details","cn":"制定；规划；构想；准备","ex":{"en":"to formulate a policy/theory/plan/proposal","cn":"制定政策；创立理论；构想计划；准备建议"}},{"en":"to express your ideas in carefully chosen words","cn":"确切表达；认真阐述","ex":{"en":"She has lots of good ideas, but she has difficulty formulating them.","cn":"她有很多好主意，但就是不善于表达。"}}]}},"foil":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"(用来包裹食物的)箔(纸)","en":"Foil consists of sheets of metal as thin as paper. It is used to wrap food in.","ex":{"en":"Pour cider around the meat and cover with foil.","cn":"在肉周围倒上苹果酒，然后以箔纸覆盖。"}},{"pos":"VERB 动词","cn":"阻止;挫败","en":"If you foil someone's plan or attempt to do something, for example to commit a crime, you succeed in stopping them from doing what they want.","ex":{"en":"A brave police chief foiled an armed robbery on a jewellers' by grabbing the raiders' shotgun","cn":"一位勇敢的警长夺过了意图袭击珠宝店的劫匪手中的猎枪，挫败了这起持械抢劫案。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"陪衬物;烘托者","en":"If you refer to one thing or person as a foil for another, you approve of the fact that they contrast with each other and go well together, often in a way that makes the second thing or person seem better or less harmful.","ex":{"en":"He thought of her serenity as a foil for his intemperance","cn":"在他看来，她的平静反衬出了他的放纵。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"花剑","en":"A foil is a thin light sword used in fencing, which has a button on its tip to prevent injury."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"metal sheets that are as thin as paper, used for wrapping food 〔","cn":"包裹食物用的〕箔"},{"en":"paper that is covered with very thin sheets of metal","cn":"箔纸"},{"en":"to emphasize the good qualities of another person or thing, by being very different from them","cn":"衬托出某人/某物﹐作为某人/某物的陪衬"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"1 v 2 n v 3 n v 4 n ","senses":[{"en":"You can serve as a foil to someone if you show them to be better than you by contrast. If you can't dance but your friend Lisa can, you can be a foil to Lisa's grace."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. aluminium, gold, silver, tin | kitchen","QUANT. piece, sheet | roll","VERB + FOIL cover sth with, wrap sth in I wrapped the sandwiches in kitchen foil. 2 sth that shows off the qualities of sth else","ADJ. good, ideal, perfect","VERB + FOIL be, provide","PREP. as a ~ She has used mosses as a foil for the brightly coloured flowers in the bed. | ~ for/to The couple provided the perfect foil for"]},"media":{"img":["media/ldoce/img/chocolate.jpg"],"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/foil_n0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/foil1.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Customs officials foiled an attempt to smuggle the paintings out of the country.","cn":"海关关员阻截了一次企图走私画作出境的阴谋。"},{"en":"The pale walls provide a perfect foil for the furniture.","cn":"浅色的墙壁完全衬托出家具的特色。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fɔɪl","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"metal made into very thin sheets that is used for covering or wrapping things, especially food","cn":"（尤指包装食物等用的）箔","g":"[uncountable]","lab":"British English also","ex":{"en":"aluminium foil","cn":"铝箔"}},{"en":"paper that is covered in very thin sheets of metal","cn":"箔纸（覆有箔的纸）","g":"[uncountable]","ex":{"en":"The chocolates are individually wrapped in gold foil.","cn":"巧克力用金箔纸一颗颗独立包装。"}},{"en":"a person or thing that contrasts with, and therefore emphasizes, the qualities of another person or thing","cn":"陪衬者；陪衬物","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"The pale walls provide a perfect foil for the furniture.","cn":"浅色的墙壁完全衬托出家具的特色。"}},{"en":"a long thin light sword used in the sport of fencing","cn":"（击剑运动用的）花剑","g":"[countable]"},{"en":"to stop something from happening, especially something illegal; to prevent somebody from doing something","cn":"挫败，阻止，制止（非法活动等）","ex":{"en":"to foil a plan/crime/plot","cn":"挫败计划／犯罪／阴谋"},"pos":"verb"}]}},"foolish":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(举止或行为)愚蠢的，傻的，笨的","en":"If someone's behaviour or action is foolish, it is not sensible and shows a lack of good judgment.","ex":{"en":"It would be foolish to raise hopes unnecessarily","cn":"无谓地燃起人们的希望是愚蠢的。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"傻的;蠢的;显得难堪的","en":"If you look or feel foolish, you look or feel so silly or ridiculous that people are likely to laugh at you.","ex":{"en":"I just stood there feeling foolish and watching him","cn":"我只是傻傻地站在那里看着他。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"showing a total lack of good sense or good judgment. Stupid sounds very strong and is often used when you are annoyed or strongly criticizing someone’s behaviour","cn":""},{"en":"doing or saying things that are not sensible or serious, and that may make you feel embarrassed later. Silly sounds much gentler than stupid","cn":""},{"en":"not sensible, often in a way that is also amusing","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS appear, be, feel, look, seem, sound","ADV. exceedingly, extremely, incredibly, really, singularly, very | utterly | a bit, a little, quite, rather, slightly, vaguely"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/foolish0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/d/foolish.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The accident was my fault — it would be foolish to pretend otherwise.","cn":"这次事故是我的过失 — 装作没有责任那才傻呢。"},{"en":"We foolishly thought that everyone would speak English.","cn":"我们真蠢，竟以为人人都会说英语。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfuːlɪʃ","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"not showing good sense or judgement","cn":"愚蠢的；傻的","ex":{"en":"There are some very foolish people out there.","cn":"那里有一些非常愚蠢的人。"}},{"en":"made to feel or look silly and embarrassed","cn":"不知所措；出丑；显得尴尬","g":"[not usually before noun]","ex":{"en":"I felt foolish and a failure.","cn":"我自觉是个愚蠢的失败者。"}}]}},"forefront":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"显著地位;重要位置;最前沿","en":"If you are at the forefront of a campaign or other activity, you have a leading and influential position in it.","ex":{"en":"They have been at the forefront of the campaign for political change.","cn":"他们一直处于政治变革运动的风口浪尖上。"}},{"pos":"N-SING 单数名词","cn":"(思考或关注的)重心,焦点","en":"If something is at the forefront of people's minds or attention, they think about it a lot because it is particularly important to them.","ex":{"en":"The pension issue was not at the forefront of his mind in the spring of 1985.","cn":"在 1985 年春，养老金问题并非他关注的重点。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"to be in a leading position in an important activity that is trying to achieve something or develop new ideas","cn":"位于（某事物的）最前列﹐处于（某事物的）领先地位"},{"en":"to be what someone is thinking about most, because it is very important to them","cn":"是某人首先考虑/注意到等的事情"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERB + FOREFRONT remain at/in Education remains at the forefront of the state's planning. | keep sb/sth at/in/to | come into/to She came to ","PREP. at/in the ~ (of) issues at the forefront of government policy","PHRASES at/in/to the forefront of sb's mind This question remained at the forefront of her mind."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/e/forefront0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/b/forefront.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The new product took the company to the forefront of the computer software field.","cn":"该新产品使这家公司跻身计算机软件业的前列。"},{"en":"Women have always been at the forefront of the Green movement.","cn":"妇女总是在环境保护运动的最前列。"}]},"follower":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"信徒;追随者;支持者","en":"A follower of a particular person, group, or belief is someone who supports or admires this person, group, or belief.","ex":{"en":"...followers of the Zulu Inkatha movement.","cn":"祖鲁因卡塔运动的支持者"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who supports a person, political party, or idea","cn":""},{"en":"all the people who support a person, group, or plan","cn":""},{"en":"someone who supports the ideas of a political organization but does not belong to it, especially an organization that is illegal","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A follower is a person who believes in a particular cause, faith, or specific person. A follower of Hinduism, for example, usually worships many gods."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. ardent, close, enthusiastic, keen a keen follower of football | dedicated, devoted, devout, faithful, loyal, true a true follower of Is","QUANT. band","VERB + FOLLOWER have She still has many loyal followers. | attract | lead The myth says that he led a small band of followers to seek their ","PREP. among sb's ~ The king was not powerful enough to command respect among his followers."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/follower_las3_br.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/f/follower.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She is a leader, not a follower.","cn":"她是领导者，不是追随者。"},{"en":"the followers of Mahatma Gandhi","cn":"圣雄甘地的拥护者"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɒləʊə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who supports and admires a particular person or set of ideas","cn":"拥护者；追随者；信徒","ex":{"en":"the followers of Mahatma Gandhi","cn":"圣雄甘地的拥护者"}},{"en":"a person who is very interested in a particular activity and follows all the recent news about it","cn":"爱好者","ex":{"en":"keen followers of football","cn":"足球迷"}},{"en":"a person who does things after somebody else has done them first","cn":"仿效者；追随者","ex":{"en":"She is a leader, not a follower.","cn":"她是领导者，不是追随者。"}},{"en":"a person who chooses to regularly receive somebody’s messages using a social media service","cn":"（社交媒体上某人的）关注者，粉丝","ex":{"en":"a celebrity with thousands of followers on Twitter","cn":"一个在推特上有成千上万关注者的名人"}}]}},"foothold":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"立足点;稳固地位","en":"A foothold is a strong or favourable position from which further advances or progress may be made.","ex":{"en":"If British business is to have a successful future, companies must establish a firm foothold in Europe.","cn":"如果英国公司想在未来成功发展，就必须在欧洲建立稳固的基础。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(攀登时的)立足点,支点","en":"A foothold is a place such as a small hole or area of rock where you can safely put your foot when climbing.","ex":{"en":"He lowered his legs until he felt he had a solid foothold on the rockface beneath him.","cn":"他把腿向下伸，直到他感觉稳稳地踩住下面的石头。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a position from which you can start to make progress and achieve your aims","cn":"基础﹔立足点"},{"en":"a small hole or crack where you can safely put your foot when climbing a steep rock 〔","cn":"攀登陡峭岩石时的〕立脚点"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. firm, secure","VERB + FOOTHOLD have | find, get, scrabble for He found a secure foothold and pulled himself up. scrabbling for a foothold on the steep gras","ADJ. firm, secure | permanent | big | small","VERB + FOOTHOLD have | establish, gain, get, obtain, secure The company is trying to gain a foothold in the European market. | maintain | lo","PREP. ~ in The firm has a firm foothold in this market."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/foothold0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/foothold.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The company is eager to gain a foothold in Europe.","cn":"这家公司急于在欧洲取得一席之地。"},{"en":"Extreme right-wing parties gained a foothold in the latest European elections.","cn":"极右翼党派在最近的欧洲各国选举中站稳了脚跟。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊthəʊld","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a place where your foot can be safely supported when climbing","cn":"立足处（攀登时脚可踩的支撑点）","ex":{"en":"She edged forward feeling for a foothold.","cn":"她向前挪动，寻找立足点。"}},{"en":"a strong position in a business, profession, etc. from which somebody can make progress and achieve success","cn":"（可以此发展或取得成功的）稳固地位，立足点","g":"[usually singular]","ex":{"en":"The company is eager to gain a foothold in Europe.","cn":"这家公司急于在欧洲取得一席之地。"}}]}},"forerunner":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"先驱;先行者;预兆","en":"If you describe a person or thing as the forerunner of someone or something similar, you mean they existed before them and either influenced their development or were a sign of what was going to happen.","ex":{"en":"...a machine which, in some respects, was the forerunner of the modern helicopter","cn":"在某些方面成为现代直升机前身的机器"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the previous person or thing is the one that existed just before now or before the time you are talking about","cn":""},{"en":"the last thing or person is the one that you had just before now, or the one that existed just before now","cn":""},{"en":"someone who used to be someone's wife, used to be a soldier etc, but is not any more","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A forerunner is someone or something that came before and paved the way for something today. Rotary phones were forerunners of today's complex cell phones."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. early, immediate an early forerunner of the modern jet engine | direct"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/4/forerunner0703.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/forerunner.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Country music was undoubtedly one of the forerunners of rock and roll.","cn":"乡村音乐无疑是摇滚乐的先导之一。"},{"en":"Babbage’s engine was the forerunner of the modern computer.","cn":"巴贝奇发明的机器是现代计算机的前身。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːrʌnə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person or thing that came before and influenced somebody/something else that is similar; a sign of what is going to happen","cn":"先驱；先行者；预兆；前兆","ex":{"en":"Country music was undoubtedly one of the forerunners of rock and roll.","cn":"乡村音乐无疑是摇滚乐的先导之一。"}}]}},"foresight":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"先见之明;预见;深谋远虑","en":"Someone's foresight is their ability to see what is likely to happen in the future and to take appropriate action.","ex":{"en":"He was later criticised for his lack of foresight","cn":"他后来被指责缺少先见之明。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the ability to imagine what is likely to happen and to consider this when planning for the future","cn":"先见之明﹐预见﹔深谋远虑"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Use the noun foresight to describe successful planning for the future, like on a cloudy morning having the foresight to bring an umbrella in case of rain showers later in the day."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. considerable, great","VERB + FORESIGHT have He had had the foresight to bring in the washing before the rain started. | show The plans showed great foresight. | l","PHRASES a lack of foresight"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/1/foresight0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/1/foresight.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"She had had the foresight to prepare herself financially in case of an accident.","cn":"她有先见之明，经济上作了准备以防万一发生事故。"},{"en":"It was an example of the authorities’ lack of foresight .","cn":"这是当权者缺乏远见的一个例证。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːsaɪt","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the ability to predict what is likely to happen and to use this to prepare for the future","cn":"深谋远虑；先见之明","ex":{"en":"She had had the foresight to prepare herself financially in case of an accident.","cn":"她有先见之明，经济上作了准备以防万一发生事故。"}}]}},"foreboding":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-VAR 可变名词","cn":"(不祥的)预兆，预感","en":"Foreboding is a strong feeling that something terrible is going to happen.","ex":{"en":"His triumph was overshadowed by an uneasy sense of foreboding.","cn":"他的胜利因为一种令人不安的不祥预感蒙上了阴影。"}},{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"给人不祥预感的","en":"If you describe something as foreboding, you mean that it makes you feel that something terrible is going to happen.","ex":{"en":"Prisons like Strangeways, built more than 100 years ago, were intended to look grim and foreboding places.","cn":"诸如斯特兰奇韦斯监狱之类建于 100 多年前的监狱故意营造出一种阴森、不祥的气氛。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a feeling of being frightened","cn":""},{"en":"a feeling of great fear, because you think that something terrible is about to happen","cn":""},{"en":"a sudden feeling of fear, or a situation that makes you feel this","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n adj","senses":[{"en":"When you get a foreboding, you get a sense that something bad is going to happen. A foreboding is a foretelling, a sign or a glimpse, that \"something wicked this way comes\" — or might come."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. deep, gloomy","VERB + FOREBODING feel, have I felt a gloomy foreboding that something was going to go wrong. | be full of He returned, full of foreboding, ","PREP. with (a) ~ The sky was dull, with a foreboding of rain. | ~ of She had a foreboding of danger.","PHRASES a feeling/sense of foreboding"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/b/foreboding0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/9/foreboding.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He knew from her face that his forebodings had been justified.","cn":"他从她的脸上看出，自己不祥的预感是正确的。"},{"en":"She had a sense of foreboding that the news would be bad.","cn":"她预感到这会是坏消息。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fɔːˈbəʊdɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a strong feeling that something unpleasant or dangerous is going to happen","cn":"（对不祥或危险事情的）强烈预感","ex":{"en":"She had a sense of foreboding that the news would be bad.","cn":"她预感到这会是坏消息。"}},{"en":"making you feel that something unpleasant or dangerous is going to happen","cn":"（对不祥或危险事情的）强烈预感","ex":{"en":"a foreboding feeling that something was wrong","cn":"一种出了差错的不祥感觉"},"pos":"adjective"}]}},"footballer":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"踢足球的人;(尤指)足球运动员","en":"A footballer is a person who plays football, especially as a profession."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"someone who plays football, especially a professional player 〔","cn":"尤指职业的〕足球运动员"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. brilliant, good, skilful, talented | famous | keen | amateur, professional | international","FOOTBALLER + VERB play"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/footballer0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/ld41footballer.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtbɔːlə(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a person who plays football, especially as a profession","cn":"（职业）足球运动员","ex":{"en":"a professional footballer","cn":"职业足球员"}}]}},"forgery":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"伪造罪","en":"Forgery is the crime of forging money, documents, or paintings.","ex":{"en":"He was found guilty of forgery.","cn":"他被判伪造罪名成立。"}},{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"伪造品;仿造物;赝品","en":"You can refer to a forged document, banknote, or painting as a forgery .","ex":{"en":"The letter was a forgery.","cn":"这封信是伪造的。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"an illegal copy of something official such as a bank note, legal documentation or work of art","cn":""},{"en":"made to look like the product of a particular company or the work of a particular artist in order to trick people in to buying them","cn":""},{"en":"counterfeit money looks exactly like real money but has been produced illegally","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"If you painted a copy of the Mona Lisa and sold it to a museum, claiming it was the original, your painting could be called a forgery , and the crime you've committed is also forgery ."}]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/forgery0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/e/forgery.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Experts are dismissing claims that the painting is a forgery.","cn":"专家排除了这幅画是赝品的说法。"},{"en":"The painting was a very clever forgery.","cn":"这幅画是件很巧妙的赝品。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːdʒəri","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the crime of copying money, documents, etc. in order to cheat people","cn":"伪造；伪造罪","g":"[uncountable]"},{"en":"something, for example a document, piece of paper money, etc., that has been copied in order to cheat people","cn":"伪造品；赝品","g":"[countable]","ex":{"en":"Experts are dismissing claims that the painting is a forgery.","cn":"专家排除了这幅画是赝品的说法。"}}]}},"footpath":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"(尤指乡间的)小路","en":"A footpath is a path for people to walk on, especially in the countryside."}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a long, narrow piece of ground for people to walk along","cn":""},{"en":"a path built along the side of a street for people to walk on","cn":""},{"en":"a public path for people to walk on in the country","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. public | long-distance","VERB + FOOTPATH follow, take, use | keep to","FOOTPATH + VERB follow sth, lead, run The footpath runs along the canal. | cross sth a footpath crossing farmland | link sth the footpath li","FOOTPATH + NOUN network, system","PREP. along a/the ~ We walked along the footpath. | by (a/the) ~ The monastery is an hour away by footpath. | down a/the ~, on the ~ We stoo"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/9/brelasdefootpath.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/footpath.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"a public footpath","cn":"人行道"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtpɑːθ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a path that is made for people to walk along, especially in the country","cn":"（尤指乡间的）人行小道","lab":"especially British English","ex":{"en":"a public footpath","cn":"步道"}},{"en":"a flat part at the side of a road for people to walk on; a pavement","cn":"（马路边的）人行道","lab":"Australian English, New Zealand English, British English，，，，"}]}},"foyer":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"门厅;大厅;休息室","en":"The foyer is the large area where people meet or wait just inside the main doors of a building such as a theatre, cinema, or hotel.","ex":{"en":"I went and waited in the foyer.","cn":"我进去在大厅里等着。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a room or hall at the entrance to a public building 〔","cn":"公共建筑物入口处的〕休息厅﹐门厅"},{"en":"a small room or hall at the entrance to a house or apartment 〔","cn":"房屋或公寓入口处的〕前厅﹐门厅"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A foyer is a large entrance, like the foyer of a building that you enter before you reach the elevators. Sometimes a foyer is also called a \"lobby.\""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. entrance, reception | cinema, hospital, hotel, school, station, theatre | crowded, deserted","PREP. across the ~, in the ~ We arranged to meet up in the foyer of the Hyatt hotel."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/foyer_las3_br.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/c/foyer.mp3"},"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔɪeɪ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large open space inside the entrance of a theatre or hotel where people can meet or wait","cn":"（剧院或旅馆的）门厅，休息厅","ex":{"en":"I’ll meet you in the foyer at 7 o’clock.","cn":"我7点钟在门厅等你。"}},{"en":"an entrance hall in a private house or flat","cn":"（私宅或公寓的）前厅，玄关","lab":"North American English","ex":{"en":"An elegant foyer leads directly to the living room.","cn":"典雅的门厅直通起居室。"}}]}},"footstep":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"脚步声;足迹","en":"A footstep is the sound or mark that is made by someone walking each time their foot touches the ground.","ex":{"en":"I heard footsteps outside.","cn":"我听见了外面的脚步声。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"效仿;步…后尘","en":"If you follow in someone's footsteps, you do the same things as they did earlier.","ex":{"en":"My father is extremely proud that I followed in his footsteps and became a doctor.","cn":"我的父亲非常自豪，因为我继承他的事业，成为了一名医生。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the single movement that you make when you put one foot in front of the other when you are walking","cn":""},{"en":"the sound of someone's foot being placed on the ground when they are walking or running","cn":""},{"en":"the distance you go when you take a single step","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. heavy | light | dragging He heard the sound of heavy, dragging footsteps in the corridor. | measured, slow | brisk, hurried, hurrying, ","VERB + FOOTSTEP hear, listen to | listen for listening for her mother's footsteps | retrace I am retracing the footsteps of the lost expedit","FOOTSTEP + VERB run, walk | halt, stop The footsteps halted in the doorway. | approach, come The footsteps came closer as she listened. | re","PHRASES the sound of (sb's) footsteps"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/footstep0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/6/footstep.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"the sound of footsteps on the stairs","cn":"楼梯上的脚步声"},{"en":"footsteps in the snow","cn":"雪地上的足迹"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtstep","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the sound or mark made each time your foot touches the ground when you are walking or running","cn":"脚步声；足迹","ex":{"en":"the sound of footsteps on the stairs","cn":"楼梯上的脚步声"}}]}},"foolproof":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"(计划、机器等)十分简单的，容易操作的，万无一失的","en":"Something such as a plan or a machine that is foolproof is so well designed, easy to understand, or easy to use that it cannot go wrong or be used wrongly.","ex":{"en":"The system is not 100 per cent foolproof","cn":"这个系统并非是万无一失。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"if someone is destined to do or become something, they will certainly do it or become it, especially something that will make them famous or admired","cn":""},{"en":"to be certain to get something good or to be successful","cn":""},{"en":"use this to say that someone or something will definitely win or succeed","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj v","senses":[{"en":"When something is bound to work out, you can call it foolproof . Your foolproof plan for having a great summer might involve spending lots of time at the beach."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, look, seem | make sth We're trying to work out a way to make the system foolproof.","ADV. absolutely, quite | nearly, pretty well, virtually The system is pretty well foolproof."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/6/foolproof0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/4/foolproof.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"This recipe is foolproof — it works every time.","cn":"这个食谱绝对管用，每次都万无一失。"},{"en":"a foolproof way of preventing credit card fraud","cn":"一个防止信用卡诈骗的万全之策"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfuːlpruːf","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very well designed and easy to use so that it cannot fail and you cannot use it wrongly","cn":"使用简便的；完全可靠的；万无一失的","ex":{"en":"This recipe is foolproof—it works every time.","cn":"这个食谱绝对管用，每次都万无一失。"}}]}},"folklore":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"民间传说;民俗","en":"Folklore is the traditional stories, customs, and habits of a particular community or nation.","ex":{"en":"In Chinese folklore the bat is an emblem of good fortune.","cn":"在中国的民间传说中蝙蝠是好运的象征。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"all the beliefs and ways of behaving that have existed for a very long time in a particular country or among a particular group of people","cn":""},{"en":"old stories which the people in a country or area have told each other for a very long time, and which often contain historical or religious ideas","cn":""},{"en":"art, literature, and traditions that are considered to belong as a right to all the people in a society, especially because they form an important part of a country's history","cn":""}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"Stories, customs, and beliefs that are passed from one generation to the next are called folklore . According to folklore , you shouldn't take rocks from the volcanoes in Hawaii because Pele, the volcano goddess, will be angry and curse you."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. popular | local | cricket, sporting, etc.","VERB + FOLKLORE be part of | become part of, enter (into), pass into The victory became part of sporting folklore.","FOLKLORE + VERB have it that &hellip; Local folklore has it that prehistoric men drove cattle over these cliffs.","PREP. according to ~ According to popular folklore, anyone who owns such a picture will have bad luck. | in &hellip; ~ a character in Americ"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/folklore0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/8/folklore.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"The story rapidly became part of family folklore.","cn":"这个故事很快就成为家族传说的一部分。"},{"en":"Irish/Indian folklore","cn":"爱尔兰/印度民俗"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfəʊklɔː(r)","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the traditions and stories of a country or community","cn":"民间传统；民俗；民间传说","ex":{"en":"Irish/Indian folklore","cn":"爱尔兰／印度民俗"}}]}},"fortress":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-COUNT 可数名词","cn":"堡垒;防御阵地;要塞","en":"A fortress is a castle or other large strong building, or a well-protected place, which is intended to be difficult for enemies to enter.","ex":{"en":"...a 13th-century fortress.","cn":"13 世纪的堡垒"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a large strong building used for defending an important place","cn":"堡垒"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"n","senses":[{"en":"A fortress is a large building or complex of buildings used as a military stronghold. In a military sense a fortress is often called a “fort”."}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. great | formidable, impregnable, strong | grim","VERB + FORTRESS attack, besiege, lay siege to | take Greek warriors took the fortress with little effort. | hold, occupy","FORTRESS + VERB be/come under attack, be/come under siege | fall The fortress fell after a nine-day siege.","FORTRESS + NOUN town","PREP. in a/the ~ They took refuge in the fortress."]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/c/fortress0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/7/fortress.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"Fear of terrorist attack has turned the conference centre into a fortress.","cn":"由于害怕恐怖分子袭击，会议中心已变成了堡垒。"},{"en":"a fortress town enclosed by four miles of ramparts","cn":"由四英里长的城墙围着的设防城镇"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfɔːtrəs","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"a building or place that has been made stronger and protected against attack","cn":"城堡；堡垒；要塞；设防的地方","ex":{"en":"a fortress town enclosed by four miles of ramparts","cn":"由四英里长的城墙围着的设防城镇"}}]}},"formidable":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"ADJ-GRADED 能被表示程度的副词或介词词组修饰的形容词","cn":"可怕的;令人惊叹的;艰巨的","en":"If you describe something or someone as formidable, you mean that you feel slightly frightened by them because they are very great or impressive.","ex":{"en":"We have a formidable task ahead of us","cn":"我们面临着一项艰巨的任务。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"very powerful or impressive, and often frightening","cn":"令人敬畏的﹔可怕的"},{"en":"difficult to deal with and needing a lot of effort or skill","cn":"难对付的"}]},"vocab":{"pos":"adj","senses":[{"en":"What do the national debt, your old gym teacher, and your mother-in-law have in common? They're all formidable — that is, they inspire fear and respect thanks to their size, or special ability, or unusual qualities. (Or possibly all three in the case of your mother-in-law.)"}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["VERBS be, look, seem, sound The task looks formidable. | remain | find sth Men found her formidable.","ADV. really, truly, very a very formidable opponent | a bit, pretty, quite, rather, somewhat"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/2/formidable0205.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/5/formidable.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"He now has the chance to prove himself in a formidably difficult role.","cn":"现在他的任务十分艰巨，有机会证明自己的能力。"},{"en":"In debate he was a formidable opponent.","cn":"在辩论中他是位难应付的对手。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"fəˈmɪdəbl","pos":"adjective","senses":[{"en":"if people, things or situations are formidable, you feel fear and/or respect for them, because they are impressive or powerful, or because they seem very difficult","cn":"可怕的；令人敬畏的；难对付的","ex":{"en":"In debate he was a formidable opponent.","cn":"在辩论中他是位难应付的对手。"}}]}},"footing":{"collins":{"senses":[{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"立足点;基础","en":"If something is put on a particular footing, it is defined, established, or changed in a particular way, often so that it is able to develop or exist successfully.","ex":{"en":"The new law will put official corruption on the same legal footing as treason.","cn":"新法律将规定对公职腐败适用与叛国罪相同的量刑标准。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"人际关系;联系;地位","en":"If you are on a particular kind of footing with someone, you have that kind of relationship with them.","ex":{"en":"They decided to put their relationship on a more formal footing","cn":"他们决定正式交往。"}},{"pos":"PHRASE 短语","cn":"将要开战;准备打仗","en":"If a country or armed force is on a war footing, it is ready to fight a war.","ex":{"en":"The president placed the republic on a war footing.","cn":"总统把共和国推到了战争的边缘。"}},{"pos":"N-UNCOUNT 不可数名词","cn":"立稳;站稳","en":"You refer to your footing when you are referring to your position and how securely your feet are placed on the ground. For example, if you lose your footing, your feet slip and you fall.","ex":{"en":"He was cautious of his footing, wary of the edge","cn":"他小心翼翼地站在边缘。"}}]},"ldoce":{"phon":"hwd","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"people who are equal have the same rights as each other and are treated in the same way as each other; if people get equal treatment, pay etc, they are all treated in the same way or get paid the same money","cn":""},{"en":"when all people have the same rights and opportunities in society and are treated equally","cn":""},{"en":"people, countries, or organizations that are on an equal footing in a particular situation are being treated as equal, even though this would not happen in other places or situations","cn":""}]},"collocations":{"phrases":["ADJ. firm, sure","VERB + FOOTING keep He struggled to keep his footing on the slippery floor. | be sure of She looked over her shoulder to be sure of her foot","ADJ. firm, proper, right, secure, solid, sound | wrong | equal, the same All claimants stand on an equal legal footing. | different, unequal","VERB + FOOTING be on, stand on The two teams stand on an equal footing. | be back on | gain Town planning procedures gained a footing in loc","PREP. on a &hellip; ~ an attempt to put the economy on a more secure footing"]},"media":{"uk":"media/ldoce/hwd/bre/5/brelasdefooting.mp3","us":"media/ldoce/hwd/ame/3/footing.mp3"},"examples":[{"en":"They were demanding to be treated on the same footing as the rest of the teachers.","cn":"他们要求得到和其他老师同等的待遇。"},{"en":"I slipped and struggled to regain my footing.","cn":"我滑了一下，但挣扎着站稳了脚跟。"}],"oxford":{"phon":"ˈfʊtɪŋ","pos":"noun","senses":[{"en":"the position of your feet when they are safely on the ground or some other surface","cn":"立足；站稳","ex":{"en":"She lost her footing (= she slipped or lost her balance) and fell backwards into the water.","cn":"她脚未站稳，向后一仰掉进水中。"}},{"en":"the basis on which something is established or organized","cn":"立足点；基础","ex":{"en":"The company is now on a sound financial footing.","cn":"该公司现在已是资金稳健。"}},{"en":"the position or status of somebody/something in relation to others; the relationship between two or more people or groups","cn":"地位；人际关系","ex":{"en":"The two groups must meet on an equal footing.","cn":"这两个集团必须以平等地位会谈。"}}]}}});
